{"raw": {"https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100843": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 160 Department Neurological Sciences 50001975 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule As directed by supervisor Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Title/Academic Rank Postdoctoral Research Associate Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 04/17/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Neurological Sciences at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) seeks a post-doctoral research associate that will work in the laboratory of Dr. David E. Warren (principal investigator/PI) with the PI and his research team to plan, develop, implement, and conduct research projects at UNMC . This includes ongoing NIH -funded research in developmental, aging, and neurological populations including healthy children, healthy older adults, and patients on the Alzheimer\u2019s disease continuum. The PI\u2019s lab uses cognitive neuroscience techniques including cognitive assessment, neuropsychology, psychophysical testing, eye-movement monitoring, structural and functional magnetic resonance imaging, transcranial magnetic stimulation, and genomic assays. Duties involve research study design, participant recruitment, data collection, data analyses, and preparation of scholarly products. Scholarly products will include peer-reviewed publications, conference abstracts, extramural grant applications, progress reports, intramural institutional review board protocols, and other compliance reports as directed. Finally, the post-doc will also work as directed with collaborators at UNMCand other institutions. Postdoctoral research associate will be expected to have strong scientific writing skills and excellent communication skills, good early track record of submitted or published peer-reviewed articles, exceptional organizational skills, ability to work as a team member, ability to advise and supervise more junior laboratory personnel, familiarity with standard office productivity software (e.g., MS Office), and ability to operate standard office equipment (copy machine, fax machine, multi-line phone). Applications are being accepted on line at https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/97497 Inquiries: David Warren, PhD at david.warren@unmc.edu Required Qualifications Ph.D. in an appropriate scientific field (e.g., psychology, neuroscience, bioinformatics) Supplemental Qualifications 1. Proficiency in: experimental design, study implementation, and advanced applied statistics. 2. Experience with methods including: structural and functional magnetic resonance imaging, eye-tracking, transcranial magnetic stimulation, genetic/genomic analyses, and/or other cognitive neuroscience techniques 3. Experience with populations including: typically-developing children and adolescents, healthy older adults, and/or neurological patients including individuals on the Alzheimer\u2019s disease continuum. 4. Experience with UNIX -like and Windows operating systems. 5. Experience with programming in languages including Python, R, Julia, MATLAB , C, C++, etc. 6. Experience with development, implementation, and management of clinical/translational research protocols. 7. Broad technical competence; for example, capacity to troubleshoot specialized lab equipment in consultation with vendors. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking 2-5 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Use of computer and research projects Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * If you have not yet graduated, can you provide an enrollment verification or enrollment certificate with expected graduation date from your university or institution? This can be uploaded as \"other document\" Yes No * If you do not yet have the degree required for this position, what is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * How many published articles do you have? (Open Ended Question) * Of these published articles, how many are you first-author (Open Ended Question) * Please enter the name of your doctoral degree-granting institution. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of postgraduate research experience do you have as of the date you are submitting this application? (Open Ended Question) * Please select one of the following: I am a U.S. citizen I am a non-citizen national of the U.S. I am a permanent resident (green card holder) Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100833": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 254 Department Biochem and Molecular Biology 50000510 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Title/Academic Rank Postdoctoral Research Associate Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 06/19/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary A postdoctoral position currently available in the Biochemistry and Molecular Biology Department at the University of Nebraska Medical Center broadly focused on comparative interactomics in human health and disease. The potential candidate is expected to enact experimental workflows including the development of model cell lines, executing affinity \u2018omics, and integrative analysis of combined results. Required Qualifications \u00b7 PhD degree in Biochemistry, Molecular Biology, or a related field in Life sciences. \u00b7 Extensive experience with molecular interactions analysis. Publications as the first author in peer-reviewed journals. Supplemental Qualifications \u00b7 Ideally 2-3 years of relevant hand on research experience. \u00b7 Strong background in proteomics and/or nucleic acids biochemistry. Competence with bioinformatics programming in R Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Not Applicable Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Precautions will be used when working with hazards in the lab. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation both Repetitive Motion both Grasping both If you selected any area above, please explain lab work Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * If you have not yet graduated, can you provide an enrollment verification or enrollment certificate with expected graduation date from your university or institution? This can be uploaded as \"other document\" Yes No * If you do not yet have the degree required for this position, what is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * How many published articles do you have? (Open Ended Question) * Of these published articles, how many are you first-author (Open Ended Question) * Please enter the name of your doctoral degree-granting institution. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of postgraduate research experience do you have as of the date you are submitting this application? (Open Ended Question) * Please select one of the following: I am a U.S. citizen I am a non-citizen national of the U.S. I am a permanent resident (green card holder) Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100795": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 384 Department Pharmacology/Exp Neuroscience 50000523 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by Research Needs Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Title/Academic Rank Postdoctoral Research Associate Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 10/12/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Pharmacology and Experimental Neuroscience at the University of Nebraska Medical Center is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Associate to join our research program investigating mechanisms of neuroinflammation associated with HIV infection and substance use. The successful candidate will study cellular and molecular mechanisms involving mitochondrial dysfunction, lysosomal impairment, autophagy, mitophagy, inflammasome signaling, ferroptosis, and pyroptosis. The position will involve experimental design, data analysis, manuscript preparation, and contribution to grant related research activities. Applicants should have a PhD or equivalent degree in neuroscience, neurobiology, pharmacology, molecular biology, or a related field. Experience with molecular and cellular techniques and neuroinflammation is required. Expertise in primary neural cell culture, microglial biology, neuronal morphology and spine analysis, rodent behavioral studies, cell signaling, autophagy, mitophagy, lysosomal biology, ferroptosis, or pyroptosis is highly desirable. We seek an independent, productive, and collaborative scientist with strong communication skills and a commitment to rigorous research. The position provides excellent research infrastructure and opportunities for scientific and professional development at UNMC . Required Qualifications Ph.D., or expected Ph.D. in next three months, in biological sciences, biochemistry, immunology, neuroscience, pharmacology, physiology, pathology Supplemental Qualifications Ability to write manuscripts, give presentations and think independently. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Lab environment, Animal facility Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Occasionally Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals Yes Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Candidate will be exposed to laboratory chemicals, and centrifuges which would be noisy. Will also be wearing PPE when working with animals (rodents) Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation both Repetitive Motion both Grasping both If you selected any area above, please explain Pipetting and keyboarding will involve repetitive motion and grasping. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * If you have not yet graduated, can you provide an enrollment verification or enrollment certificate with expected graduation date from your university or institution? This can be uploaded as \"other document\" Yes No * If you do not yet have the degree required for this position, what is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * How many published articles do you have? (Open Ended Question) * Of these published articles, how many are you first-author (Open Ended Question) * Please enter the name of your doctoral degree-granting institution. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of postgraduate research experience do you have as of the date you are submitting this application? (Open Ended Question) * Please select one of the following: I am a U.S. citizen I am a non-citizen national of the U.S. I am a permanent resident (green card holder) Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100794": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 383 Department Pharmacology/Exp Neuroscience 50000523 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by Research Needs Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Title/Academic Rank Postdoctoral Research Associate Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 10/12/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Pharmacology and Experimental Neuroscience, at the University of Nebraska Medical Center, is seeking a highly motivated postdoctoral research associate to join our research team investigating the mechanisms of HIV -associated aging and neuroimmune dysfunction. The successful candidate should hold a Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent degree in Immunology, Neuroscience, Pharmacology, Virology, Molecular Biology, or a related biomedical field, with a strong publication record and demonstrated expertise in HIV or infectious disease research or aging-related studies. Required Qualifications Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent degree in Immunology, Neuroscience, Pharmacology, Virology, Molecular Biology, or a related biomedical field Candidates should have hands-on experience in immunological techniques (flow cytometry, immune profiling, cell culture), neuroscience research (immunohistology and immunofluorescence imaging and associated data analysis, biochemical (measurement of reactive oxygen species from cells and tissues) and molecular biology methods (Western blotting, ELISA , PCR , omics-based analyses), and small animal handling. Supplemental Qualifications Experience with working on mouse models, behavioral testing, drug efficacy and toxicity studies, pharmacokinetic/pharmacodynamic analyses, and testing of antiretroviral or other therapeutic agents is highly desirable. The ideal candidate should possess excellent organizational, analytical, and communication skills, demonstrate the ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment, and be committed to conducting innovative translational research aimed at understanding and developing interventions for HIV -associated aging and related complications. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Lab environment, Animal facility, Office environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Not Applicable Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals Yes Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain As the work involves handling blood samples from humanized mice, all procedures will be performed in BSL -2+ laboratories with negative-pressure rooms and mandatory PPE to minimize the risk of direct exposure. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation both Repetitive Motion both Grasping both If you selected any area above, please explain Pipetting, keyboarding, slicing Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * If you have not yet graduated, can you provide an enrollment verification or enrollment certificate with expected graduation date from your university or institution? This can be uploaded as \"other document\" Yes No * If you do not yet have the degree required for this position, what is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * How many published articles do you have? (Open Ended Question) * Of these published articles, how many are you first-author (Open Ended Question) * Please enter the name of your doctoral degree-granting institution. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of postgraduate research experience do you have as of the date you are submitting this application? (Open Ended Question) * Please select one of the following: I am a U.S. citizen I am a non-citizen national of the U.S. I am a permanent resident (green card holder) Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100774": {"title": "Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Lincoln, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 389 Department CON-Lincoln Division 50000659 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Nursing FTE: TBD Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule DOQ Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 10/09/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Will provide classroom and clinical instruction in undergraduate and/or graduate programs and maintain academic scholarship and/or faculty practice, as appropriate. Required Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing minimum; doctorate in nursing preferred. Licensed or eligible for licensure in Nebraska. Supplemental Qualifications Current teaching experience and experience in clinical environment preferred. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Occasionally Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Occasionally Standing Occasionally Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals Yes Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Clinical setting Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation NA Repetitive Motion NA Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Resume Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a minimum of a Master's degree? Yes No * Are you eligible for practice licensure in NE? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100770": {"title": "Medical Director Kidney/Pancreas Transplant Program/Academic Rank/DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Medical Director Kidney/Pancreas Transplant Program/Academic Rank/DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Medical Director Kidney/Pancreas Transplant Program/Academic Rank/DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 376 Department Int Med Nephrology 50000593 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Medical Director Kidney/Pancreas Transplant Program/Academic Rank/DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Medical Director Kidney/Pancreas Transplant Program/Academic Rank/DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 10/09/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Medical Director Kidney/Pancreas Transplant Program The Division of Nephrology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha, NE is recruiting an experienced transplant nephrologist to join our faculty as Medical Director of the Kidney/Pancreas Transplant Program. This is a unique opportunity to provide clinical and administrative leadership for an established transplant program while helping shape its continued growth and development. The Division consists of fifteen faculty members who are committed to providing state of the art care to our patients, training nephrologists, internists and medical students, and building strong clinical and translational research programs. The transplant program consists of five transplant nephrologists (4 clinical, 1 research). We have had an AST accredited transplant nephrology fellowship and anticipate ACGME certification for 2027. We are also home to a fully accredited nephrology fellowship that offers three positions each year. Faculty within the Division are consistently rated as the top educators in Internal Medicine and have clinical and research interests in transplantation, glomerular disease, home dialysis and medical student education. Nebraska Medicine, our clinical partner, is home to Nebraska\u2019s only transplant center , and has performed more than 4,600 adult and pediatric kidney transplants and more than 1,250 living-donor kidney transplants. Over the past 3 years, the program has averaged 180 total kidney transplants and 50 living donor transplants Why Join Us \u00b7 Leadership with Impact \u2013 Provide clinical, administrative and strategic leadership for an established kidney/pancreas transplant program, with opportunities to advance quality, patient outcomes, program development and growth. \u00b7 Academic Excellence \u2013 Engage in the education and mentorship of nephrology fellows, residents and medical students while pursuing clinical and translational research within an academic medical center. \u00b7 Collaborative Environment \u2013 Practice within a multidisciplinary transplant team, partnering with transplant surgeons and specialists to provide comprehensive care for kidney and pancreas transplant patients. Exceptional Compensation and Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan (clinical, academic, and quality bonus compensation). Additional benefits include: \u00b7 CME allowance \u00b7 Competitive retirement contributions and other deferred comp opportunities \u00b7 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u00b7 A full suite of health and wellness benefits \u00b7 Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) eligible employer Why Omaha? Omaha offers the best of both worlds \u2013 affordability and opportunity. Recognized by Livability as one of the Top 100 Best Places to Live in 2026, highlighting the city for its quality of life, affordability, and strong community appeal. \u00b7 Highly rated public and private schools \u00b7 Vibrant arts, dining, and cultural scene \u00b7 Outdoor recreation, parks, and trails throughout the metro Omaha is an exceptional place to build your career and your life. Apply online: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100422 For additional information, please contact: Troy J. Plumb, MD Professor of Medicine Dr. Dennis Ross Chair and Chief, Division of Nephrology University of Nebraska Medical Center megan.frisbie@ unmc.edu Required Qualifications MD or DO (or equivalent) \u00b7 Board certified in Nephrology with UNOS certification or eligibility Supplemental Qualifications Demonstrated interpersonal, organizational, and leadership skills Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activities PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100679": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 382 Department Pediatrics Cardiology 50000628 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Title/Academic Rank Postdoctoral Research Associate Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 10/05/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) and Children\u2019s Nebraska invite applications for a Postdoctoral Research Fellow in Fetal Cardiovascular Imaging. We are seeking a highly motivated researcher with specialized training or experience in fetal ultrasound, fetal echocardiography, obstetric ultrasound, or cardiovascular imaging to join a multidisciplinary research program focused on improving prenatal detection and characterization of congenital heart disease ( CHD ) and other fetal conditions. The successful candidate will contribute clinical imaging expertise to research involving fetal ultrasound and echocardiography, including image review, annotation, quality assessment, quantitative analysis, and development of standardized imaging datasets. The fellow will work closely with fetal/pediatric cardiologists, maternal-fetal medicine specialists, sonographers, biomedical engineers, and artificial intelligence (AI)/data science collaborators. A major focus of the position will be translating knowledge of fetal anatomy, ultrasound imaging, and clinical workflows into high-quality imaging datasets and clinically meaningful research applications. The fellow will also participate in validation of AI-enabled fetal imaging tools but is not required to have primary expertise in AI algorithm development. Key Responsibilities Conduct research involving fetal ultrasound and fetal echocardiographic imaging, with emphasis on fetal cardiovascular anatomy, congenital heart disease, and prenatal screening. Review fetal ultrasound and echocardiographic studies and perform structured image annotation, cardiac view identification, image-quality assessment, and phenotypic characterization. Develop and implement standardized imaging annotation and quality-control protocols for fetal imaging research.Perform image preprocessing, quantitative measurements, and imaging feature extraction from clinical ultrasound and echocardiographic datasets. Assist with the development and curation of well-characterized fetal imaging datasets for clinical, translational, and AI-enabled research. Collaborate with AI/data science investigators by providing fetal imaging domain expertise for model development, training-data curation, validation, error analysis, and assessment of clinical relevance. Participate in studies evaluating AI-assisted fetal ultrasound screening and prenatal detection and classification of congenital heart disease and other fetal abnormalities. Work with fetal/pediatric cardiologists, maternal-fetal medicine specialists, sonographers, engineers, and data scientists on multidisciplinary research projects.Support management of imaging datasets, including DICOM organization, data quality assurance, de-identification, and documentation. Contribute to study design, IRB activities, research protocols, and data management.Analyze research findings and prepare abstracts, presentations, manuscripts, and grant-related materials. Present research at national and international scientific meetings and participate in the academic activities of the research team. Assist with training students and research personnel in fetal imaging review, annotation, and research methodology. Required Qualifications - MD, PhD, MD/PhD, or equivalent doctoral degree in medicine, ultrasound medicine, medical imaging, biomedical sciences, cardiovascular sciences, maternal-fetal medicine, or a closely related field. - Education, research training, or professional experience in fetal ultrasound, obstetric ultrasound, fetal echocardiography, or related clinical imaging. - Demonstrated knowledge of fetal anatomy, ultrasound imaging principles, and image-quality assessment. - Experience with medical image review, analysis, annotation, or quantitative imaging research. - Ability to work effectively in a multidisciplinary research environment involving clinicians, sonographers, engineers, and data scientists. - Strong written and verbal communication skills, with an interest in scientific publication and collaborative research. Supplemental Qualifications - Clinical or research experience in fetal echocardiography or fetal cardiac ultrasound. - Knowledge of fetal cardiovascular anatomy and standard fetal cardiac imaging views. - Experience with congenital heart disease, prenatal diagnosis, or fetal anomaly assessment. - Experience with fetal ultrasound image annotation, quality assessment, or imaging dataset development and curation. - Familiarity with DICOM imaging data, PACS , and medical imaging software. - Experience with quantitative ultrasound or echocardiographic analysis. - Experience with statistical analysis, scientific writing, and preparation of abstracts or peer-reviewed publications. - Previous participation in clinical, translational, or federally funded research. - Familiarity with artificial intelligence or machine-learning applications in medical imaging is desirable but not required. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Not Applicable Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise Yes Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * If you have not yet graduated, can you provide an enrollment verification or enrollment certificate with expected graduation date from your university or institution? This can be uploaded as \"other document\" Yes No * If you do not yet have the degree required for this position, what is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * How many published articles do you have? (Open Ended Question) * Of these published articles, how many are you first-author (Open Ended Question) * Please enter the name of your doctoral degree-granting institution. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of postgraduate research experience do you have as of the date you are submitting this application? (Open Ended Question) * Please select one of the following: I am a U.S. citizen I am a non-citizen national of the U.S. I am a permanent resident (green card holder) Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100660": {"title": "Remote Neuroradiology Overnights- Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Remote Neuroradiology Overnights- Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Remote Neuroradiology Overnights- Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Nebraska Requisition Number: 2026 - 370 Department Radiology 50000527 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: TBD Reg-Temp Academic - TBD Work Schedule Overnights Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Remote Neuroradiology Overnights- Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Remote Neuroradiology Overnights- Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type L1 - REG SPECIAL FAC/S Salary Range Salary Commesurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 10/02/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Radiology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) is seeking a fellowship trained teleradiologist in consideration for a remote evening position with manageable imaging volumes. This remote position has an evening schedule (5PM \u2013 3AM CST ) .Salary is highly competitive for this model (W2 and 1099 options are available). This position entails reading a mixture of both ER, inpatient and outpatient studies. The successful candidate should have outstanding credentials and be experienced in the interpretation of CT, CTA , MRI , ultrasound, and plain films with preference given to candidates who have previously completed a neuroradiology or emergency radiology fellowship. The position includes reading with and alongside our excellent in-house residents. Minimal phone call responsibilities. As this is strictly a clinical position, no lectures or research responsibilities are required for this role unless specifically sought out by the candidate. Candidates must be comfortable interpreting imaging studies outside of their primary subspecialty. The position is coupled with a fellowship trained neuroradiologist and a body radiologist during all hours of this shift. Additional swing shift radiologist coverage is utilized to keep imaging volumes very manageable. Our department utilizes state-of-the-art equipment in diagnostic radiology, interventional radiology, ultrasound, computed tomography, magnetic resonance imaging, and nuclear medicine. Enjoy an outstanding radiology lifestyle without sacrificing image quality or professional satisfaction in a progressive academic department supportive of work-life balance in radiology. Required Qualifications M.D. Board Certified in Radiology Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting 2-5 hours Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Body fluids \u2013 potential due to interaction with patients Moving machinery \u2013 x ray equipment has movement Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Keyboarding and writing Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100659": {"title": "Interventional Radiologist", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Interventional Radiologist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Interventional Radiologist Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 307 Department Radiology 50000527 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: TBD Reg-Temp Academic - TBD Work Schedule days, nights, weekends, as needed Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Interventional Radiologist Job Title/Academic Rank Interventional Radiologist/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 10/02/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Radiology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha, Nebraska is actively recruiting for a board-certified interventional radiologist with outstanding credentials to join our team of compassionate, patient-focused team of faculty. This 100% IR position is based at our University campus and also supports several satellite locations for our hospital partner, Nebraska Medicine. The division performs approximately 8,000 procedures per year. Our medical center has transplant services for all transplant organs and offers a full spectrum of liver directed therapies. Successful candidates should have a strong interest and dedication to academic radiology and duties will include teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows. Position will allow for dedicated academic time for teaching, CME , and potentially for research. Fellowship or additional training in Interventional Radiology is required. The Department of Radiology at UNMC offers a collegial and supportive working atmosphere, and as Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, UNMC is committed to the education of a 21st century health care work force. By supporting the mission of education, discovery, and leading-edge care, the Academic Health Sciences Center aims to improve the health of people and the communities across Nebraska and around the world. UNMC is nestled in mid-town Omaha with many amenities nearby. A mid-western city with a low cost of living, Omaha has many options for excellent public and private schools, with several universities and additional training programs available in the area. The city has an active food and entertainment life, and Eppley Airfield serves all major airlines with exceptionally easy access. Family activities include numerous parks and recreational facilities, children\u2019s museum, and children\u2019s theater. Numerous golf courses and country clubs also can be found spread throughout the city, and The Henry Doorly Zoo has consistently been named one of the premier zoos in the United States. The University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive work and learning environment free from discrimination and harassment. UNMC is dedicated to creating an environment where everyone feels valued, respected and included. Applications are being accepted online at http://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/. Applicants from diverse backgrounds are encouraged to apply. Required Qualifications M.D. Board certified in Radiology Fellowship or additional training in Interventional Radiology Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting 2-5 hours Crawling 2-5 hours Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Body fluids \u2013 potential due to interaction with patients Moving machinery \u2013 x ray equipment has movement Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Yes Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Manipulation and repetitive motion \u2013 keyboarding and handwriting Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent. Board certified or Board eligible (if within one-year of graduation). Yes No * Are you board eligible/board certified in the field specified in this posting? Yes No * Fellowship or additional training in Interventional Radiology? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100658": {"title": "Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 381 Department CON-Omaha Division 50000658 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Nursing FTE: TBD Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule DOQ Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 10/02/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Will provide classroom and clinical instruction in undergraduate and/or graduate programs and maintain academic scholarship and/or faculty practice, as appropriate. Required Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing minimum; doctorate in nursing preferred. Licensed or eligible for licensure in Nebraska. Supplemental Qualifications Current teaching experience and experience in clinical environment preferred. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Occasionally Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Occasionally Standing Occasionally Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Clinical setting Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation NA Repetitive Motion NA Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Resume Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a minimum of a Master's degree? Yes No * Are you eligible for practice licensure in NE? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100645": {"title": "Cardiovascular Postdoctoral Research Associate", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Cardiovascular Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Cardiovascular Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 377 Department Int Med Cardiovascular Med 50000584 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Cardiovascular Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Title/Academic Rank Cardiovascular Postdoctoral Research Associate Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 10/01/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Postdoctoral Opportunity in Hydrogel Synthesis and Biomedical Application Postdoctoral fellow position available in Dr. Bin Duan\u2019s lab within the Regenerative Medicine Program and Department of Internal Medicine at the University of Nebraska Medical Center. The research goal of Dr. Duan\u2019s lab is to develop innovative biomaterial-based drug delivery systems and engineered tissue platforms to understand and modulate cell\u2013material interactions, protect tissues from injury and disease, and promote tissue repair and regeneration. The lab focuses on advanced biomaterials, biofabrication approaches, and therapeutic delivery systems for applications in tissue protection, disease treatment, and regenerative medicine. The project associated with this postdoctoral opportunity will focus on the development and synthesis of novel hydrogels and their applications in anti-biofilm therapy and the prevention of postoperative surgical adhesions. Candidates with a strong background in polymer chemistry, hydrogel design and synthesis, organic chemistry, and cell and tissue culture are highly desired. Candidates should have a good publication record, should also demonstrate excellent communication skills and be independent, enthusiastic, and responsible. For additional information, please contact Bin Duan, Ph.D, bin.duan@unmc.edu . Required Qualifications PhD Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by academic and research activity. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving 2-5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by academic and research activity. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by academic and research activity. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100585": {"title": "Hematologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Hematologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Hematologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 342 Department Int Med Oncology/Hematology 50000591 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Hematologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Hematologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 09/28/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary BMT /Leukemia Faculty Opportunity The Division of Hematology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) is recruiting a compassionate, collaborative, and academically driven physician to join our nationally recognized Leukemia and Blood and Marrow Transplant Program. Practice at the Fred & Pamela Buffett Cancer Center, Nebraska\u2019s only National Cancer Institute ( NCI )-designated cancer center, where you will care for patients with acute and chronic leukemias across the continuum of disease. This faculty position offers the opportunity to expand access to novel therapies, advance leukemia research, and educate the next generation of hematologists and oncologists. Why Join Us \u00b7 Care for patients with acute and chronic leukemias while helping shape the future of leukemia treatment. \u00b7 Expand patient access to targeted therapies, immunotherapies, cellular therapies, and innovative clinical trials not widely available in the region. \u00b7 Collaborate with nationally recognized leukemia physicians, blood and marrow transplant specialists, cellular therapy experts, and a dedicated multidisciplinary team. \u00b7 Advance clinical and translational research through the Big Ten Cancer Research Consortium and investigator-initiated studies. \u00b7 Build an academic career through opportunities in research, teaching, leadership, and mentorship. Exceptional Compensation and Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: \u00b7 CME allowance \u00b7 Competitive retirement contributions and other deferred comp opportunities \u00b7 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u00b7 A full suite of health and wellness benefits \u00b7 Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) eligible employer Why Omaha? Omaha offers the best of both worlds \u2013 affordability and opportunity. Recognized by Livability as one of the Top 100 Best Places to Live in 2026, highlighting the city for its quality of life, affordability, and strong community appeal. \u00b7 Highly rated public and private schools \u00b7 Vibrant arts, dining, and cultural scene \u00b7 Outdoor recreation, parks, and trails throughout the metro Omaha is an exceptional place to build your career and your life. Qualifications \u00b7 MD or DO (or equivalent) \u00b7 Board certified or board eligible in Medical Oncology and/or Hematology \u00b7 Interest in teaching fellows, residents, and medical students \u00b7 Experienced physicians and graduating fellows are encouraged to apply Apply online: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99873 For additional information, please contact: Matthew Lunning, MD Chief, Division of Hematology Medical Director, Gene & Cellular Therapy Assistant Vice Chancellor of Research mlunning@unmc.edu Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent. Board certified in internal medicine and BC/BE in medical oncology and/or hematology. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment TBD by patient care, academic activity and research. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving 2-5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain TBD by patient care, academic activity and research. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain TBD by patient care, academic activity and research. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100584": {"title": "Hematologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Hematologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Hematologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 341 Department Int Med Oncology/Hematology 50000591 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Hematologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Hematologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 09/28/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary BMT /Lymphoma Faculty Opportunity Awaits The Division of Hematology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) is seeking a compassionate, collaborative, and academically driven physician to join our nationally recognized Lymphoma and Blood and Marrow Transplant Program. Practice at the Fred & Pamela Buffett Cancer Center, Nebraska\u2019s only National Cancer Institute ( NCI )-designated cancer center, where you\u2019ll provide comprehensive care for patients with lymphoma while contributing to groundbreaking research, medical education, and the advancement of innovative cancer therapies. Why Join Us \u00b7 Become part of a nationally recognized multidisciplinary lymphoma program dedicated to advancing patient care through collaboration and innovation. \u00b7 Practice alongside more than 200 medical oncologists, hematologists, surgeons, radiation oncologists, and cancer researchers. \u00b7 Help translate discoveries into patient care through robust clinical trials and research collaborations within the Big Ten Cancer Research Consortium. \u00b7 Deliver cutting-edge lymphoma care utilizing precision medicine, immunotherapy, cellular therapies, and targeted treatments. \u00b7 Grow your academic career through opportunities in research, teaching, leadership, and mentorship. Exceptional Compensation and Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: \u00b7 CME allowance \u00b7 Competitive retirement contributions and other deferred comp opportunities \u00b7 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u00b7 A full suite of health and wellness benefits \u00b7 Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) eligible employer Why Omaha? Omaha offers the best of both worlds \u2013 affordability and opportunity. Recognized by Livability as one of the Top 100 Best Places to Live in 2026, highlighting the city for its quality of life, affordability, and strong community appeal. \u00b7 Highly rated public and private schools \u00b7 Vibrant arts, dining, and cultural scene \u00b7 Outdoor recreation, parks, and trails throughout the metro Omaha is an exceptional place to build your career and your life. Qualifications \u00b7 MD or DO (or equivalent) \u00b7 Board certified or board eligible in Medical Oncology and/or Hematology \u00b7 Interest in teaching fellows, residents, and medical students \u00b7 Experienced physicians and graduating fellows are encouraged to apply Apply online: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99872 For additional information, please contact: Matthew Lunning, MD Chief, Division of Hematology Medical Director, Gene & Cellular Therapy Assistant Vice Chancellor of Research mlunning@unmc.edu Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent. Board certified in internal medicine and BC/BE in medical oncology and/or hematology. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment TBD by patient care, academic activity and research. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving 2-5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain TBD by patient care, academic activity and research. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain TBD by patient care, academic activity and research. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100583": {"title": "Rheumatologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Rheumatologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Rheumatologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 347 Department Int Med Rheumatology 50000594 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: Academic TBD Reg-Temp Academic - TBD Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Rheumatologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Rheumatologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 09/28/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary ACADEMIC RHEUMATOLOGIST OPPORTUNITY IN AMERICA\u2019S HEARTLAND The Division of Rheumatology and Immunology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, Nebraska is seeking an outstanding rheumatologist to join our faculty. The Division of Rheumatology has built a dynamic and collaborative group of academic clinicians with expertise in Rheumatology. We have strong clinical and basic research programs, including a nationally and internally famous clinical research program for rheumatoid arthritis. The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified/eligible in Rheumatology and has special interest in psoriatic arthritis. Candidates should excel in teaching medical students, residents and rheumatology fellows, and have a demonstrated commitment to excellence in basic and translational research. There will be opportunities for academic growth, career development and mentorship. As Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, UNMC and Nebraska Medicine are committed to the education of a 21st century health care work force, to finding cures and treatments for devastating diseases, to providing the best care for patients, and to serving our state and its communities through award-winning outreach. Our compensation package is extremely competitive. In addition, comprehensive benefits and relocation assistance are offered. Academic rank is dependent on qualifications. Interested candidates may apply with CV and letter of interest via this link \u2013 https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99867 Required Qualifications MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified/eligible in Rheumatology and has special interest in psoriatic arthritis. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, research and academic activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving 2-5 hours Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking 2-5 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, research and academic activities Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement TBD by patient care, research and academic activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100580": {"title": "Academic EM Physician/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Academic EM Physician/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Academic EM Physician/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 335 Department Emergency Medicine 50000655 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Varied Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Academic EM Physician/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Academic EM Physician/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 09/28/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Emergency Medicine at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, Nebraska is recruiting Emergency Medicine physicians to be an integral part of our faculty. The incoming faculty member will join a collegial team of Emergency Medicine physicians that are dedicated to providing extraordinary patient care to all. We are home to a well-established and fully accredited three-year emergency medicine residency program that offers 12 positions per year. The physician faculty for the Department of Emergency Medicine provide professional medical services at both Nebraska Medicine and Nebraska Medicine-Bellevue Medical Center. Nebraska Medicine is a nationally certified Level I Trauma Center, with a busy, high acuity ED serving nearly 65,000 patients annually, providing excellent physician and advanced practice provider coverage and 24/7 Emergency Medicine resident coverage. The community emergency department at Bellevue Medical Center is the second busiest ED in the state, with a census of over 35,000 visits annually. As Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, UNMC and Nebraska Medicine are committed to the education of a 21st century health care work force, to finding cures and treatments for devastating diseases, to providing the best care for patients, and to serving our state and its communities through award-winning outreach. The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified or board eligible in Emergency Medicine and possess excellent clinical, professional, and communication skills. We offer a highly competitive benefits package and rank and salary commensurate with qualifications. Candidates interested in working within a dynamic and stimulating setting may apply with CV and letter of interest. https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99771 Required Qualifications M.D. or equivalent. Board Certified/Board Eligible, Emergency Medicine Physician Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting 2-5 hours Crawling Occasionally Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Over 5 hours Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Over 5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Over 5 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current No Noise Yes Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Normal Emergency Department environment. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Suturing and keyboarding. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100395": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 367 Department Pathology, Microbiology & Immunology 50000521 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Monday-Friday, 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Title/Academic Rank Postdoctoral Research Associate Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 09/18/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary An NIH -funded Postdoctoral Research Associate position is available to study bacterial subversion of host lipid metabolism in the laboratory of Dr. Stacey Gilk in the Department of Pathology, Microbiology, and Immunology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center. The successful candidate will join an interdisciplinary research program investigating how the intracellular bacterial pathogen Coxiella burnetii , the causative agent of Q fever, reprograms host lipid metabolism to support infection and replication. Current projects focus on understanding how Coxiella manipulates lipid droplets and endoplasmic reticulum-lipid droplet (ER-LD) membrane contact sites through bacterial effector proteins, and how host lipid trafficking pathways contribute to pathogen survival. The postdoctoral fellow will employ a combination of cell biology, microbiology, molecular genetics, imaging, biochemistry, lipidomics, and metabolic approaches to characterize host-pathogen interactions and define mechanisms of lipid flux during intracellular infection. Ideal candidates will have a PhD in microbiology, cell biology, molecular biology, biochemistry, genetics, immunology, or a related field. Experience in one or more of the following areas is desirable: host-pathogen interactions, microscopy, intracellular bacteria, lipid metabolism, membrane trafficking, organelle biology, or metabolomics/lipidomics. The successful candidate will be a highly motivated, independent, rigorous, and hypothesis-driven scientist who will be expected to participate in training of graduate students, lab meetings, and other duties appropriate to the applicant\u2019s career goals. Applications should be submitted to https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100327 and include: A cover letter describing research experience, accomplishments, and future research interests and how they align with the position (maximum 2 pages) Curriculum vitae, including a complete list of publications Names and contact information for three references Required Qualifications PhD in microbiology or parasitology, cell biology, genetics, or other related field. Experience in related scientific field of study Supplemental Qualifications 2-3 years of research experience in host-pathogen interactions, cell biology, lipid metabolism, membrane trafficking, organelle biology, or related fields. Experience with one or more of the following techniques: mammalian cell culture, bacterial culture and growth assays, fluorescence and confocal microscopy, molecular cloning, genetic manipulation of mammalian cells and bacteria, quantitative gene expression analysis (qPCR/ RNA -based approaches), protein analysis, lipidomics/metabolomics, flow cytometry, or biochemical assays. Demonstrated ability to design and execute hypothesis-driven research, analyze complex datasets, and communicate findings effectively through publications and presentations. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Animal facility Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Lab coat, gloves and mask Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Laboratory techniques require the use of both sets of hands and wrists Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Ability to visualize test results. Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter C.V. Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * If you have not yet graduated, can you provide an enrollment verification or enrollment certificate with expected graduation date from your university or institution? This can be uploaded as \"other document\" Yes No * If you do not yet have the degree required for this position, what is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * How many published articles do you have? (Open Ended Question) * Of these published articles, how many are you first-author (Open Ended Question) * Please enter the name of your doctoral degree-granting institution. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of postgraduate research experience do you have as of the date you are submitting this application? (Open Ended Question) * Please select one of the following: I am a U.S. citizen I am a non-citizen national of the U.S. I am a permanent resident (green card holder) Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100392": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 366 Department Cellular/Integrative Physiology 50000525 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Title/Academic Rank Postdoctoral Research Associate Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 09/18/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary A Postdoctoral Research Associate position is available in the laboratory of Dr. Mabruka Alfaidi in the Department of Cellular and Integrative Physiology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center. The Alfaidi Lab studies vascular cell signaling and the role of molecular and genetic mechanisms in phenotypic changes associated with cardiopulmonary vascular disease. The successful candidate will design and conduct independent and collaborative research, analyze and interpret data, develop new research directions, and prepare scientific manuscripts under the guidance of the Principal Investigator. This position also offers advanced training to support scientific independence and career development, including opportunities to mentor students and contribute to a collaborative research environment. Required Qualifications Candidates must have a PhD or MD/PhD in vascular biology, pulmonary hypertension, or a closely related biomedical field. Applicants should have prior research experience in pulmonary vascular disease or related areas, with demonstrated expertise in several of the following techniques: \u2022 Endothelial cell culture. \u2022 Animal models of cardiovascular diseases. \u2022 Western blotting and qPCR. \u2022 Immunohistochemistry. \u2022 Single-cell sequencing and ATAC -seq. \u2022 Statistical analysis of experimental data. Candidates with previous experience in animal models of pulmonary or atherosclerotic diseases are particularly encouraged to apply. The ideal applicant will have experience presenting research findings at local, national, or international meetings and contributing to manuscript preparation for peer-reviewed scientific journals. The successful candidate should be self-motivated, able to manage multiple projects, work independently, and maintain professionalism in a collaborative research setting. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Animal facility Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Up to 2 hours Crawling Occasionally Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Up to 2 hours Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals Yes Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Works with chemicals and animals. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation NA Repetitive Motion NA Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * If you have not yet graduated, can you provide an enrollment verification or enrollment certificate with expected graduation date from your university or institution? This can be uploaded as \"other document\" Yes No * If you do not yet have the degree required for this position, what is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * How many published articles do you have? (Open Ended Question) * Of these published articles, how many are you first-author (Open Ended Question) * Please enter the name of your doctoral degree-granting institution. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of postgraduate research experience do you have as of the date you are submitting this application? (Open Ended Question) * Please select one of the following: I am a U.S. citizen I am a non-citizen national of the U.S. I am a permanent resident (green card holder) Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100303": {"title": "Multiple Sclerosis Neurologist - Academic Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Multiple Sclerosis Neurologist - Academic Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Multiple Sclerosis Neurologist - Academic Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 288 Department Neurological Sciences 50001975 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule As directed by Division Chief Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Multiple Sclerosis Neurologist - Academic Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Multiple Sclerosis Neurologist - Academic Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Neurological Sciences at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha, Nebraska is searching for a board certified/board eligible neurologist with fellowship training in Multiple Sclerosis and Neuroimmunology. The selected candidate will join our faculty and partner with two MS fellowship trained physicians, experienced nurse practitioners and physician assistancts and dedicated MS nurse case managers. This opportunity offers the ability to participate in the enhancement of our Multiple Sclerosis program and assist in further developing community services to boost access for patients with MS and other CNS demyelinating conditions in our community and the surrounding region through telemedicine initiatives. A teaching role with MS fellows, neurology residents and students, research activities and the provision of inpatient and outpatient services is included. UNMC supports robust research opportunities including current MS clinical trials. Our MS Clinic serves over 2000 patients, is proud to be designated as a Center for Comprehensive MS Care by the National Multiple Sclerosis Society and is affiliated with the Consortium of Multiple Sclerosis Centers ( CMSC ). The clinic has strong support from a designated pharmacy team essential in expediting MS therapies and supporting patients. Other multi-disciplinary partners and subspecialties include neuroradiology, neuroophthalmology, urology and uro-gynecology, rehab medicine and rehab physicians, spasticity and intrathecal baclofen clinic, psychiatry, Neurology trained physical, occupational, speech therapists, nutritionist and social work. As Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, UNMC is committed to the education of a 21st century health care work force, to finding cures and treatments for devastating diseases, to providing the best care for patients, and to serving our state and its communities through award-winning outreach. We offer a highly competitive benefits package. Rank and salary commensurate with qualifications. Omaha is a vibrant, attractive city with 1,000,000 people in the metropolitan area. Required Qualifications Board certified/board eligible neurologist with fellowship training in Multiple Sclerosis and demyelinating CNS illnesses. Supplemental Qualifications Experience in Multiple Sclerosis and demyelinating CNS illnesses research. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Clinical patient care Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100298": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 360 Department Eppley Inst Research 50000686 Business Unit(College/Institute) Eppley Institute FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Title/Academic Rank Postdoctoral Research Associate Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 09/15/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Caglayan laboratory at the Eppley Institute for Research in Cancer and Allied Diseases, University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ), is actively seeking highly motivated and talented Postdoctoral Research Associates to join out research team. Our research program, supported by funding from the National Institute of General Medical Services ( NIGMS ) and start-up funding for the Eppley Institute, is focused on unraveling the molecular mechanisms that govern DAN repair and genome maintenance. We integrate biochemistry, structural biology (X-ray crystallography and cryo-EM), and biophysics. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to contribute to cutting-edge research focused on the s ingle-molecule characterization of DNA repair proteins using Total Internal Reflection Fluorescence ( TIRF ) microscopy and C-Trap optical tweezers. Required Qualifications Seeking highly motivated candidates with a Ph.D. in Physics, Biochemistry, and/or Biophysics Supplemental Qualifications Candidates should have demonstrated research experience in one or more areas involving p rotein-nucleic acid interactions, single-molecule biophysics, fluorescence microscopy, optical tweezers, or related biophysical approaches. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Up to 2 hours Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Mice Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation N/A Repetitive Motion N/A Grasping N/A If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * If you have not yet graduated, can you provide an enrollment verification or enrollment certificate with expected graduation date from your university or institution? This can be uploaded as \"other document\" Yes No * If you do not yet have the degree required for this position, what is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * How many published articles do you have? (Open Ended Question) * Of these published articles, how many are you first-author (Open Ended Question) * Please enter the name of your doctoral degree-granting institution. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of postgraduate research experience do you have as of the date you are submitting this application? (Open Ended Question) * Please select one of the following: I am a U.S. citizen I am a non-citizen national of the U.S. I am a permanent resident (green card holder) Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100264": {"title": "Physician Assistant Education - Faculty Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Physician Assistant Education - Faculty Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Physician Assistant Education - Faculty Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 361 Department CAHP Physician Assistant 50000728 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Allied Health Professions FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Mon-Fri 8:00 am - 4:30 pm Telecommuting Opportunity Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Physician Assistant Education - Faculty Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Physician Assistant Education - Faculty Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title P.A. Education Faculty - DOQ Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 09/11/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The College of Allied Health Professions ( CAHP ) at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ), is seeking applicants for a full-time, 12-month faculty position in the Physician Assistant Education Program in Omaha, Nebraska. The position may offer the opportunity for a portion of the FTE to be devoted to clinical practice. The faculty member will provide teaching and clinical education support to students on both the Omaha and Kearney campuses. They will assist in PBL , clinical skills, and OSCE evaluations. Additionally, they will join in student experiences focused on clinical reasoning as a medical provider, assist in clinical site recruiting, support and evaluation, and assist in clinical phase student evaluation. They will engage in research in an area of clinical/educational expertise. This position has the opportunity for a hybrid work week that consists of a combination of both remote and on-campus work. Required Qualifications Graduate of an accredited PA, NP, or Medical Program. Master\u2019s degree in an appropriate field required. Two or more years of clinical experience required. Current license as a Clinician in the state of Nebraska or eligible for licensure. Current active certification as a Clinician required. Valid driver\u2019s license. Ability to maintain confidentiality in all matters. Ability to identify with, share in and have a commitment to the mission, philosophy and goals to the University of Nebraska Medical Center. Ability to travel to locations in and outside of the Omaha metro area for clinical site recruitment. Excellent human relations and effective communication skills. Qualities conducive to establishing and maintaining effective relationships with clinicians, co-workers in a small office setting, and community. Supplemental Qualifications The well qualified applicant will: \u2022 Hold a clinical or academic Doctoral degree, \u2022 Have work experience in a college or university setting, \u2022 Experience educating medical or PA students. \u2022 Relevant teaching experience. \u2022 Experience participating in an accreditation process \u2022 Experience in curriculum design, objective writing, and assessment. \u2022 Experience interacting with students. \u2022 Preferred knowledge of ARC -PA accreditation requirements for PA programs. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment n/a PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Up to 2 hours Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Participation in clinical practice will involve direct patient contact and could involve the use of medical equipment. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Use of a computer keyboard and mouse, medical equipment, writing utensils. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Will require occasional travel to to clinical sites and distant campuses. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a graduate of an accredited PA, NP, or Medical Program? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100263": {"title": "Academic EM Physician/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Academic EM Physician/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Academic EM Physician/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 336 Department Emergency Medicine 50000655 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Varied Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Academic EM Physician/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Academic EM Physician/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 09/11/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Emergency Medicine at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, Nebraska is recruiting Emergency Medicine physicians to be an integral part of our faculty. The incoming faculty member will join a collegial team of Emergency Medicine physicians that are dedicated to providing extraordinary patient care to all. We are home to a well-established and fully accredited three-year emergency medicine residency program that offers 12 positions per year. The physician faculty for the Department of Emergency Medicine provide professional medical services at both Nebraska Medicine and Nebraska Medicine-Bellevue Medical Center. Nebraska Medicine is a nationally certified Level I Trauma Center, with a busy, high acuity ED serving nearly 65,000 patients annually, providing excellent physician and advanced practice provider coverage and 24/7 Emergency Medicine resident coverage. The community emergency department at Bellevue Medical Center is the second busiest ED in the state, with a census of over 35,000 visits annually. As Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, UNMC and Nebraska Medicine are committed to the education of a 21st century health care work force, to finding cures and treatments for devastating diseases, to providing the best care for patients, and to serving our state and its communities through award-winning outreach. The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified or board eligible in Emergency Medicine and possess excellent clinical, professional, and communication skills. We offer a highly competitive benefits package and rank and salary commensurate with qualifications. Candidates interested in working within a dynamic and stimulating setting may apply with CV and letter of interest. https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99768 Required Qualifications M.D. or equivalent. Board Certified/Board Eligible, Emergency Medicine Physician Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting 2-5 hours Crawling Occasionally Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Over 5 hours Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Over 5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Over 5 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current No Noise Yes Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Normal Emergency Department environment. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Suturing and keyboarding. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100172": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 357 Department Eppley Inst Research 50000686 Business Unit(College/Institute) Eppley Institute FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Title/Academic Rank Postdoctoral Research Associate Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 09/04/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Perform various cell and molecular biology experiments to study the fundamental mechanism of gene transcription, RNA biology, and their relation to cancer development and drug resistance Required Qualifications PhD in Biochemistry, Molecular Biology, Biomedical Sciences, of Life Science-related field. Supplemental Qualifications Extensive experience in cell culture, molecular biology and biochemistry. Bioinformatics analysis of DNA / RNA sequencing data. Ideally have publications as first author in peer-reviewed journals. 3 years research experience. Strong background in molecular biology. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Up to 2 hours Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals Yes Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Mice Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation N/A Repetitive Motion N/A Grasping N/A If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * If you have not yet graduated, can you provide an enrollment verification or enrollment certificate with expected graduation date from your university or institution? This can be uploaded as \"other document\" Yes No * If you do not yet have the degree required for this position, what is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * How many published articles do you have? (Open Ended Question) * Of these published articles, how many are you first-author (Open Ended Question) * Please enter the name of your doctoral degree-granting institution. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of postgraduate research experience do you have as of the date you are submitting this application? (Open Ended Question) * Please select one of the following: I am a U.S. citizen I am a non-citizen national of the U.S. I am a permanent resident (green card holder) Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100038": {"title": "Ambulatory Care Physician/Asst Prof", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Ambulatory Care Physician/Asst Prof Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Ambulatory Care Physician/Asst Prof Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 313 Department Family Medicine 50000512 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by patient care, academic & research activity Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Ambulatory Care Physician/Asst Prof Job Title/Academic Rank Ambulatory Care Physician/Asst Prof Additional Requisition Title Ambulatory Care Physician/Asst Prof Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 08/28/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Family Medicine in the University of Nebraska Medical Center is seeking a dynamic and enthusiastic BC/BE Family Medicine physician with a passion for teaching. This position combines direct patient care and teaching in an integrated learning environment. You will be joining a well-established, experienced and highly cohesive 77-member faculty who are dedicated to the training and education of tomorrow\u2019s medical leaders. The ideal candidate must be an outstanding clinician and have a commitment to caring for ethnically and socioeconomically diverse patients. As Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, UNMC is committed to the education of a 21st century health care work force: to find cures and treatments for devastating diseases, to providing the best care for patients, and to serving our state and its communities through award-winning outreach. Primary Care Program ranked 5th nationally by U.S. News & World Report Collegial environment with exceptional physician leadership High physician satisfaction with low attrition Protected academic time Competitive salary with incentive opportunity and comprehensive benefits To learn more about the University of Nebraska, visit the sites below: University of Nebraska Strategic Plan \u201cOdyssey to Extraordinary\u201d: https://nebraska.edu/strategic-plan Get to know Nebraska: https://nebraska.edu/get-to-know-nebraska University of Nebraska Medical Center Campus https://www.unmc.edu/aboutus/index.html https://www.unmc.edu/aboutus/facts.html University of Nebraska Faculty & Staff Benefits: https://nebraska.edu/faculty-and-staff Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99556 Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent. Board certified in Family Medicine. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Clinical environment Other working environment n/a PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Incumbent in this position will be exposed to body fluids/biohazards and operate hand tools while providing patient care. PPE may be required for patient care. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes, both Repetitive Motion yes both Grasping n/a If you selected any area above, please explain Fine manipulation maybe required during patient care procedures and keyboards will be required for input of patient records. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the next 60 days, a PhD, MD, or Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible in the are identified in this posting? Are you eligible to practice in Nebraska? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/100037": {"title": "Child/Adolescent Psychiatrist/Assistant Professor", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Child/Adolescent Psychiatrist/Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Child/Adolescent Psychiatrist/Assistant Professor Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 278 Department Psychiatry 50000526 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F with occasional weekend coverage Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Child/Adolescent Psychiatrist/Assistant Professor Job Title/Academic Rank Child/Adolescent Psychiatrist/Assistant Professor Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary commensurate with experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 08/28/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The University of Nebraska Medical Center\u2019s Department of Psychiatry in Omaha, NE, is recruiting a child/adolescent psychiatrist to enhance our growing faculty. This role offers the chance to make a significant impact on the lives of young patients while being part of a dedicated community committed to mental health care and education. Key Features: \u00b7 Impactful Work \u2013 make a difference in the lives of children and adolescents within a diverse community, fostering their mental well-being and development \u00b7 Collaborative Environment \u2013 join a multidisciplinary team of mental health professionals and nurses who are committed to providing compassionate care in a supportive setting \u00b7 Flexible Schedule \u2013 enjoy a balanced lifestyle with a flexible schedule that accommodates personal and professional needs \u00b7 Innovative Care Models \u2013 engage in the development of forward-thinking clinical programs that promote integrated and collaborative approaches to mental health \u00b7 Research Opportunities \u2013 access to resources and support for research endeavors and professional development to further your career \u00b7 Engagement and Leadership \u2013 contribute to quality improvement initiatives, committee work, and departmental programs that align with your interests. \u00b7 Public Service Loan Forgiveness \u2013 we are a qualified employer under the Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) Program \u00b7 Quality Living \u2013 benefit from a low cost of living in Omaha \u2013 named by Forbes as the #1 Best City to Move to in the USA in 2024 We offer a highly competitive compensation package, including comprehensive benefits such as relocation assistance, CME funding, and a generous employer-paid retirement plan. The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree), board-certified in Psychiatry, For additional details, reach out to Dr. Howard Liu, Chair of the Psychiatry Department, at hyliu@unmc.edu. Interested applicants can apply online at https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99242 . UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Required Qualifications M.D. Board certified or board eligible in Child & Adolescent Psychiatry Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Over 5 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Not Applicable Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain This physician would work with outpatients primarily. Physician may be exposed to bodily fluids or medications in both of these settings. This physician would operate a computer. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain This physician would be writing, using the computer and other equipment necessary for patient care. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the next 60 days, a PhD, MD, or Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99905": {"title": "Licensed Psychologist (Academic Rank DOQ)", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Licensed Psychologist (Academic Rank DOQ) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Licensed Psychologist (Academic Rank DOQ) Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 340 Department MMI ICASD 50004879 Business Unit(College/Institute) Munroe-Meyer Institute FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule 8:00am - 5:00pm; Hours May Vary Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Licensed Psychologist (Academic Rank DOQ) Job Title/Academic Rank Licensed Psychologist (Academic Rank DOQ) Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 08/21/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Munroe-Meyer Institute ( MMI ) for Genetics and Rehabilitation at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha is currently accepting applications for psychologists in the Autism Diagnostic Clinic within the integrated Center of Autism Spectrum Disorders (iCASD). This is an open rank faculty position (Rank DOQ ). Ideal candidates will have a passion for participating in autism diagnostic evaluations within an interdisciplinary team, as well as mentoring and supervising predoctoral interns and post-doctoral fellows. Candidates will also have opportunities to coordinate and implement evidence-based treatment programs, such as parent training programs, social skills groups, and individualized therapy. The position is most appropriate for candidates with strong interests in applied clinical research, as well as those interested in applying for internal and extramural funding. Funding is available for specialized training opportunities, such as training in, and establishing research reliability on, the ADOS -2. Candidates must be eligible for licensure as a psychologist in the state of Nebraska. About iCASD: iCASD offers comprehensive ABA services to children diagnosed with autism that is focused on developing robust, meaningful social communication, play, social, and adaptive skills. The department is a collegial group of clinical educators and clinical researchers who seek to incorporate training and research activities into clinical service delivery within a highly collaborative, interdisciplinary center. MMI recently moved into a brand new, state- of-the-art facility and has prioritized expansion of innovative clinical and educational programs serving those with a wide range of physical, cognitive, social-emotional, and behavioral disabilities. All department faculty play an important role in education and provide clinical supervision for a variety of undergraduate and graduate students and post-doctoral fellows. Faculty in the department supervise predoctoral interns as part of the Nebraska Internship Consortium in Professional Psychology, which is APA accredited. Department faculty have opportunities to teach courses in the ABA Master\u2019s degree program, as well as the ABA doctoral degree program, which prepares graduates for clinical, research, or faculty positions. About MMI : MMI is one of the oldest, largest, and most comprehensive intellectual and developmental disability centers in the world. MMI\u2019s mission is \u201cto be world leaders in transforming the lives of all individuals with disabilities and complex health care needs, their families and the community through outreach, engagement, premier educational programs, innovative research and extraordinary patient care\u201d. MMI utilizes an interdisciplinary team approach that assures a comprehensive integration of our four pillars: research, clinical services, education, and community engagement. MMI recently moved in the world\u2019s most advanced, 220,000 sq ft facility for diagnostics and care of individuals with IDD . MMI is one of eight academic units of UNMC . MMI has an annual budget of more than $51M, a grant portfolio of >$16M, approximately 500 employees, and our 17 disciplines provide about 90,000 clinical services each year serving individuals with disabilities and complex medical needs across the lifespan. MMI is a federally designated University Center for Excellence in Developmental Disabilities ( UCEDD ) and has a Leadership Education in Neurodevelopmental and Related Disabilities ( LEND ) program. MMI provides limitless opportunities for clinical programming, innovative research, and community engagement. MMI is committed to expanding and supporting a diverse workforce as well as a diverse patient population to reflect the rich diversity in our culture including differences in ability, age, appearance, ethnicity, gender, gender expression, immigration status, language, nationality, race, religion, sex, sexuality, socio-economic status and other personal identities and experiences. About Omaha: With a metro area population of more than 1 million, Omaha is a vibrant, family centric, affordable city, with committed community partners, fiercely loyal and extremely generous community. Omaha is known for its progressive dining scene, myriad of cultural events, and friendly people. Omaha was recently ranked by Forbes as one of the most livable and affordable cities in the US and ranked by US News in the top 30 Best Places to Live in the US. To learn more about this opportunity contact Alice Shillingsburg, PhD, Director of iCASD, ashillingsburg@unmc.edu Key words: autism, diagnostic, assistant, associate, professor Required Qualifications PhD Licensure (or license eligible) in Nebraska is required. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Occasionally Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Potential exposure to blood, urine, vomit or other bodily fluids typically found in a primary care pediatric office. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Must be able to complete behavior management training in order to safely implement approved physical management procedures. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99897": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 344 Department COP Pharmaceutical Science 50000722 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Pharmacy FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F 8am-5pm Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Title/Academic Rank Postdoctoral Research Associate Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 08/20/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Develop protocols for iPSC culture, characterize ALS patient-derived induced pluripotent stem cells (iPSCs), and develop highly phenotypic assays for compound screening, mechanism of action, and target discovery studies. Required Qualifications PhD Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * If you have not yet graduated, can you provide an enrollment verification or enrollment certificate with expected graduation date from your university or institution? This can be uploaded as \"other document\" Yes No * If you do not yet have the degree required for this position, what is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * How many published articles do you have? (Open Ended Question) * Of these published articles, how many are you first-author (Open Ended Question) * Please enter the name of your doctoral degree-granting institution. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of postgraduate research experience do you have as of the date you are submitting this application? (Open Ended Question) * Please select one of the following: I am a U.S. citizen I am a non-citizen national of the U.S. I am a permanent resident (green card holder) Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99689": {"title": "Breast Imaging Radiologist - Remote/ Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Breast Imaging Radiologist - Remote/ Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Breast Imaging Radiologist - Remote/ Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 296 Department Radiology 50000527 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: TBD Reg-Temp Academic - TBD Work Schedule days, nights, weekends, as needed Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Breast Imaging Radiologist - Remote/ Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Breast Imaging Radiologist - Remote/ Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 08/10/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Radiology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) is seeking a fellowship-trained breast imaging radiologist for a remote position within our nationally recognized academic health system. Position Highlights 100% subspecialized breast imaging practice Remote, flexible schedule models also available Interpretation of screening and diagnostic mammography, breast ultrasound, and breast MRI within a dedicated breast imaging division Established remote division with over 20 remote radiologists to supplement our 30+ on-site staff radiologists Opportunity to practice in collaboration with the Fred & Pamela Buffett Cancer Center, Nebraska\u2019s only NCI -designated cancer center Participation in a comprehensive breast imaging program accredited as a Comprehensive Breast Imaging Center by the American College of Radiology and accredited by the National Accreditation Program for Breast Centers ( NAPBC ) Opportunities for resident and fellow education, mentorship, and academic engagement based on individual interests Opportunities for participation in multidisciplinary breast conferences and breast cancer care initiatives Salary and vacation: Highly competitive total compensation package including salary and time off when compared to Midwest private practices Generous CME budget Home workstation and technology support provided Qualifications M.D. or D.O. degree Board certified or board eligible by the American Board of Radiology Completion of a breast imaging fellowship, or equivalent breast imaging training and expertise Eligibility for medical licensure in Nebraska Strong commitment to clinical excellence, patient-centered care, and collaborative practice Environment & Technology Practice within a nationally recognized academic medical center committed to excellence in patient care, education, and research Access to advanced imaging technology and robust IT infrastructure supporting remote interpretation Collaborative relationship with breast surgeons, medical oncologists, radiation oncologists, pathologists, and other members of the multidisciplinary care team Supportive departmental culture focused on quality, innovation, professional growth, and physician satisfaction Opportunity to contribute to the education of residents and fellows within an established academic radiology program The University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive work and learning environment free from discrimination and harassment. UNMC is dedicated to creating an environment where everyone feels valued, respected, and included. Applications are being accepted online at https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99382 . Required Qualifications M.D. Board certified in Radiology Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting 2-5 hours Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Body fluids \u2013 potential due to interaction with patients Moving machinery \u2013 x ray equipment has movement Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Yes Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Manipulation and repetitive motion \u2013 keyboarding and handwriting Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you BC/BE in the area identified in the job posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99648": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 393 Department Anesthesiology 50000508 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F, 8:00 AM - 4:30 PM Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Title/Academic Rank Postdoctoral Research Associate Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 01/12/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The postdoctoral position will be part of a team effort to investigate HIV -induced vascular dysfunction and neuroAIDS molecular mechanisms using in vitro and in vivo (animal models) approaches. Specifically, the person will utilize HIV mouse models and HIV -1 infected cellular models to conduct experiments investigating the molecular events associated with cellular and vascular dysfunction in neuroAIDS. These studies will involve advanced molecular biology, including single cell transcriptomics, genomics and epigenomics, data analysis and interpretation. Additionally, molecular and cell biology techniques include molecular cloning, gene transfection and expression, siRNA technology, qPCR, FACS analysis, confocal imaging, histology, immunohistochemistry, immunofluorescence, ELISA , Western blots, and other protein chemistry techniques. The ideal candidate will be creative, highly motivated and have significant experience in these molecular and cell biology techniques; and preferably experience working with laboratory animals, including animal injection, collection and processing of animal tissues and biological fluids; and analyses of these samples. The candidate should be able to design and perform experiments with minimal supervision, critically analyze the results, summarize, present, and discuss the results with other team members, and help write manuscripts for publications. Required Qualifications PhD Supplemental Qualifications Ability to perform in vivo experiments with mice (including drug treatment/injection, blood collection, tissue harvesting, downstream analyses of blood and tissues); experience in molecular biology, single cell transcriptomics, genomics and/or epigenomics analyses. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Lab environment, Animal facility Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals Yes Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain This project will include work with laboratory animals (mice) collection and analysis of animal\u2019s blood and tissues, HIV infection of cells and mice, drug treatment of mice, and wearing of PPE during those experiments. Routine lab molecular biology and protein chemistry experiments involve solutions and media that include chemical compounds. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Yes, both Repetitive Motion Yes, both Grasping Yes, both If you selected any area above, please explain Routine animals and lab experiments will include very accurate pipetting, animal\u2019s dissection; accurate harvesting, collection, processing, and analysis of blood, organs, tissues and cells. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. N/A Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * If you have not yet graduated, can you provide an enrollment verification or enrollment certificate with expected graduation date from your university or institution? This can be uploaded as \"other document\" Yes No * If you do not yet have the degree required for this position, what is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * How many published articles do you have? (Open Ended Question) * Of these published articles, how many are you first-author (Open Ended Question) * Please enter the name of your doctoral degree-granting institution. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of postgraduate research experience do you have as of the date you are submitting this application? (Open Ended Question) * Please select one of the following: I am a U.S. citizen I am a non-citizen national of the U.S. I am a permanent resident (green card holder) Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99584": {"title": "Family Medicine Physician / OB / Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Family Medicine Physician / OB / Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Family Medicine Physician / OB / Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 267 Department Family Medicine 50000512 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by patient care, academic & research activity Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Family Medicine Physician / OB / Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Family Medicine Physician / OB / Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 07/31/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Family Medicine with OB The Department of Family Medicine at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha is recruiting a physician with a strong commitment to full-spectrum family medicine and obstetric care to join our faculty. We are continually looking for new and innovative ways to improve education and deliver high-value care for our patients. You will join a collaborative department of 73 faculty, resident physicians, and staff members dedicated to excellence in patient care, medical education, scholarship, and community engagement. This faculty position offers the opportunity to provide comprehensive obstetric services including prenatal care, labor and delivery, inpatient maternity care, postpartum care, and shared call coverage while helping educate and mentor medical students and residents in an academic environment. Opportunity Highlights Practice full-spectrum family medicine with obstetrics in a supportive academic environment Comprehensive obstetric care including prenatal care, labor and delivery, inpatient maternity care, postpartum care, and shared call responsibilities Strong commitment to physician well-being, supported by dedicated resources and engaged leadership Collegial faculty culture with exceptional physician leadership High physician satisfaction and strong faculty retention Protected academic time to support teaching and scholarly activities Collaborative academic environment with opportunities for clinical, educational, and scholarly engagement Opportunities to educate and mentor medical students and family medicine residents UNMC was recognized as a top-tier institution for primary care in the 2024\u20132025 U.S. News & World Report rankings UNMC is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness eligible employer Exceptional Compensation & Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: CME allowance Competitive retirement contributions and deferred compensation opportunities Comprehensive malpractice coverage Full suite of health and wellness benefits Living in Omaha Omaha offers the affordability of the Midwest with the amenities of a larger metropolitan area. Recognized by Livability as one of the Top 100 Best Places to Live in the U.S. in 2026, Omaha provides a welcoming, family-friendly community with a strong economy and exceptional quality of life. Residents enjoy: Top-rated schools A vibrant cultural scene Abundant recreational opportunities Qualifications MD/DO (or equivalent) with board certification/eligibility in Family Medicine. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to full-spectrum family medicine and obstetric care, possess outstanding interpersonal and teaching skills, and have enthusiasm for patient care in a collaborative academic setting. Experience caring for patients from diverse ethnic, cultural, and socioeconomic backgrounds is valued. Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99037 . Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent. Board certified in Family Medicine. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Clinical environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Incumbent in this position will be exposed to body fluids/biohazards and operate hand tools while providing patient care. PPE may be required during and epidemic. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Yes, both Repetitive Motion Yes, both Grasping n/a If you selected any area above, please explain Fine manipulation maybe required during patient care procedures and keyboards will be required for input of patient records. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the next 60 days, a PhD, MD, or Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible in the are identified in this posting? Are you eligible to practice in Nebraska? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99226": {"title": "Vice Chair of Research / General Dermatologist", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Vice Chair of Research / General Dermatologist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Vice Chair of Research / General Dermatologist Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 169 Department Dermatology 50000585 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F 8-5 pm, night call and weekends, varies Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Vice Chair of Research / General Dermatologist Job Title/Academic Rank Vice Chair of Research / General Dermatologist Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 07/10/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary We are seeking an accomplished and visionary Vice Chair of Research to lead our Department of Dermatology\u2019s research efforts and contribute to the advancement of dermatological science. The Vice Chair of Research will play a key role in shaping the research direction of the department, fostering collaboration, and elevating our academic and research programs. This position offers the opportunity to make a substantial impact on the future of dermatology research and patient care. Key Responsibilities: Research Leadership: Provide strategic leadership for the department\u2019s research initiatives, including basic, translational, and clinical research. Develop and execute a research strategy that aligns with the department\u2019s mission and objectives. Promote a culture of innovation, scientific rigor, and excellence in research. Collaboration and Networking: Foster collaboration with internal and external stakeholders, including academic institutions, industry partners, and funding agencies. Develop partnerships that enhance the department\u2019s research capabilities and opportunities. Represent the department in research-related matters at local, national, and international levels. Research Development: Lead efforts to secure research funding, grants, and contracts. Encourage and support faculty, researchers, and trainees in their research endeavors. Promote interdisciplinary research and facilitate multidisciplinary research teams. Academic Engagement: Contribute to the academic mission of the department by mentoring and educating students, residents, fellows, and faculty. Promote the dissemination of research findings through publications, presentations, and academic activities. Administration: Oversee the administrative aspects of the research program, including budget management, compliance, and research support services. Collaborate with the department chair on strategic planning and decision-making. Research Ethics and Compliance: Ensure adherence to ethical standards and regulatory requirements in research. Promote a culture of research integrity and responsible conduct. For Additional Information Karle Olnes, MBA Administrator, Department of Dermatology Email: karle.olnes@unmc.edu To Apply Please submit your CV, a cover letter outlining your research and leadership experience, and contact information for three professional references. Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/97575 Required Qualifications Medical Doctor (MD) or Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO) degree with board certification in Dermatology. Eligibility for medical licensure in the state of Nebraska. A record of significant contributions to dermatology research, including publications, grants, and collaborative research. Proven leadership experience in research, preferably in an academic or healthcare setting. Strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills. PhD, MS, or other advanced research degree preferred, not required. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Up to 2 hours Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PPE -gloves, gowns, mask potentially with sterile procedures. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Keyboarding is required for electronic medical record keeping Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/99103": {"title": "Physical Therapy Program Director", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Physical Therapy Program Director Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Physical Therapy Program Director Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 262 Department CAHP Physical Therapy 50000729 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Allied Health Professions FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Mon-Fri 8:00 am - 5 pm Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Physical Therapy Program Director Job Title/Academic Rank Physical Therapy Program Director Additional Requisition Title Physical Therapy Program Director Appointment Type M1 - REG ACAD ADMIN SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 07/01/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Program Director serves as the principal agent for each of the respective educational programs in the CAHP . The Program Director is responsible for providing leadership and administrative oversight to achieve the highest quality program outcomes in education, research, clinical practice, and service, thus ensuring continuous program accreditation. The Program Director oversees the development of program strategic priorities; participates in the execution of UNMC and CAHP strategic priorities, provides curricular oversight; recruits, develops, and evaluates program faculty and staff; participates in fiscal oversight and management of the program, and in collaboration with the CAHP Office of Research, develops the program\u2019s agenda for scholarly activity. Required Qualifications Holds an active, unencumbered PT license in any United States jurisdiction and is in compliance with the practice act in the jurisdiction where the program is located. Has earned an academic doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DSc, or related) or previous CAPTE -granted exemption. Holds the rank of associate professor or professor. Has a minimum of six years of full-time higher education experience, with a minimum of three years of full-time experience as a core faculty member in a CAPTE -accredited physical therapist education program. Supplemental Qualifications Commitment and capability to foster and sustain relationships with campus and community partners to support student success and programmatic growth. Collaborative communication and management style; working with all university stakeholders to ensure the success of the program. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Not Applicable Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Keyboarding, mousing. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This posting is for UNMC Employees only. Are you currently employed by the University of Nebraska Medical Center? Yes No Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98986": {"title": "Transplant Hepatologist/Assistant Professor/UnityPoint Health", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Transplant Hepatologist/Assistant Professor/UnityPoint Health Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Transplant Hepatologist/Assistant Professor/UnityPoint Health Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Des Moines, IA Requisition Number: 2026 - 237 Department Int Med GI 50001304 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Transplant Hepatologist/Assistant Professor/UnityPoint Health Job Title/Academic Rank Transplant Hepatologist/Assistant Professor/UnityPoint Health Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type P1 - REG HLTH FAC SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 06/26/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Transplant Hepatologist in beautiful south-central Iowa The Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center is recruiting a Transplant Hepatologist to practice at UnityPoint Health in Des Moines, Iowa . This is a unique opportunity to deliver the latest techniques and expertise in living-related, reduced-size, and auxiliary liver transplantation, while enjoying the benefits and support of a full-time academic faculty appointment. Highlights: \u00b7 Join a collaborative, multidisciplinary transplant team supporting living donors, candidates, and recipients \u00b7 Practice within an established multi-specialty clinic offering advanced diagnostic and therapeutic services. \u00b7 Participate in a robust tumor board and coordinate care for complex hepatology and transplant cases. \u00b7 Partner with referring physicians across central Iowa to deliver seamless, patient-focused care. \u00b7 Enjoy the autonomy and clinical support of a satellite transplant and hepatology program backed by UNMC expertise. \u00b7 Contribute to teaching, research, and shaping the future of transplant hepatology across central Iowa. Exceptional Compensation and Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: \u00b7 CME allowance \u00b7 Competitive retirement contributions and other deferred comp opportunities \u00b7 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u00b7 A full suite of health and wellness benefits We are committed to ensuring our physicians have the resources they need to excel both professionally and personally. Life in Des Moines Greater Des Moines ( DSM ) is a community that invests in itself, that is powered by multi-national corporations and also supports small, locally owned businesses. DSM is a community committed to cultivating an inclusive, equitable environment for people of all background. Whether you\u2019re looking for vibrant, urban living or a fresh start in the surrounding suburbs, Greater Des Moines has many communities to call home. Learn why Des Moines is one of the fastest-growing major metros in the nation and an amazing place to call home. Join Us! The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified/eligible in gastroenterology and transplant hepatology. Contact Fedja Rochling, MD, frochling@unmc.edu with questions or apply directly online \u2013 https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98631 We invite J-1 and H-1B visa candidates to apply. Required Qualifications The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified/eligible Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Keyboarding is required. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98984": {"title": "Gastroenterology Hospitalist/Academic Rank/DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Gastroenterology Hospitalist/Academic Rank/DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Gastroenterology Hospitalist/Academic Rank/DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 244 Department Int Med GI 50001304 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 50 Reg-Temp Part-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Gastroenterology Hospitalist/Academic Rank/DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Gastroenterology Hospitalist/Academic Rank/DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 06/26/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Gastroenterology Hospitalist \u2013 Part time The Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) is seeking a part time Gastroenterology Hospitalist to join our established and respected team. This opportunity offers an excellent balance of clinical practice, collaboration, and flexibility, making it ideal for a physician seeking a reduced schedule while remaining engaged in academic medicine and high-quality patient care. The successful candidate will work alongside a collegial group of specialists dedicated to clinical excellence, education, and advancing the mission of one of the nation\u2019s leading academic health centers. Why UNMC ? Dedicated Inpatient Role \u2013 Focus exclusively on general GI inpatient consults and endoscopies with a dedicated procedure room every day. Flexible Scheduling \u2013 Enjoy a two weeks on / two weeks off model \u2013 26 weeks per year (or alternative scheduling options, including 7 on/7 off, tailored to candidate preferences). Subspecialty Support \u2013 Access to subspecialists in Advanced Endoscopy ( EUS / ERCP ), IBD , hepatology, motility and nutrition support. Collaborative Team \u2013 Partner with GI Fellows to run the GI Inpatient Consult Service. Academic Environment \u2013 Ample opportunities for teaching fellows, residents, and medical students, as well as engaging in academic and quality-improvement initiatives. Exceptional Compensation and Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: \u00b7 CME allowance \u00b7 Competitive retirement contributions and other deferred comp opportunities \u00b7 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u00b7 A full suite of health and wellness benefits \u00b7 UNMC is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) eligible employer Living in Omaha Omaha offers an outstanding balance of urban amenities and family-friendly living. It is recognized by Livability as one of the Top 100 Best Places to Live in 2026, highlighting its quality of life, affordability, and strong sense of community. Residents enjoy vibrant food and arts scene, excellent schools, and easy access to parks and outdoor recreation all with a cost of living that allows for a comfortable and rewarding lifestyle. Join Us The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO, MD/PhD (or equivalent degree), board certified/board eligible in gastroenterology, and possess outstanding communication skills to collaborate with consulting physicians and hospital leadership. Contact: Fedja Rochling, MD, BCh, MBA \u2013 frochling@unmc.edu with questions Apply today: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98654 Required Qualifications MD, DO, or MBBS Must have completed an accredited three year gastroenterology training at time of start date. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Keyboarding is required. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98971": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 264 Department Genetics Cell Biology & Anatomy 50000507 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule 8:00 am - 5:00 pm Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Title/Academic Rank Postdoctoral Research Associate Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 06/25/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Developing and/or applying artificial intelligence, machine learning and/or data science-based methods to address cutting-edge topics, including but not limited to, large language models and foundation models, single cell analysis, spatial transcriptomics, multi-omics analysis, cancer research, intelligent healthcare, and precision medicine. Required Qualifications The prospective postdocs should have a PhD degree in a related field, and have research experience in artificial intelligence, machine learning, bioinformatics, and computational biology. A strong programming capability is necessary. Supplemental Qualifications Preferences will be given to those who have research experience in large language models (LLMs)/foundation models (FMs), single-cell analysis, multi-omics analysis, spatial transcriptomics, cancer research, intelligent healthcare, or precision medicine. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Not Applicable Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Not Applicable Sitting Over 5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Not Applicable Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation NA Repetitive Motion NA Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * If you have not yet graduated, can you provide an enrollment verification or enrollment certificate with expected graduation date from your university or institution? This can be uploaded as \"other document\" Yes No * If you do not yet have the degree required for this position, what is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * How many published articles do you have? (Open Ended Question) * Of these published articles, how many are you first-author (Open Ended Question) * Please enter the name of your doctoral degree-granting institution. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of postgraduate research experience do you have as of the date you are submitting this application? (Open Ended Question) * Please select one of the following: I am a U.S. citizen I am a non-citizen national of the U.S. I am a permanent resident (green card holder) Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98760": {"title": "Gastroenterology/Hospitalist/Academic Rank/DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Gastroenterology/Hospitalist/Academic Rank/DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Gastroenterology/Hospitalist/Academic Rank/DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 241 Department Int Med GI 50001304 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Gastroenterology/Hospitalist/Academic Rank/DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Gastroenterology/Hospitalist/Academic Rank/DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 06/11/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Gastroenterology Hospitalist The Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) is seeking a Gastroenterology Hospitalist to join our established and respected team. This role is ideal for a motivated physician who values collaboration, teaching, and providing the highest quality care to patients. Why UNMC ? Dedicated Inpatient Role \u2013 Focus exclusively on general GI inpatient consults and endoscopies with a dedicated procedure room every day. Flexible Scheduling \u2013 Enjoy a two weeks on / two weeks off model \u2013 26 weeks per year (or alternative scheduling options, including 7 on/7 off, tailored to candidate preferences). Subspecialty Support \u2013 Access to subspecialists in Advanced Endoscopy ( EUS / ERCP ), IBD , hepatology, motility and nutrition support. Collaborative Team \u2013 Partner with GI Fellows to run the GI Inpatient Consult Service. Academic Environment \u2013 Ample opportunities for teaching fellows, residents, and medical students, as well as engaging in academic and quality-improvement initiatives. Exceptional Compensation and Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: \u00b7 CME allowance \u00b7 Competitive retirement contributions and other deferred comp opportunities \u00b7 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u00b7 A full suite of health and wellness benefits \u00b7 Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) eligibility We are committed to ensuring our physicians have the resources they need to excel both professionally and personally. Living in Omaha Omaha is one of the most affordable cities in the U.S., with one of the lowest costs of living nationwide. Recognized by Forbes as the #1 Best City to Move to in 2024 , Omaha offers a thriving urban setting with a welcoming, family-friendly atmosphere. Residents enjoy: \u00b7 Top-rated schools \u00b7 A vibrant cultural scene \u00b7 Abundant recreational opportunities Join Us The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO, MD/PhD (or equivalent degree), board certified/board eligible in gastroenterology, and possess outstanding communication skills to collaborate with consulting physicians and hospital leadership. Contact: Fedja Rochling, MD, BCh, MBA \u2013 frochling@unmc.edu with questions Apply today: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98642 Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent Board certified in internal medicine. Board certified/eligible in gastroenterology or hepatology Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98759": {"title": "Genitourinary Oncologist/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Genitourinary Oncologist/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Genitourinary Oncologist/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 239 Department Int Med Oncology/Hematology 50000591 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Genitourinary Oncologist/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Genitourinary Oncologist/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 06/11/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary MEDICAL ONCOLOGY FACULTY AT THE UNIVERSITY OF NEBRASKA MEDICAL CENTER The Division of Hematology and Oncology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha, Nebraska is actively recruiting compassionate, patient-focused and collegial physicians to join our faculty. Successful candidates will have a focused interest in clinical care and clinical research for patients with Genitourinary malignancies including prostate cancer, bladder cancer, and renal cancer. The successful applicant will participate in the multidisciplinary clinical care of patients and the design and conduct of cancer clinical trials. These are exciting opportunities to join more than 200 oncologists, translational and basic scientists working together fusing science and medicine to speed up breakthroughs in the lab and deliver state of the art care to patients. As part of the Big Ten Cancer Research Consortium , a unique team-research culture drives science rapidly from ideas to treatment-changing paradigms. The Fred & Pamela Buffett Cancer Center, the only National Cancer Institute-designated cancer center in Nebraska, provides the best in science and clinical practice. Through collaboration between the UNMC\u2019s Oncology/Hematology Division and our hospital partner, Nebraska Medicine, patients experience personalized care based on the latest scientific research. The selected candidates will enjoy participation in multidisciplinary patient care teams, inpatient treatment, outpatient care, clinical trials and opportunities for collaboration for investigator initiated clinical research, and translational research. Ideal candidates will be board certified in internal medicine and BC/BE in medical oncology and/or hematology. We welcome newly trained physicians to consider these opportunities. Interest in teaching fellows, residents and medical students required. Inquiries may be directed to: Nicole Shonka, MD nshonka@unmc.edu Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98633 Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent. Board certified in internal medicine, Board certified/Board eligible in medical oncology and/or hematology. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activity. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activity. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activity. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98671": {"title": "General Dermatologist / Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | General Dermatologist / Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application General Dermatologist / Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 216 Department Dermatology 50000585 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F 8-5 pm, night call and weekends, varies Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title General Dermatologist / Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank General Dermatologist / Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 06/05/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary General Dermatology Faculty Opportunity University of Nebraska Medical Center \u2013 Department of Dermatology Omaha, Nebraska The University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) Department of Dermatology is seeking a BC/BE General Dermatologist to join our growing academic department in Omaha, Nebraska. Our Department Vision To advance dermatologic care through excellence in patient care, education, and impactful research within a collaborative and supportive academic environment. Our Core Values Innovation \u2022 Teamwork \u2022 Excellence \u2022 Compassion \u2022 Communication \u2022 Transparency What We Offer A collegial, engaged group of faculty committed to a shared mission Competitive salary and comprehensive benefits Opportunities for teaching medical students and residents Clinical partnerships with Children\u2019s Hospital & Medical Center, the VA Nebraska\u2013Western Iowa Health Care System, and hospitals across the Nebraska Medicine system Candidate Qualifications We are seeking board-certified or board-eligible dermatologists who are committed to delivering high-quality patient care and interested in academic medicine. Opportunities exist for involvement in education, research, and leadership. Strong interpersonal and communication skills are essential. As Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, UNMC is dedicated to improving the health of our communities and educating the next generation of health care professionals. For Additional Information Karle Olnes, MBA Administrator, Department of Dermatology Email: karle.olnes@unmc.edu To Apply Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98125 Required Qualifications M.D. or equivalent Board certified or Board eligible in Dermatology Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment, Lab environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving 2-5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Up to 2 hours Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current Yes Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PPE -gloves, gowns, mask potentially with sterile procedures. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Keyboarding is required for electronic medical record keeping Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98669": {"title": "Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 178 Department Pathology, Microbiology & Immunology 50000521 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 06/05/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Pathology and Microbiology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) invites applications for a full-time, tenure-leading faculty position in the division of Anatomic Pathology with board certification/eligibility in neuropathology. The successful candidate should be board-certified/eligible in neuropathology and will have the opportunity to participate in other services such as molecular diagnostics, surgical pathology subspecialties, or autopsy. Educational opportunities include teaching within the medical school and within an ACGME accredited AP/CP residency program. Candidates interested in developing a funded research program are encouraged to apply. Opportunities for developing clinical/translational research projects are also available. The successful candidate will hold an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. (or equivalent) degree, and they should be certified or eligible for certification in AP or AP/CP by the American Board of Pathology. Fellowship training in neuropathology is required. The department is a rapidly growing academic subspeciality-based practice with highly competitive compensation and opportunities for academic growth and administrative responsibilities. For additional information, please contact Dr. Joseph D. Khoury, Professor and Chair, Department of Pathology, Microbiology, and Immunology by clicking email . Interested candidates should submit a summary of their interests, CV and other documentation online through this link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/97640 Nebraska Medicine and UNMC share the same mission: to lead the world in transforming lives to create a healthy future for all individuals and communities through premier educational programs, innovative research and extraordinary patient care. This leading tertiary academic healthcare system is home to over 15,000 employees that include nearly 1,400 affiliated physicians covering primary care and nearly all specialty areas in medicine. The Nebraska Medical Center is the state\u2019s largest hospital and for several consecutive years has been awarded best in state by U.S. News & World Report, listed as one of the 100 greatest hospitals in America by Becker\u2019s Hospital Review and included in Forbes best in state employers. Omaha is the largest city in Nebraska and home to four Fortune 500 companies. This historic city sits along the Missouri River and features a vibrant cultural scene, family-friendly neighborhoods, and more than 250 public parks spread across its unique historic districts. In addition to supporting UNMC and Nebraska Medicine, Omaha\u2019s strong philanthropic community supports renowned attractions such as the Omaha Henry Doorly Zoo, Lauritzen Gardens, and the Omaha Symphony. Required Qualifications M.D., M.D./Ph.D., Ph.D., or equivalent degree Certified or eligible for certification in AP or AP/CP by the American Board of Pathology Supplemental Qualifications Fellowship training and board certification or eligibility in neuropathology Experience in medical student, pathology resident and/or fellowship training Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain PPE includes lab coat, gloves and mask plus N95 mask Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Pathology techniques require both sets of hands and wrist to complete. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Visual capacity is essential for medical direction and review of patient cases whether in paper, computer, physical or slide format. Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter C.V. Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an MD or MD/PhD degree in the field identified in the posting? Yes No * Are you board certified/board eligible in AP or AP/CP? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98474": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 217 Department Biochem and Molecular Biology 50000510 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Title/Academic Rank Postdoctoral Research Associate Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 05/26/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary A postdoctoral position is currently available in the Biochemistry and Molecular Biology Department at the University of Nebraska Medical Center, focused on novel combination therapy for glioblastoma (brain cancer). The potential candidate is expected to perform various cell and molecular biology techniques and in vitro and in vivo experiments to evaluate combination drug therapy in glioblastoma. He/she will also be involved in animal genotyping, animal drug treatment, and animal breeding. Required Qualifications A postdoc applicant should have a PhD in Biochemistry, Biomedical Sciences, or Life Sciences. Extensive experience in cell culture, 3D culture, drug screening, and fluorescent microscopy. A prior experience in molecular and cancer biology. A candidate should have publications as the first author in peer-reviewed journals. Bioinformatics analysis using a publicly available database. Supplemental Qualifications He/she should have at least 2-3 years of research experience. A strong background in cancer biology and therapeutic targeting is required. Further, knowledge in RNA -sequencing, pathological techniques, and in vivo preclinical research experience is desirable. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Lab environment, Animal facility Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Not Applicable Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Occasionally Standing Occasionally Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals Yes Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain All general hazards when working in any lab. Precautions will be used when working with hazardous materials. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation both Repetitive Motion both Grasping both If you selected any area above, please explain General lab benchwork, pipetting, etc. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * If you have not yet graduated, can you provide an enrollment verification or enrollment certificate with expected graduation date from your university or institution? This can be uploaded as \"other document\" Yes No * If you do not yet have the degree required for this position, what is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * How many published articles do you have? (Open Ended Question) * Of these published articles, how many are you first-author (Open Ended Question) * Please enter the name of your doctoral degree-granting institution. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of postgraduate research experience do you have as of the date you are submitting this application? (Open Ended Question) * Please select one of the following: I am a U.S. citizen I am a non-citizen national of the U.S. I am a permanent resident (green card holder) Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98456": {"title": "Addiction Psychiatrist/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Addiction Psychiatrist/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Addiction Psychiatrist/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 223 Department Psychiatry 50000526 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F with occasional weekend coverage Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Addiction Psychiatrist/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Addiction Psychiatrist/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Commensurate with experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary Addiction Medicine Psychiatry Opportunity Awaits at the University of Nebraska Medical Center The Department of Psychiatry at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, NE is recruiting an addiction psychiatrist to join our addiction division faculty. This unique opportunity shares time between a busy Addiction Psychiatry Consult Liaison Service and a robust outpatient addiction psychiatry practice that involves directing a true dual diagnosis intensive outpatient program. The rapidly growing Psychiatry Department and Addiction Division currently is comprised of an outpatient addiction psychiatrist, psychiatrist running the consult service, and an emergency medicine physician and pediatrician, all board certified in addiction medicine. The Addiction Medicine Fellowship is entering its 7th year. Nebraska Medicine, our hospital partner, has been recognized by U.S. News & World Report for the past 20 years. This means we continue to be ranked as one of America\u2019s Best Hospitals and the top hospital in Nebraska. Opportunity highlights: \u2022 Teaching opportunities alongside national leaders in psychiatry education and research \u2022 Multidisciplinary team of mental health professionals and nurses in a collegial environment \u2022 Flexible schedule for work life balance \u2022 Potential to develop novel clinical programs in integrated collaborative care \u2022 Abundant research and career advancement \u00b7 Addiction Medicine Fellowship that is in it\u2019s 5th year allows for ample teaching opportunities Community highlights: \u2022 Omaha, Nebraska is rated by Forbes magazine one of the top five best cities to raise a family \u2022 Continually earns national accolades for quality of life \u2022 Cost of living is 19 percent less than the national average \u2022 Thriving arts and entertainment scene \u2022 Home of the NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series and the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo Our compensation package is extremely competitive and includes comprehensive benefits, generous CME and faculty development funding are offered. The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree), who is board certified/eligible in addiction psychiatry or addiction medicine. Contact Dr. Howard Liu, Psychiatry Department Chair at hyliu@unmc.edu with questions. Interested candidates may apply online with CV and letter of interest at https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94688 . Required Qualifications M.D. Board eligible or board certified in addiction medicine and psychiatry Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Over 5 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Not Applicable Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain This physician would work with outpatient and inpatient patients. Physician may be exposed to bodily fluids or medications in both of these settings. This physician would operate a computer. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain This physician would be writing, using the computer and other equipment necessary for patient care. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a MD? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98447": {"title": "Consultation Liaison Psychiatrist/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Consultation Liaison Psychiatrist/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Consultation Liaison Psychiatrist/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 345 Department Psychiatry 50000526 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F with occasional weekend coverage Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Consultation Liaison Psychiatrist/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Consultation Liaison Psychiatrist/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The University of Nebraska Medical Center\u2019s Department of Psychiatry in Omaha, NE is looking for a Consultation Liaison Psychiatrist to join our dynamic faculty team. This position offers a rewarding blend of clinical practice, teaching, and the opportunity to engage with a diverse patient population, while contributing to the development of future healthcare providers. With 41 dedicated faculty members, our department co-administers a fully accredited residency program in general psychiatry and post-doctoral fellowship programs in addiction medicine and forensic psychiatry. Opportunity Highlights: -Balanced Work Schedule \u2013 enjoy a flexible 8-5 schedule that supports a family-friendly work-life balance -Collaborative Environment \u2013 work within a collegial team that includes psychiatrists, residents, APPs, and social workers -Program Development \u2013 opportunities to contribute to the creation of innovative clinical programs, particularly in integrated collaborative care -Professional Growth \u2013 participate in quality improvement initiatives, departmental committees, and programs tailored to your professional interests Exceptional Compensation & Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: - CME allowance -Competitive retirement contributions and other deferred comp opportunities -Comprehensive malpractice coverage -A full suite of health and wellness benefits -Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) qualified employer Living in Omaha Omaha is one of the most affordable cities in the US, with one of the lowest costs of living nationwide. Recognized by Forbes as the #1 Best City to Move to in 2024. Omaha offers a thriving urban setting with a welcoming, family-friendly atmosphere. Residents enjoy: -Top rated schools -A vibrant cultural scene -Abundant recreational opportunities The ideal candidate will be board certified/board eligible with interests in providing inpatient psychiatric consultation services to our hospitalized patients. both general psychiatry and addiction psychiatry. Fellowship training and/or board certification/eligibility for consultation-liaison psychiatry or addiction psychiatry is preferred but not required. For more information, please contact Dr. Howard Liu, Chair of the Psychiatry Department, at hyliu@unmc.edu. Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94659 Required Qualifications M.D. Board certified or board eligible in psychiatry Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Over 5 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Not Applicable Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain This physician would work with inpatients primarily. Physician may be exposed to bodily fluids or medications in both of these settings. This physician would operate a computer. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain This physician would be writing, using a computer and other equipment necessary for patient care. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a MD? Yes No * Are you board eligible/board certified in the field specified in this posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/98350": {"title": "Genetic Nurse Practitioner (Academic/Faculty Rank DOQ)", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Genetic Nurse Practitioner (Academic/Faculty Rank DOQ) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Genetic Nurse Practitioner (Academic/Faculty Rank DOQ) Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 213 Department MMI Genetic Medicine 50000694 Business Unit(College/Institute) Munroe-Meyer Institute FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Full time (12 months) Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Genetic Nurse Practitioner (Academic/Faculty Rank DOQ) Job Title/Academic Rank Genetic Nurse Practitioner (Academic/Faculty Rank DOQ) Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 05/15/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Munroe-Meyer Institute ( MMI ) for Genetics and Rehabilitation at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha is currently accepting applications for a faculty position in the Department of Genetic Medicine (Rank DOQ ) as a Genetic Nurse Practitioner. This role will involve direct collaboration with a medical geneticist and genetic counselor team to assess the needs of patients with genetic diseases and disorders and independently provide care to established patients with longitudinal needs, including individuals with inborn errors of metabolism. Prior experience within a genetics specialty team is not required. Practice Responsibilities: Conduct physical exams and assess health status, consulting with geneticists as needed. Conduct comprehensive genetic and medical evaluations in an outpatient setting. Collaborate closely with geneticists, genetic counselors, metabolic dietitians, and specialty care nursing. Order, interpret, and communicate results of genetic testing and biochemical studies. Develop and implement individualized care plans and provide longitudinal specialty care. Document clinical encounters accurately and in a timely manner in the Epic electronic health record. Educate patients and families regarding genetic conditions, testing options, and care plans. Research and review primary literature related to specific genetic diseases in the context of patient care. Participate in quality improvement, clinical program development, and academic activities as appropriate. Maintain compliance with institutional, state, and federal regulations, including HIPAA . Must maintain clinical privileges as a condition of employment. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong clinical assessment and diagnostic reasoning skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including accurate and thorough documentation. Commitment to patient- and family-centered care. Interest in developing expertise in genetics and genomics. Willingness to work collaboratively in an interdisciplinary and team-based environment. About MMI Genetic Medicine: MMI Genetic Medicine provides comprehensive genetic services through evaluation, counseling and testing in a clinic setting. Our providers offer patients information on recurrence risks and future family implications. This can help parents gain an understanding of what may have caused a disorder. About MMI : MMI is one of the oldest, largest, and most comprehensive intellectual and developmental disability centers in the world. MMI\u2019s mission is \u201cto be world leaders in transforming the lives of all individuals with disabilities and complex health care needs, their families and the community through outreach, engagement, premier educational programs, innovative research and extraordinary patient care\u201d. MMI utilizes an interdisciplinary team approach that assures a comprehensive integration of our four pillars: research, clinical services, education, and community engagement. MMI is one of eight academic units of UNMC . MMI has an annual budget of more than $40M, approximately 500 employees, and our 17 disciplines provide over 90,000 clinical services each year serving individuals with disabilities and complex medical needs across the lifespan. MMI is a federally designated University Center for Excellence in Developmental Disabilities ( UCEDD ) and has a Leadership Education in Neurodevelopmental and Related Disabilities ( LEND ) program. MMI provides limitless opportunities for clinical programming, innovative research, and community engagement. About Omaha: Omaha, Nebraska, is a dynamic and welcoming city that offers an exceptional quality of life. Known for its affordability, short commutes, and friendly Midwest atmosphere, Omaha also boasts a vibrant arts scene, nationally acclaimed restaurants, and abundant parks and trails. The city is home to the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo and Aquarium and hosts the annual NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series, both of which draw visitors from across the country. With several Fortune 500 companies, a growing innovation economy, and a strong sense of community, Omaha provides the perfect balance of professional opportunity and small-town charm\u2014making it an ideal place to live and work. Additional Information: MMI provides convenient on-site parking and access to an employee fitness center. To learn more about this opportunity, contact Craig V. Baker, MD, Director, MMI Genetic Medicine, at: cbaker@unmc.edu. Review of applicants will occur on a rolling basis as recruitment is ongoing. Rank will depend on qualifications. Applicants should upload with their application a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, and three letters of recommendation with contact information. University of Nebraska Employee Information: Faculty and Staff Benefits Required Qualifications Doctor of Nursing Practice ( DNP ), PhD in Nursing, or other terminal nursing practice degree. Eligibility for Nebraska APRN -NP. National certification ( AANP or ANCC , as applicable). Basic Life Support ( BLS ) certification. Supplemental Qualifications Experience as an APP in a clinical setting. Experience with Epic electronic health record system. Interest to teach trainees in both clinical and didactic setting. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Over 5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Masks when needed. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation NA Repetitive Motion NA Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD or DNP? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/97894": {"title": "Pediatrics Dental Faculty - Academic Rank Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Pediatrics Dental Faculty - Academic Rank Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Pediatrics Dental Faculty - Academic Rank Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 170 Department COD-Growth and Development 50000753 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Dentistry FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F hours TBD Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Pediatrics Dental Faculty - Academic Rank Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Pediatrics Dental Faculty - Academic Rank Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 04/30/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Join Our Team: Full-Time Tenure Leading Faculty \u2013 Pediatric Dentistry University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) College of Dentistry Department of Growth and Development, Division of Pediatric Dentistry The UNMC College of Dentistry invites applications for a full-time, tenure leading faculty position in the Department of Growth and Development, Division of Pediatric Dentistry. We are looking for a passionate educator and clinician who brings experience in teaching, research, and a shared commitment to excellence in patient care and dental education. Position Highlights -Teach and mentor dental students and residents in both didactic and clinical settings Provide instruction at multiple sites, including: -Children\u2019s Hospital & Medical Center (Omaha) -College of Dentistry (Lincoln) -Select extramural rotation sites Engage in scholarly activity and contribute to the growth of pediatric dental education Collaborate with a diverse team of educators and healthcare providers We especially welcome candidates who demonstrate: -Strong emotional and social intelligence -The ability to engage effectively with students, colleagues, and patients from all backgrounds Required Qualifications Qualifications - DDS / DMD from an ADA -accredited dental school or equivalent international degree -Completion of Part I and II of the National Board Dental Examination -Certificate/degree from a CODA -accredited Pediatric Dentistry program -Eligible for Nebraska dental licensure Supplemental Qualifications -Prior experience in dental education is preferred Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Not Applicable Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise Yes Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain exposures in conjunction with dental treatment Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation both Repetitive Motion both Grasping both If you selected any area above, please explain in conjunction with dental treatment Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Other Doc Cover Letter Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a DDS/DMD or foreign equivalent degree? Yes No * Will you have a Residency certificate in Pediatric Dentistry from an ADA accredited specialty training program by the date indicated in the position summary? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/97890": {"title": "Hospitalist/Academic Rank/DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Hospitalist/Academic Rank/DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Hospitalist/Academic Rank/DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 124 Department Int Med Hospital Medicine 50000599 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Hospitalist/Academic Rank/DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Hospitalist/Academic Rank/DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 04/30/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Join Our Team of 80 physician providers from varied backgrounds who have come together to create a true team in Omaha, Nebraska. Our Team Vision: To be identified by those we serve as the leaders, educators, and innovators transforming healthcare by providing extraordinary patient care. Our Team Core Values: Support Diversity of People, Flexibility of Practice, Encourage Professional Growth, Create an Environment of Inquiry and Enjoyment, and Embrace and Drive Change. With our team, you will find: \u2022 Opportunity to create and shape your career \u2022 Strong division mentorship \u2022 Highly engaged colleagues \u2022 Extremely competitive compensation package including tuition assistance \u2022 Flexible scheduling \u2022 Teaching and non-teaching services \u2022 Access to community and university hospitals \u2022 Robust ultrasound curriculum We are seeking BC/BE Internal or Family Medicine trained physicians committed to delivering excellent patient care. Ideally these individuals would have strong interest or experience in teaching, participation in meaningful quality improvement efforts and scholarly research. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills are a must. The University of Nebraska Medical Center is proud to be Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, committed to the next-generation education of our state\u2019s health care work force. Nebraska Medicine, our hospital partner, has been recognized by U.S. News & World Report for the past 20 years. This means we continue to be ranked as one of America\u2019s Best Hospitals and the top hospital in Nebraska. https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96843 Specific questions may be directed to: Chad Vokoun, MD Professor, Hospital Medicine Chief, Division of Hospital Medicine cvokoun@unmc.edu Required Qualifications MD, MBBS , DO or equivalent. Board certified or Board eligible Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, research and academic activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving 2-5 hours Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Up to 2 hours Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, research and academic activities Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement TBD by patient care, research and academic activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/97588": {"title": "Cardiac Surgeon - Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Cardiac Surgeon - Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Cardiac Surgeon - Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 168 Department Surgery-Cardiothoracic Surgery 50003926 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F 8-5; some night call and weekends; varies Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Cardiac Surgeon - Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Cardiac Surgeon - Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 04/16/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Cardiovascular Surgeon The Division of Cardiothoracic Surgery at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) is recruiting a cardiovascular surgeon to join our growing, high-volume practice. This is an exciting opportunity to work alongside national and international leaders in surgery, education, and research within a collaborative and innovative environment. As a regional leader in heart transplantation and ECMO , our division performs more than 40 annual heart transplants, 60 LVADs, and 100 ECMO procedures each year. Our expanding programs in transplantation, structural heart, and minimally invasive valve surgery make this an exceptional position for a surgeon passionate about advancing both clinical care and surgical education. This position is well suited to a new graduate or someone with 1-5 years of experience post training. The principal requirement for the candidate is the willingness and ability to do a wide variety of complex heart surgery including CABG , valve, multi-valve, and aortic cases. There is strong mentorship with several senior surgeons, however, the caseload tends to the more complex side, consistent with most academic medical centers. In addition to heavy clinical responsibility, the Division partners closely with the Center for Heart and Vascular Research, led by Rebecca Gundry, PhD. With robust extramural funding and a dedicated Heart and Vascular Clinical Research Unit, faculty with inclination can be well supported to do clinical trials or translational research. Opportunity Highlights Join a collegial team of five adult cardiac surgeons plus a dedicated procurement surgeon. Manageable 1:6 call schedule. Established cardiothoracic surgery residency program. Growing lung transplant program, top heart transplant program Active participation in TAVR , structural heart, and TEER programs Exceptional Compensation & Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: CME allowance Competitive retirement contributions and other deferred comp opportunities Comprehensive malpractice coverage A full suite of health and wellness benefits Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) eligible employer Living in Omaha Omaha is one of the most affordable cities in the US, with one of the lowest costs of living nationwide. Recognized by Forbes as the #1 Best City to Move to in 2024, Omaha offers a thriving urban setting with a welcoming, family-friendly atmosphere. Residents enjoy: \u2022 Top-rated schools \u2022 A vibrant cultural scene \u2022 Abundant recreational opportunities The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified/eligible in cardiovascular surgery with expertise and primary interest in heart valve disease including minimally invasive approaches. Excellent clinical skills and commitment to education are a must. A track record in minimally invasive valve operations and interest in translational or clinical research is preferred. Experience with transplant and mechanical circulatory support a plus. Apply today : https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/97566 Required Qualifications MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified/eligible in cardiovascular surgery with expertise and primary interest in heart valve disease including minimally invasive approaches. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current Yes Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals Yes Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Atmospheric and biohazards: radiation (x-rays), exposure to patients and research materials. Blood/body fluids: during patient exams and procedures Chemical hazards: lab chemicals Working on or around machinery: Medical/lab equipment Electrical current: Medical/lab equipment Work with lab animals: Research animals Operating hand/power tools: medical/lab equipment PPE : Surgical mask and non-latex gloves Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Operation of surgical tools and medical equipment during surgical procedures. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible in the are identified in this posting? Are you eligible to practice in Nebraska? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/97290": {"title": "Allergy &amp; Immunology/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Allergy &amp; Immunology/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Allergy & Immunology/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 137 Department Int Med Allergy/Immunology 50000597 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Allergy & Immunology/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Allergy & Immunology / Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 04/02/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Division of Allergy & Immunology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha has an opportunity for a physician with strong clinical interests to join our dynamic and close-knit team of six dedicated faculty members in this unique opportunity. Our division may be small, but it is vibrant and offers an engaging and collaborative environment where your contributions can make a real impact. The growing division features a rapidly expanding practice across five clinical sites. These include notable locations such as the Omaha VA Medical Center and Children\u2019s Nebraska. We are proud of the newly initiated fellowship program in allergy & immunology Why Join Us? \u00b7 Collaborative, collegial environment with opportunities for personal and professional development \u00b7 Basic science research labs located in state-of-the-art facilities in the heart of the campus \u00b7 An active clinical studies program with both investigator initiated and industry projects Exceptional Compensation & Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: \u00b7 CME allowance \u00b7 Competitive retirement contributions and other deferred comp opportunities \u00b7 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u00b7 A full suite of health and wellness benefits \u00b7 Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) qualified employer Living in Omaha Omaha is one of the most affordable cities in the US, with one of the lowest costs of living nationwide. Recognized by Forbes as the #1 Best City to Move to in 2024 , Omaha offers a thriving urban setting with a welcoming, family-friendly atmosphere. Residents enjoy: \u00b7 Top-rated schools \u00b7 A vibrant cultural scene \u00b7 Abundant recreational opportunities The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is a board certified/eligible in allergy & immunology. Contact Jill Poole, MD \u2013 csibley@unmc.edu with questions. Apply online at Apply online: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/97147 Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS , or equivalent degree who is board certified/eligible in allergy & immunology Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environment TBD by patient care, academic activity and research activity. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving 2-5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposure TBD by patient care, academic activity and research activity. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent Hand/Wrist TBD by patient care, academic activity and research activity Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/97186": {"title": "Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 133 Department COP Pharmaceutical Science 50000722 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Pharmacy FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F 8am-4:30pm Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Faculty position - Academic Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 03/27/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Tenure-leading Faculty Position in the Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences at the University of Nebraska Medical Center The Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) seeks outstanding applicants for a tenure-leading, twelve-month faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor. We seek an innovative and collaborative scientist whose research integrates computational approaches to advance any area of the drug discovery process such as medicinal chemistry and chemical biology. We are seeking candidates who will develop and apply computational approaches to understand, design, and optimize bioactive molecules and chemical probes. Applicants should have demonstrated productivity within their area of expertise and the potential to build a nationally recognized, externally funded research program and contribute to interdisciplinary teaching and training programs in medicinal chemistry and drug discovery. Candidates must have strong expertise in at least one of the following areas: Use of Artificial intelligence for De-Novo molecular design Machine learning/Neuronal networks to develop novel drug discovery tools Molecular modeling and simulation Theoretical biophysical medicinal chemistry Deep learning-based approaches to advanced molecular design Network Pharmacology Quantum computing Hybrid In Silico/In Vitro Pipelines Work at the interface of medicinal chemistry and computational approaches Responsibilities Establish and maintain an externally funded, high-impact research program Develop innovative computational and/or hybrid computational\u2013experimental drug discovery methods Teach undergraduate, graduate and professional courses in medicinal chemistry and related areas and develop undergraduate, graduate, and/or professional courses in their area of research expertise. Mentor graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and professional trainees Contribute to interdisciplinary research and training initiatives Participate in departmental and institutional service Application requirements \u00b7 A cover letter describing interest for the position \u00b7 Current curriculum vitae including a complete list of publications \u00b7 Concise four-page description of research plans \u00b7 One-page teaching philosophy \u00b7 The applicant must provide the names and contact information of at least three references The documents containing the research plans, teaching philosophy, and references should be uploaded as an \u201cother document\u201d. Applications must be submitted online at: jobs@unmc.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications should be received by July 15, 2026. Applications will be received and considered until the position is filled. Expected start date is Spring 2027. Relevant inquiries may be directed to the Chair of the Search Committee, Martin Conda Sheridan, at martin.condasheridan@unmc.edu . Required Qualifications PhD in Medicinal Chemistry, Computational Chemistry, Chemical Biology, Pharmaceutical Sciences, Chemistry, or a closely related field Postdoctoral training or equivalent Evidence of securing external funding Strong publication record in peer-reviewed journals Supplemental Qualifications Experience applying AI/ML methods to molecular or drug discovery problems Expertise in molecular modeling, cheminformatics, or simulation Experience with generative or predictive molecular design methods Integration of computational and experimental medicinal chemistry Collaborative and interdisciplinary research experience Teaching experience in medicinal chemistry or computational chemistry related to drug discovery Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Other Doc Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD degree in the field identified in this posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/97185": {"title": "Clinical Psychologist/Faculty Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Clinical Psychologist/Faculty Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Clinical Psychologist/Faculty Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 122 Department Psychiatry 50000526 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F with occasional weekend coverage Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Clinical Psychologist/Faculty Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Clinical Psychologist/Faculty Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range 95,000-110,000 Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 03/27/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The University of Nebraska Medical Center, Department of Psychiatry, in Omaha, Nebraska is seeking a Clinical Psychologist. The ideal candidate will have a doctoral degree in psychology from an APA / CPA -accredited or equivalent doctoral program with an APA / CPA accredited or equivalent doctoral internship required. The ideal candidate will have experience in women\u2019s health, including providing peripartum and postpartum psychological services, and a commitment to providing evidence-based care (e.g., evaluation, diagnosis, consultation and treatment) to patients within the organization and affiliated institutions using a biopsychosocial approach in concert with other members of the patient\u2019s health care team for the purpose of preventing or eliminating symptomatic, maladaptive, or undesired behavior and/or facilitating adaptation to physical illness, accident, or injury. Outstanding interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills required. Independent problem-solving skills and self-directed work experience required. These opportunities offer: -Medical student, resident and interprofessional teaching alongside national leaders in psychiatric education and research. -Multidisciplinary team of mental health professionals in partnership with more than 450 primary and specialty care physicians. -Highly competitive compensation package. -Flexible schedule in a family friend environment for work life balance. -Potential to develop novel clinical programs in integrated collaborative care. As Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, UNMC is committed to the education of a 21st century health care work force, to finding cures and treatments for devastating diseases, to providing the best care for patients, and to serving our state and its communities through award-winning outreach. Candidates are requested to apply online at: Specific questions may be addressed to Howard Liu, M.D., M.B.A., Chair, UNMC Psychiatry Department at hyliu@unmc.edu . Interested candidates can apply at https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96831 . Required Qualifications Doctoral degree in psychology from an APA / CPA -accredited or equivalent doctoral program with an APA / CPA accredited or equivalent doctoral internship required. Outstanding interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills required. Independent problem-solving skills and self-directed work experience required. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain This PhD would work with outpatients primarily. PhD may be exposed to bodily fluids or medications in this setting, and would operate a computer. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain This PhD would be writing, using the computer and other equipment necessary for patient care. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned doctoral degree in the field(s) identified in this post? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/97183": {"title": "Child/Adolescent Psychiatrist/Assistant Professor", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Child/Adolescent Psychiatrist/Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Child/Adolescent Psychiatrist/Assistant Professor Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 131 Department Psychiatry 50000526 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F with occasional weekend coverage Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Child/Adolescent Psychiatrist/Assistant Professor Job Title/Academic Rank Child/Adolescent Psychiatrist/Assistant Professor Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary commensurate with experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 03/27/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The University of Nebraska Medical Center\u2019s Department of Psychiatry in Omaha, NE, is recruiting a child/adolescent psychiatrist to enhance our growing faculty. This role offers the chance to make a significant impact on the lives of young patients while being part of a dedicated community committed to mental health care and education. Key Features: \u00b7 Impactful Work \u2013 make a difference in the lives of children and adolescents within a diverse community, fostering their mental well-being and development \u00b7 Collaborative Environment \u2013 join a multidisciplinary team of mental health professionals and nurses who are committed to providing compassionate care in a supportive setting \u00b7 Flexible Schedule \u2013 enjoy a balanced lifestyle with a flexible schedule that accommodates personal and professional needs \u00b7 Innovative Care Models \u2013 engage in the development of forward-thinking clinical programs that promote integrated and collaborative approaches to mental health \u00b7 Research Opportunities \u2013 access to resources and support for research endeavors and professional development to further your career \u00b7 Engagement and Leadership \u2013 contribute to quality improvement initiatives, committee work, and departmental programs that align with your interests. \u00b7 Public Service Loan Forgiveness \u2013 we are a qualified employer under the Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) Program \u00b7 Quality Living \u2013 benefit from a low cost of living in Omaha \u2013 named by Forbes as the #1 Best City to Move to in the USA in 2024 We offer a highly competitive compensation package, including comprehensive benefits such as relocation assistance, CME funding, and a generous employer-paid retirement plan. The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree), board-certified in Psychiatry, For additional details, reach out to Dr. Howard Liu, Chair of the Psychiatry Department, at hyliu@unmc.edu. Interested applicants can apply online at https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95565 . UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Required Qualifications M.D. Board certified or board eligible in Child & Adolescent Psychiatry Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Over 5 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Not Applicable Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain This physician would work with outpatients primarily. Physician may be exposed to bodily fluids or medications in both of these settings. This physician would operate a computer. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain This physician would be writing, using the computer and other equipment necessary for patient care. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96994": {"title": "General Neurologist Academic Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | General Neurologist Academic Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application General Neurologist Academic Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 112 Department Neurological Sciences 50001975 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule As directed by Division Chief Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title General Neurologist Academic Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank General Neurologist - Academic Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 03/20/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Neurological Sciences at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, NE has a position for a general neurologist. This is an opportunity to practice comprehensive neurology within a large academic department. Work and collaboration with multiple subspecialty programs such as Epilepsy, Headache, Neurovascular/Stroke, Movement Disorders, Neuromuscular, Multiple Sclerosis, Neuro-ophthalmology, and Cognitive & Behavioral Neurology. Opportunity Highlights: Work-life balance is a top priority Very diverse case mix spanning the spectrum of neurological disease Dedicated, robust ancillary services including neuropsychology, EMG , EEG and MEG , APP\u2019s, dietitians, & nurse case managers Opportunity to participate in clinical research, outreach activities, telemedicine, inpatient care, or quality improvement if desired Outpatient clinic opportunities at multiple locations Hospital partner, Nebraska Medicine, recognized by U.S. News & World Report as one of America\u2019s Best Hospitals Large neurology residency program with opportunities to work with residents in the clinic and teach Multiple fully accredited fellowship programs Community Highlights: Attractive city with population of more than 925,000 people Continually earns national accolades for quality of life Cost of living is far less than national average Thriving arts and entertainment scene Home of the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo and NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series Our compensation package is extremely competitive and includes multiple bonus opportunities, comprehensive benefits, generous employer paid retirement contributions, CME , and paid time off. The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) and is a board certified/eligible neurologist. Candidates should have an interest in teaching and be passionate about providing top level clinical care. Apply online at https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96712 Required Qualifications MD, MD/PhD or DO \u2013 Board eligible or certified in Neurology, eligible for Nebraska medical license Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Over 5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Over 5 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Patient care Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96756": {"title": "Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 082 Department CON-Omaha Division 50000658 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Nursing FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule DOQ Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 03/06/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Will provide classroom and clinical instruction in undergraduate and/or graduate programs and maintain academic scholarship and/or faculty practice, as appropriate. Required Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing minimum; doctorate in nursing preferred. Licensed or eligible for licensure in Nebraska. Supplemental Qualifications Current teaching experience and experience in clinical environment preferred. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Occasionally Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Occasionally Standing Occasionally Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Clinical setting Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation NA Repetitive Motion NA Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Resume Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a minimum of a Master's degree? Yes No * Are you eligible for practice licensure in NE? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96681": {"title": "Academic EM Physician/Faculty Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Academic EM Physician/Faculty Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Academic EM Physician/Faculty Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 099 Department Emergency Medicine 50000655 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Varied Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Academic EM Physician/Faculty Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Academic EM Physician/Faculty Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 03/04/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Emergency Medicine at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, Nebraska is recruiting Emergency Medicine physicians to be an integral part of our faculty. The incoming faculty member will join a collegial team of Emergency Medicine physicians that are dedicated to providing extraordinary patient care to all. We are home to a well-established and fully accredited three-year emergency medicine residency program that offers 12 positions per year. The physician faculty for the Department of Emergency Medicine provide professional medical services at both Nebraska Medicine and Nebraska Medicine-Bellevue Medical Center. Nebraska Medicine is a nationally certified Level I Trauma Center, with a busy, high acuity ED serving nearly 65,000 patients annually, providing excellent physician and advanced practice provider coverage and 24/7 Emergency Medicine resident coverage. The community emergency department at Bellevue Medical Center is the second busiest ED in the state, with a census of over 35,000 visits annually. As Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, UNMC and Nebraska Medicine are committed to the education of a 21st century health care work force, to finding cures and treatments for devastating diseases, to providing the best care for patients, and to serving our state and its communities through award-winning outreach. The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified or board eligible in Emergency Medicine and possess excellent clinical, professional, and communication skills. Preference will be given to candidates with experience in academic emergency medicine and/or has completed fellowship or advanced training. We offer a highly competitive benefits package and rank and salary commensurate with qualifications. Candidates interested in working within a dynamic and stimulating setting may apply with CV and letter of interest. https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96548 Required Qualifications M.D. or equivalent. Board Certified/Board Eligible, Emergency Medicine Physician Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting 2-5 hours Crawling Occasionally Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Over 5 hours Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Over 5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Over 5 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current No Noise Yes Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Normal Emergency Department Environment. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Suturing and keyboarding. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96342": {"title": "Non-Invasive Cardiologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Non-Invasive Cardiologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Non-Invasive Cardiologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 081 Department Int Med Cardiovascular Med 50000584 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by patient care, research and academic activity Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Non-Invasive Cardiologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Non-Invasive Cardiologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 02/13/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Non-Invasive Cardiologist in the Heart of America The Division of Cardiology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, Nebraska is recruiting a general, non-invasive cardiologist to join our rapidly growing and nationally recognized Division of Cardiovascular and Heart and Vascular programs. This exciting opportunity is ideally suited for a physician with clinical interests in consultative and outpatient cardiovascular care with non-invasive imaging (echo). Opportunity highlights: \u00b7 Join an 8-person general cardiology and advanced imaging group which has rapidly expanded to over 25,000 imaging procedures per year. The Section of Non-Invasive Cardiology and Advanced Imaging has expertise in all aspects of cardiac diagnostic imaging and is a part of an academic Division of Cardiology with more than 30 highly skilled cardiovascular physicians \u00b7 Combine clinical care, research, and medical student, resident, and fellow teaching in a world-renowned academic environment \u00b7 Perform research with research support available \u00b7 Be supported by a dedicated staff including experienced Nurse Practitioners and Physician Assistants \u00b7 Employer qualifies for the Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) Program Exceptional Compensation & Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: \u00b7 CME allowance \u00b7 Competitive retirement contributions and other deferred comp opportunities \u00b7 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u00b7 A full suite of health and wellness benefits Why Omaha? Omaha is consistently ranked among the most affordable and family-friendly cities in the U.S. In 2025, Forbes named Omaha the #1 Best City to Move To. Highlights include: \u00b7 Top-rated public and private schools \u00b7 A thriving arts and culture scene \u00b7 Home of the NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series and the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) is board certified/eligible in Cardiovascular Medicine. Excellent clinical, professional, and communication skills are required. Contact Division Chief Shane Tsai, shane.tsai@unmc.edu with questions or apply online \u2013 https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96239 Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent. Board certified or Board eligible in Cardiology. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments to be determined by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise Yes Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures to be determined by patient care, academic and research activities. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion to be determined by patient care, academic and research activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible in the are identified in this posting? Are you eligible to practice in Nebraska? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96175": {"title": "Physiatrist/ Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Physiatrist/ Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Physiatrist/ Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 069 Department Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation 50000718 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Varies Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Physiatrist/ Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Physiatrist/ Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 02/09/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha is recruiting physiatrists to join our expanding academic team for outpatient positions including musculoskeletal and pain. We are building a program that will elevate UNMC on the national stage, providing exceptional patient care, innovative research opportunities, and strong educational experiences. Opportunity Highlights \u00b7 Accredited PM&R residency (16 residents) and brain injury fellowship. \u00b7 Strong clinical partner: Collaborate with Madonna Rehabilitation Hospitals, one of the nation\u2019s largest free-standing rehab hospitals, providing a full spectrum of post-acute care including LTCH , inpatient, and outpatient rehabilitation. \u00b7 We treat a diverse patient population, including brain injury, stroke, spinal cord injury, and complex medical rehabilitation. \u00b7 Access to advanced rehabilitation technology and research collaboration through the Madonna Institute for Rehabilitation Science & Engineering. \u00b7 Opportunities to shape clinical programs, resident education, and research initiative s in a supportive academic environment. \u00b7 Work in a highly interdisciplinary setting with colleagues in therapy, neuropsychology, prosthetics/orthotics, and more. \u00b7 UNMC is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness eligible employer. Exceptional Compensation & Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: \u00b7 CME allowance \u00b7 Competitive retirement contributions and deferred comp opportunities \u00b7 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u00b7 Full suite of health and wellness benefits Living in Omaha Omaha is ranked by Forbes as the #1 Best City to Move to (2024) \u2013 affordable, family-friendly, and vibrant, with top-rated schools, cultural amenities, and abundant recreation. Qualifications MD/DO (or equivalent) with board certification/eligibility in Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation. Candidates should have outstanding interpersonal skills, enthusiasm for patient care, medical student, and resident education. Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96089 For more information, contact: Samuel Bierner, MD pmr@unmc.edu Required Qualifications MD/DO, BC/BE in Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Up to 2 hours Crawling Up to 2 hours Driving Up to 2 hours Kneeling Up to 2 hours Reaching Up to 2 hours Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Up to 2 hours Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current Yes Noise Yes Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Usual exposure risks in hospital or clinic Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation both Repetitive Motion both Grasping both If you selected any area above, please explain use of keyboard, usual physical examination maneuvers Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the next 60 days, a PhD, MD, or Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96173": {"title": "Retina Specialist/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Retina Specialist/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Retina Specialist/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 064 Department Ophthalmology and Visual Sciences 50000516 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by patient care Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Retina Specialist/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Retina Specialist/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 02/09/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Ophthalmology & Visual Sciences at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, NE, is recruiting a faculty member with fellowship training in retina diseases and surgery. This position includes opportunities for premier teaching, innovative research and extraordinary patient care in a world renowned academic environment. Faculty members enjoy the benefit of joining a well-established, expanding department with a collegial atmosphere that includes clinicians, basic scientists, and training professionals in an academic medical center setting. Our faculty pursue innovation, intellectual discourse and participation in an academic practice with an outstanding clinical partner in Nebraska Medicine. Ideal candidates will have an interest in pursuing a career encompassing robust clinical and surgical volumes, excellent clinical and basic science research opportunities and participation in outstanding residency and fellowship programs. Our 54,000 square foot Stanley M. Truhlsen Institute, opened in 2013, is a highly interactive, modern facility with a state of the art diagnostic center and experienced clinical research staff. As Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, UNMC is committed to the education of a 21st century health care work force, to finding cures and treatments for devastating diseases, to providing the best care for patients, and to serve Nebraska and its communities through award-winning outreach. We offer a highly competitive benefits package with academic rank and salary dependent on qualifications and experience. Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96069 Required Qualifications M.D Board Certified / Board Eligible Ophthalmologist. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Occasionally Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Occasionally Standing Occasionally Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Both fine, repetitive and grasping use both the right and left hand. One hand is not used over the other. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a MD? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96171": {"title": "Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 059 Department Pathology, Microbiology & Immunology 50000521 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBA Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 02/09/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Pathology and Microbiology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) invites applications for a full-time, tenure-leading faculty position in the division of Anatomic Pathology with board certification/eligibility in Cytopathology. The successful candidate should possess strong diagnostic skills in cytopathology and will have the opportunity to participate in rapid on-site evaluation as well as ultrasound-guided superficial fine needle aspiration procedures. Coverage of another subspecialty is an option. Educational opportunities include teaching within the medical school and within an ACGME -accredited AP/CP residency program. Opportunities for developing research projects are available. Candidates interested in developing a funded research program are also encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will hold an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. (or equivalent) degree, and they should be certified or eligible for certification in AP or AP/CP by the American Board of Pathology. Fellowship training in cytopathology is preferred. The department is a rapidly growing academic subspeciality-based practice with highly competitive compensation and opportunities for administrative responsibilities. For additional information, please contact Dr. Joseph D. Khoury, Professor and Chair, Department of Pathology and Microbiology through this email . Interested candidates should submit a summary of their interests, CV and other documentation online through this link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95956 Nebraska Medicine and UNMC , share the same mission: to lead the world in transforming lives to create a healthy future for all individuals and communities through premier educational programs, innovative research and extraordinary patient care. This leading tertiary academic healthcare system is home to over 15,000 employees that include nearly 1,400 affiliated physicians covering primary care and nearly all specialty areas in medicine. The Nebraska Medical Center is the state\u2019s largest hospital and for several consecutive years has been awarded best in state by U.S. News & World Report, listed as one of the 100 greatest hospitals in America by Becker\u2019s Hospital Review and included in Forbes best in state employers. Omaha is the largest city in Nebraska and home to four Fortune 500 companies. This historic city sits along the Missouri River and features a vibrant cultural scene, family-friendly neighborhoods, and more than 250 public parks spread across its unique historic districts. In addition to benefiting from major investments in the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ), Omaha\u2019s strong philanthropic community supports renowned attractions such as the Omaha Henry Doorly Zoo, Lauritzen Gardens, and the Omaha Symphony. Required Qualifications M.D., M.D./Ph.D., Ph.D., or equivalent degree Certified or eligible for certification in AP or AP/CP by the American Board of Pathology Supplemental Qualifications Fellowship training in breast pathology and/or surgical pathology Experience in medical student, pathology resident and/or fellowship training subspecialty fellow training. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain PPE includes lab coat, gloves and mask and N95 fitted Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Pathology techniques require both sets of hands and wrist to complete. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Visual capacity is essential for medical direction and review of patient cases whether in paper, computer, physical or slide format. Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter C.V. Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96103": {"title": "Fellow", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Fellow Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Fellow Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 073 Department MMI ICASD 50004879 Business Unit(College/Institute) Munroe-Meyer Institute FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Mon - Fri 8:00 am - 5:00 pm; Hours May Vary Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Fellow Job Title/Academic Rank Fellow Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 02/05/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Munroe-Meyer Institute ( MMI ) for Genetics and Rehabilitation at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha is currently accepting applications for a Fellow position(s) in the integrated Center of Autism Spectrum Disorders (iCASD). The fellow position is designed to provide interdisciplinary training in research and the provision of clinical services for individuals with genetic and behavior disorders and their families. Training occurs within the fertile clinical, research, and teaching environment of the University of Nebraska Medical Center. The individuals are encouraged to develop an area of clinical expertise, to begin a corresponding programmatic line of research, and to acquire the grant-writing skills necessary for securing extramural funding for the study and the assessment/treatment of autism spectrum disorders emphasized in the position but may also pursue the study and treatment of other genetic and behavior disorders. Track options include: 1) autism diagnostic services, 2) autism treatment tracks, 3) and autism diagnostic/treatment hybrid track. See UNMC \u2013 MMI iCASD website for more information regarding fellowship tracks. About MMI : MMI is one of the oldest, largest, and most comprehensive intellectual and developmental disability centers in the world. MMI\u2019s mission is \u201cto be world leaders in transforming the lives of all individuals with disabilities and complex health care needs, their families and the community through outreach, engagement, premier educational programs, innovative research and extraordinary patient care\u201d. MMI utilizes an interdisciplinary team approach that assures a comprehensive integration of our four pillars: research, clinical services, education, and community engagement. MMI is one of eight academic units of UNMC . MMI has an annual budget of more than $40M, approximately 500 employees, and our 17 disciplines provide over 90,000 clinical services each year serving individuals with disabilities and complex medical needs across the lifespan. MMI is a federally designated University Center for Excellence in Developmental Disabilities ( UCEDD ) and has a Leadership Education in Neurodevelopmental and Related Disabilities ( LEND ) program. MMI provides limitless opportunities for clinical programming, innovative research, and community engagement. About Omaha: Omaha, Nebraska, is a dynamic and welcoming city that offers an exceptional quality of life. Known for its affordability, short commutes, and friendly Midwest atmosphere, Omaha also boasts a vibrant arts scene, nationally acclaimed restaurants, and abundant parks and trails. The city is home to the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo and Aquarium and hosts the annual NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series, both of which draw visitors from across the country. With several Fortune 500 companies, a growing innovation economy, and a strong sense of community, Omaha provides the perfect balance of professional opportunity and small-town charm\u2014making it an ideal place to live and work. Additional Information: MMI provides convenient on-site parking and access to an employee fitness center. To learn more about this opportunity, contact Alice Shillingsburg, Director, integrated Center for Autism Spectrum Disorders (iCASD), at: ashillingsburg@unmc.edu. Review of applicants will occur on a rolling basis as recruitment is ongoing. Applicants should upload with their application a letter of interest and curriculum vitae. University of Nebraska Employee Information: Faculty and Staff Benefits Required Qualifications PhD or PsyD in Psychology or ABA Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Occasionally Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Occasionally Standing Occasionally Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Children with severe behavior disorders may cause bleeding to self or others. Arm guards and other protective equipment is sometimes worn to prevent injury from aggressive patients. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Must be able to stabilize and secure aggressive children for the child\u2019s safety as well as the safety of others. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * If you have not yet graduated, can you provide an enrollment verification or enrollment certificate with expected graduation date from your university or institution? This can be uploaded as \"other document\" Yes No * If you do not yet have the degree required for this position, what is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * How many published articles do you have? (Open Ended Question) * Of these published articles, how many are you first-author (Open Ended Question) * Please enter the name of your doctoral degree-granting institution. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of postgraduate research experience do you have as of the date you are submitting this application? (Open Ended Question) * Please select one of the following: I am a U.S. citizen I am a non-citizen national of the U.S. I am a permanent resident (green card holder) Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96039": {"title": "Academic Gastroenterologist/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Academic Gastroenterologist/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Academic Gastroenterologist/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 057 Department Int Med GI 50001304 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Academic Gastroenterologist/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Academic Gastroenterologist/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 02/02/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Gastroenterology faculty The Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha, NE is expanding and actively recruiting an academic gastroenterologist to join our faculty performing clinical care at our partner hospital, Bellevue Medical Center. This position offers an exciting opportunity to contribute to a growing clinical and academic program with diverse patient care, education, outreach, and research opportunities. Our division is part of a nationally recognized academic medical center with a strong commitment to excellence in patient care, teaching, and innovation. Through our primary clinical partner, Nebraska Medicine, we provide world\u2011class diagnosis and management of the broadest range of gastrointestinal and liver disorders using some of the most advanced diagnostic technologies available. We strongly emphasize a culture of: \u00b7 Collaboration, teamwork, and collegiality \u00b7 Education and mentorship of learners at all levels \u00b7 Patient\u2011centric, evidence\u2011based care \u00b7 Supportive and dedicated clinical and administrative staff Why Omaha? Omaha is recognized as the #1 Best City to Move To in 2024 by Forbes , boasting outstanding affordability, quality of life, strong employment opportunities, and a welcoming community \u2014 making it ideal for professionals and their families. Community highlights include: \u00b7 Affordable cost of living and housing \u00b7 Short commute times and excellent quality of life \u00b7 Robust cultural amenities, parks, and family\u2011friendly activities \u00b7 A thriving arts and entertainment scene with professional sporting events, museums, and one of the world\u2019s best zoos (Henry Doorly) Exceptional Compensation & Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: \u00b7 CME allowance \u00b7 Competitive retirement contributions and deferred comp opportunities \u00b7 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u00b7 Full suite of health and wellness benefits Qualifications The ideal candidate will be an MD/DO (or equivalent) with board certification/eligibility in Gastroenterology. We welcome physicians with interests across the full spectrum of gastroenterology. Candidates should have outstanding interpersonal skills, enthusiasm for patient care, medical student, and resident education. Visa Sponsorship We welcome applications from international medical graduates. J-1 visa candidates are encouraged to apply, and institutional support for J-1 visa sponsorship is available for this position. Contact Fedja Rochling, MD, BCh, MBA \u2013 frochling@unmc.edu Apply online: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95955 Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent Board certified in internal medicine. Board certified/eligible in gastroenterology or hepatology Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96038": {"title": "Academic Gastroenterologist/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Academic Gastroenterologist/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Academic Gastroenterologist/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 056 Department Int Med GI 50001304 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Academic Gastroenterologist/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Academic Gastroenterologist/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 02/02/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Gastroenterology faculty The Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha, NE is expanding and actively recruiting an academic gastroenterologist to join our faculty performing clinical care at our partner hospital, Bellevue Medical Center. This position offers an exciting opportunity to contribute to a growing clinical and academic program with diverse patient care, education, outreach, and research opportunities. Our division is part of a nationally recognized academic medical center with a strong commitment to excellence in patient care, teaching, and innovation. Through our primary clinical partner, Nebraska Medicine, we provide world\u2011class diagnosis and management of the broadest range of gastrointestinal and liver disorders using some of the most advanced diagnostic technologies available. We strongly emphasize a culture of: \u00b7 Collaboration, teamwork, and collegiality \u00b7 Education and mentorship of learners at all levels \u00b7 Patient\u2011centric, evidence\u2011based care \u00b7 Supportive and dedicated clinical and administrative staff Why Omaha? Omaha is recognized as the #1 Best City to Move To in 2024 by Forbes , boasting outstanding affordability, quality of life, strong employment opportunities, and a welcoming community \u2014 making it ideal for professionals and their families. Community highlights include: \u00b7 Affordable cost of living and housing \u00b7 Short commute times and excellent quality of life \u00b7 Robust cultural amenities, parks, and family\u2011friendly activities \u00b7 A thriving arts and entertainment scene with professional sporting events, museums, and one of the world\u2019s best zoos (Henry Doorly) Exceptional Compensation & Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: \u00b7 CME allowance \u00b7 Competitive retirement contributions and deferred comp opportunities \u00b7 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u00b7 Full suite of health and wellness benefits Qualifications The ideal candidate will be an MD/DO (or equivalent) with board certification/eligibility in Gastroenterology. We welcome physicians with interests across the full spectrum of gastroenterology. Candidates should have outstanding interpersonal skills, enthusiasm for patient care, medical student, and resident education. Visa Sponsorship We welcome applications from international medical graduates. J-1 visa candidates are encouraged to apply, and institutional support for J-1 visa sponsorship is available for this position. Contact Fedja Rochling, MD, BCh, MBA \u2013 frochling@unmc.edu Apply online: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95954 Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent Board certified in internal medicine. Board certified/eligible in gastroenterology or hepatology Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96036": {"title": "Pulmonary, Critical Care/Academic Rank/DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Pulmonary, Critical Care/Academic Rank/DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Pulmonary, Critical Care/Academic Rank/DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 054 Department Int Med Pulmonary 50000592 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by patient care, research and academic activity Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Pulmonary, Critical Care/Academic Rank/DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Pulmonary, Critical Care/Academic Rank/DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 02/02/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Join a Growing Pulmonary and Critical Care Team at UNMC The University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ), Division of Pulmonary, Critical Care & Sleep, is seeking a dynamic pulmonary and critical care medicine specialist to join our esteemed faculty team. This is an exceptional opportunity to advance your career while contributing to the growth of a thriving clinical program. In partnership with Nebraska Medicine, recognized for its comprehensive solid organ transplant program, our division delivers world-class care, fosters innovation, and provides unparalleled education opportunities for students and fellows. Opportunity Highlights Strong Institutional Support : Leadership invested in your professional success. Shaping the Future : Influence patient care, education, and groundbreaking research in a collaborative environment. Advanced Training Programs : Accredited fellowships in pulmonary/critical care and sleep medicine. Balanced Work Schedule : Designed to support your personal and professional well-being. Loan Forgiveness Eligibility : Qualify through the Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program. Why Omaha? Experience a vibrant city ranked among the Top 20 Best Cities to Live in the USA by Forbes . Omaha offers: Affordable living with a high quality of life. A thriving arts, entertainment, and dining scene. Exciting attractions, including the NCAA Men\u2019s College Baseball World Series and the world-famous Henry Doorly Zoo. Compensation and Benefits We offer a highly competitive compensation package , including: Comprehensive benefits and employer-paid retirement contributions. Generous CME allowances and paid time off. A supportive environment for personal and professional growth. The successful candidate should be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree), board certified/eligible in pulmonary and critical care medicine. We invite physicians with interest or expertise in cystic fibrosis or pulmonary hypertension to apply. Passion for teaching and mentorship. Contact Dr. Ruxana Sadikot, Chief, Division of Pulmonary, Critical Care & Sleep at rsadikot@unmc.edu or apply online \u2013 https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/ 95911 . Required Qualifications MD, MBBS , DO or equivalent. Board certified. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments to be determined by patient care, research and academic activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise Yes Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures to be determined by patient care, research and academic activities. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Yes-both Repetitive Motion Yes-both Grasping Yes-both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion to be determined by patient care, research and academic activities. Keyboarding is required for electronic medical recordkeeping. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board eligible/board certified in the field specified in this posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/96033": {"title": "General Dermatologist / Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | General Dermatologist / Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application General Dermatologist / Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 051 Department Dermatology 50000585 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F 8-5 pm, night call and weekends, varies Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title General Dermatologist / Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank General Dermatologist / Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 02/02/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary General Dermatology Faculty Opportunity University of Nebraska Medical Center \u2013 Department of Dermatology Omaha, Nebraska The University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) Department of Dermatology is seeking a BC/BE General Dermatologist to join our growing academic department in Omaha, Nebraska. Our Department Vision To advance dermatologic care through excellence in patient care, education, and impactful research within a collaborative and supportive academic environment. Our Core Values Innovation \u2022 Teamwork \u2022 Excellence \u2022 Compassion \u2022 Communication \u2022 Transparency What We Offer A collegial, engaged group of faculty committed to a shared mission Competitive salary and comprehensive benefits Opportunities for teaching medical students and residents Clinical partnerships with Children\u2019s Hospital & Medical Center, the VA Nebraska\u2013Western Iowa Health Care System, and hospitals across the Nebraska Medicine system Candidate Qualifications We are seeking board-certified or board-eligible dermatologists who are committed to delivering high-quality patient care and interested in academic medicine. Opportunities exist for involvement in education, research, and leadership. Strong interpersonal and communication skills are essential. As Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, UNMC is dedicated to improving the health of our communities and educating the next generation of health care professionals. For Additional Information Karle Olnes, MBA Administrator, Department of Dermatology Email: karle.olnes@unmc.edu To Apply Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95846 Required Qualifications M.D. or equivalent Board certified or Board eligible in Dermatology Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving 2-5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Up to 2 hours Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current Yes Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PPE -gloves, gowns, mask potentially with sterile procedures. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Keyboarding is required for electronic medical record keeping Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95963": {"title": "General Internal Medicine Physician/ Academic/DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | General Internal Medicine Physician/ Academic/DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application General Internal Medicine Physician/ Academic/DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026008 Department Int Med General Medicine 50000587 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title General Internal Medicine Physician/ Academic/DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank General Internal Medicine Physician/ Academic/DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/29/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary AMBULATORY INTERNAL MEDICINE OPPORTUNITY IN THE HEART OF THE MIDWEST The University of Nebraska Medical Center is recruiting a dynamic physician for an ambulatory general Internal Medicine position located in Omaha, Nebraska. The selected candidate will join a team of specialists with many years of experience in complex cases, providing exceptional care for adults. Nebraska Medicine, our hospital partner, has been recognized by U.S. News & World Report for the past 20 years. This means we continue to be ranked as one of America\u2019s Best Hospitals and the top hospital in Nebraska. Highlights of this opportunity include: \u2022 Outpatient only \u2013 flexible scheduling (with two half days protected administrative/academic time). No nights or weekends. Infrequent outpatient telephone call. \u2022 Gradual build up to manageable patient load in a team-based patient-centered medical home practice. \u2022 Wide range of practice from annual checkups for young adults to chronic medical conditions. \u2022 Collaborative culture and collegial environment with opportunities for personal and professional development. \u2022 Preceptor supervision of students/residents in clinic is available if desired. The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified/eligible in Internal Medicine. Candidates should have outstanding interpersonal and communication skills along with enthusiasm for outpatient internal medicine. Our compensation package is extremely competitive. In addition, comprehensive benefits and relocation assistance are offered. Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95384 Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent. Board certified/eligible in Internal Medicine. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving 2-5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the next 60 days, a PhD, MD, or Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95915": {"title": "General Internal Medicine/Hospital Medicine Hybrid/Academic Internal Medicine Physician", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | General Internal Medicine/Hospital Medicine Hybrid/Academic Internal Medicine Physician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application General Internal Medicine/Hospital Medicine Hybrid/Academic Internal Medicine Physician Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 041 Department Int Med General Medicine 50000587 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title General Internal Medicine/Hospital Medicine Hybrid/Academic Internal Medicine Physician Job Title/Academic Rank General Internal Medicine/Hospital Medicine Hybrid/Academic Internal Medicine Physician Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type L1 - REG SPECIAL FAC/S Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/28/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary AMBULATORY INTERNAL MEDICINE OPPORTUNITY IN THE HEART OF THE MIDWEST The University of Nebraska Medical Center is recruiting a dynamic physician for an hospitalist and ambulatory general Internal Medicine position located in Omaha, Nebraska. The selected candidate will join a team of specialists with many years of experience in complex cases, providing exceptional care for adults. Nebraska Medicine, our hospital partner, has been recognized by U.S. News & World Report for the past 20 years. This means we continue to be ranked as one of America\u2019s Best Hospitals and the top hospital in Nebraska. Highlights of this opportunity include: A combination of Inpatient and Outpatient \u2013Opportunities are available on teaching, non-teaching and surgical co-management services. The position may include supervision of medical students and residents along with the pursuit of other academic interests. Direct patient care is also a component of the position allowing faculty to keep their own diagnostic skills well-honed along with development of their teaching skills. Applicants would be joining an exciting, diverse and enthusiastic group of physicians. The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified/eligible in Internal Medicine. Candidates should have outstanding interpersonal and communication skills along with enthusiasm for outpatient internal medicine. Our compensation package is extremely competitive. In addition, comprehensive benefits and relocation assistance are offered. Interested candidates may apply with CV and letter of interest via \u2013 https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95776. Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent. Board certified/eligible in Internal Medicine. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving 2-5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95914": {"title": "General Internal Medicine/Hospital Medicine Hybrid/Academic Internal Medicine Physician", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | General Internal Medicine/Hospital Medicine Hybrid/Academic Internal Medicine Physician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manage