cademic interests. Direct patient care is also a component of the position allowing faculty to keep their own diagnostic skills well-honed along with development of their teaching skills. Applicants would be joining an exciting, diverse and enthusiastic group of physicians. The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified/eligible in Internal Medicine. Candidates should have outstanding interpersonal and communication skills along with enthusiasm for outpatient internal medicine. Our compensation package is extremely competitive. In addition, comprehensive benefits and relocation assistance are offered. Interested candidates may apply with CV and letter of interest via \u2013 https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95775 Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent. Board certified/eligible in Internal Medicine. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving 2-5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95819": {"title": "Non-Invasive Cardiologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Non-Invasive Cardiologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Non-Invasive Cardiologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 048 Department Int Med Cardiovascular Med 50000584 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: Academic TBD Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Either full time or part time position will be considered Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Non-Invasive Cardiologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Non-Invasive Cardiologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/22/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Non-Invasive Cardiologist in the Heart of America The Division of Cardiology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, Nebraska is recruiting a general, non-invasive cardiologist to join our rapidly growing and nationally recognized Division of Cardiovascular and Heart and Vascular programs. This exciting opportunity is ideally suited for a physician with clinical interests in consultative and outpatient cardiovascular care with non-invasive imaging (echo). Opportunity highlights: \u00b7 Join an 8-person general cardiology and advanced imaging group which has rapidly expanded to over 25,000 imaging procedures per year. The Section of Non-Invasive Cardiology and Advanced Imaging has expertise in all aspects of cardiac diagnostic imaging and is a part of an academic Division of Cardiology with more than 25 highly skilled cardiovascular physicians \u00b7 Combine clinical care, research, and medical student, resident, and fellow teaching in a world-renowned academic environment \u00b7 Perform research with research support available \u00b7 Be supported by a dedicated staff including experienced Nurse Practitioners and Physician Assistants \u00b7 Employer qualifies for the Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) Program Exceptional Compensation & Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: \u2022 CME allowance \u2022 Competitive retirement contributions and other deferred comp opportunities \u2022 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u2022 A full suite of health and wellness benefits Why Omaha? Omaha is consistently ranked among the most affordable and family-friendly cities in the U.S. In 2024, Forbes named Omaha the #1 Best City to Move To. Highlights include: \u2022 Top-rated public and private schools \u2022 A thriving arts and culture scene \u2022 Ample outdoor recreation and green space \u2022 Home of the NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series and the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) is board certified/eligible in Cardiovascular Medicine. Excellent clinical, professional, and communication skills are required. Contact Division Chief Shane Tsai, shane.tsai@unmc.edu with questions or apply online \u2013 https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95801 Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent. Board certified or Board eligible in Cardiology. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments to be determined by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise Yes Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures to be determined by patient care, academic and research activities. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion to be determined by patient care, academic and research activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible in the are identified in this posting? Are you eligible to practice in Nebraska? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95812": {"title": "Clinical Endocrinologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Clinical Endocrinologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Clinical Endocrinologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 042 Department Int Med DEM 50000586 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Clinical Endocrinologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Clinical Endocrinologist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/22/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Clinical Endocrinologist The Division of Diabetes, Endocrinology and Metabolism at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha is recruiting a general endocrinologist to join our faculty. This is an opportunity to join a rapidly expanding division that is highly recognized for its clinical and basic research programs. We are committed to excellence in clinical care, the education of medical students, residents, and fellows, and new discoveries to improve the care of patients with endocrine and endocrine-related disorders through laboratory and clinical research. Our long history of outstanding performance in all these areas is unmatched. Opportunity Highlights: Provide care for both inpatients and outpatients at Nebraska Medical Center and Bellevue Medical Center Cohesive group of colleagues in an intellectually stimulating environment Clinical practice at Nebraska Medical Center and Bellevue Medical Center \u00b7 Prioritization of physician well-being with ample resources and leadership support Recognized programs in diabetes, thyroid cancer, and other thyroid disorders, and adrenal and pituitary disorders Community Highlights: Forbes listed Omaha as the #1 Best City to Move in the USA in 2024 \u00b7 High quality of life and one of the lowest costs of living in the country Thriving arts and entertainment scene Home of the NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series and the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo Our compensation package is extremely competitive and includes comprehensive benefits, generous employer paid retirement contributions, CME , and paid time off . The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified/eligible in Endocrinology. Candidates should have excellent clinical, professional, and communication skills. Training and interest in clinical research and clinical trials as well as bedside ultrasound, ultrasound guided biopsy and potentially radio-frequency ablation is desirable. Apply now at https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95778 Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent. Board certified/Board eligible. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environment TBD by patient care, research, and teaching activity. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Up to 2 hours Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposure TBD by patient care, research, and teaching activity. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement TBD by patient care, research, and teaching activity. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95706": {"title": "Physiatrist/ Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Physiatrist/ Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Physiatrist/ Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 014 Department Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation 50000718 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule varies Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Physiatrist/ Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Physiatrist/ Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/16/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha is recruiting physiatrists to join our expanding academic team for outpatient positions including musculoskeletal and pain. We are building a program that will elevate UNMC on the national stage, providing exceptional patient care, innovative research opportunities, and strong educational experiences. Opportunity Highlights \u00b7 Accredited PM&R residency (16 residents) and brain injury fellowship. \u00b7 Strong clinical partner: Collaborate with Madonna Rehabilitation Hospitals, one of the nation\u2019s largest free-standing rehab hospitals, providing a full spectrum of post-acute care including LTCH , inpatient, and outpatient rehabilitation. \u00b7 We treat a diverse patient population, including brain injury, stroke, spinal cord injury, and complex medical rehabilitation. \u00b7 Access to advanced rehabilitation technology and research collaboration through the Madonna Institute for Rehabilitation Science & Engineering. \u00b7 Opportunities to shape clinical programs, resident education, and research initiative s in a supportive academic environment. \u00b7 Work in a highly interdisciplinary setting with colleagues in therapy, neuropsychology, prosthetics/orthotics, and more. \u00b7 UNMC is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness eligible employer. Exceptional Compensation & Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: \u00b7 CME allowance \u00b7 Competitive retirement contributions and deferred comp opportunities \u00b7 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u00b7 Full suite of health and wellness benefits Living in Omaha Omaha is ranked by Forbes as the #1 Best City to Move to (2024) \u2013 affordable, family-friendly, and vibrant, with top-rated schools, cultural amenities, and abundant recreation. Qualifications MD/DO (or equivalent) with board certification/eligibility in Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation. Candidates should have outstanding interpersonal skills, enthusiasm for patient care, medical student, and resident education. Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94686 For more information, contact: Samuel Bierner, MD pmr@unmc.edu Required Qualifications MD/DO, BC/BE in Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment na PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Up to 2 hours Crawling Up to 2 hours Driving Up to 2 hours Kneeling Up to 2 hours Reaching Up to 2 hours Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Up to 2 hours Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current Yes Noise Yes Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Usual exposure risks in hospital or clinic Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation both Repetitive Motion both Grasping both If you selected any area above, please explain use of keyboard, usual physical examination maneuvers Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the next 60 days, a PhD, MD, or Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95704": {"title": "Associate Professor -- Professor / Rank DOQ (Faculty)", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Associate Professor -- Professor / Rank DOQ (Faculty) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Associate Professor -- Professor / Rank DOQ (Faculty) Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026003 Department CON-Omaha Division 50000658 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Nursing FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Associate Professor -- Professor / Rank DOQ (Faculty) Job Title/Academic Rank Associate Professor - Professor / Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type P1 - REG HLTH FAC SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/16/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary This senior scientist position will be actively engaged in the research mission. Responsible for interdisciplinary research collaboration, sustaining funded research, maintenance of a national presence with regard to research, and mentoring junior nurse scientists and graduate students. Participates in the tripartite faculty role of research, teaching, and service. Required Qualifications Terminal degree required; doctorate in nursing preferred. Licensed (or eligible for licensure) in Nebraska. Supplemental Qualifications Clear demonstration of scholarly work and career development, including research projects that have received major funding, and scholarly publications in refereed research journals. Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to guide others in their research. Demonstrated excellence in interpersonal relations and communication skills. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Not Applicable Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Not Applicable Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Not Applicable Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Potential use of PPE while teaching in a clinical environment with students. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation NA Repetitive Motion NA Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD or DNP? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95702": {"title": "Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 017 Department Pathology, Microbiology & Immunology 50000521 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/16/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Pathology, Microbiology, and Immunology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) invites applications for a full-time, tenure-leading faculty position in the division of Anatomic Pathology with a focus on Breast Pathology. The successful candidate should possess strong diagnostic skills in breast pathology and will have the opportunity to participate in another subspecialty. Educational opportunities include teaching within the medical school and within an ACGME -accredited AP/CP residency program. Opportunities for developing research projects are available. Candidates interested in developing a funded research program are also encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will hold an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. (or equivalent) degree, and they should be certified or eligible for certification in AP or AP/CP by the American Board of Pathology. Fellowship training in breast pathology and/or surgical pathology is preferred. The department is a rapidly growing academic subspeciality-based practice with highly competitive compensation and opportunities for administrative responsibilities. For additional information, please contact Dr. Joseph D. Khoury, Professor and Chair, Department of Pathology and Microbiology through this email . Interested candidates should submit a summary of their interests, CV and other documentation online through this link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95068 Nebraska Medicine and UNMC , share the same mission: to lead the world in transforming lives to create a healthy future for all individuals and communities through premier educational programs, innovative research and extraordinary patient care. This leading tertiary academic healthcare system is home to over 15,000 employees that include nearly 1,400 affiliated physicians covering primary care and nearly all specialty areas in medicine. The Nebraska Medical Center is the state\u2019s largest hospital and for several consecutive years has been awarded best in state by U.S. News & World Report, listed as one of the 100 greatest hospitals in America by Becker\u2019s Hospital Review and included in Forbes best in state employers. Omaha is the largest city in Nebraska and home to four Fortune 500 companies. This historic city sits along the Missouri River and features a vibrant cultural scene, family-friendly neighborhoods, and more than 250 public parks spread across its unique historic districts. In addition to benefiting from major investments in the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ), Omaha\u2019s strong philanthropic community supports renowned attractions such as the Omaha Henry Doorly Zoo, Lauritzen Gardens, and the Omaha Symphony. Required Qualifications M.D., M.D./Ph.D., Ph.D., or equivalent degree Certified or eligible for certification in AP or AP/CP by the American Board of Pathology Supplemental Qualifications Fellowship training in breast pathology and/or surgical pathology Experience in medical student, pathology resident and/or fellowship training Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain PPE includes lab coat, gloves and mask plus N95 mask Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Pathology techniques require both sets of hands and wrist to complete. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Visual capacity is essential for medical direction and review of patient cases whether in paper, computer, physical or slide format. Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter C.V. Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95658": {"title": "Anesthesiology Faculty/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Anesthesiology Faculty/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Anesthesiology Faculty/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 029 Department Anesthesiology 50000508 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule As determined by Department Chairman Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Anesthesiology Faculty/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Anesthesiology Faculty/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/15/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Anesthesiologists to Join University of Nebraska Medical Center Faculty The Department of Anesthesiology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha is recruiting for opportunities in general anesthesia, critical care anesthesia and pediatric anesthesia. Our renowned department consists of 80 clinical faculty, 60 CRNAs and 65 residents and fellows. We have a strong history of outstanding patient care, innovation, and excellent educational program. Here you will find abundant resources and leadership support that promotes a culture of growth, well-being and hands-on teamwork utilizing the Anesthesia Care Team model. Our clinical partner, Nebraska Medicine, is consistently recognized by U.S. News & World Report as one of the elite hospitals in the nation. Opportunity Highlights: \u00b7 Flexible schedule in a family friendly environment \u00b7 Develop subspecialist expertise while maintaining a broad range of clinical skills \u00b7 Extremely competitive compensation, student loan forgiveness options , CME , relocation , employer paid retirement contributions, generous paid time off \u00b7 Focus on 2-3 anesthesia subsections of your choice for increased work satisfaction \u00b7 Non-clinical time to pursue career advancement, academic interests clinical research, and teaching \u00b7 Excellent resident physicians and certified registered nurse anesthetists \u00b7 J1 visa sponsorship available Community Highlights: Livability ranked Omaha in its top 20 list of Best Cities to Live in the USA \u00b7 High quality of life and one of the lowest costs of living in the country \u00b7 Nebraska is ranked in the top three states for physicians to practice by Becker\u2019s Hospital Review \u00b7 Thriving arts and entertainment scene \u00b7 Home of the NCAA Men\u2019s College Baseball World Series and the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo By focusing on transparency, trust, and teamwork, we are committed to continuously fostering a diverse team that leverages the rich opportunities that can be generated through an array of ideas, backgrounds, and experiences. The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree), who is board certified/eligible in anesthesiology. Interested candidates may apply online with CV and letter of interest at \u2013 https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95620 . Contact Sasha K. Shillcutt, MD, Professor and Vice-Chair, sshillcu@unmc.edu with questions. Required Qualifications M.D. or D.O. with graduation from an accredited anesthesiology residency program. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting 2-5 hours Walking 2-5 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Possible exposure to body fluids as part of clinical care. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation NA Repetitive Motion NA Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a MD/DO? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95656": {"title": "Retina/Uveitis Specialist - Faculty Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Retina/Uveitis Specialist - Faculty Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Retina/Uveitis Specialist - Faculty Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 018 Department Ophthalmology and Visual Sciences 50000516 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Retina/Uveitis Specialist - Faculty Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Retina/Uveitis Specialist - Faculty Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type P1 - REG HLTH FAC SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/15/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Ophthalmology & Visual Sciences at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, NE, is recruiting a board eligible/board certified faculty member for its retina division with fellowship training in uveitis and either medical or surgical retina. This position includes opportunities for premier teaching, innovative research and extraordinary patient care in a world-renowned academic environment. Faculty members enjoy the benefit of joining a well-established, expanding department with a collegial atmosphere that includes clinicians, basic scientists, and training professionals in an academic medical center setting. Our faculty pursue innovation, intellectual discourse and participation in an academic practice with an outstanding clinical partner in Nebraska Medicine. Ideal candidates will have an interest in pursuing a career encompassing robust clinical volumes, excellent clinical and basic science research opportunities and participation in outstanding residency and fellowship programs. Our 54,000 square foot Stanley M. Truhlsen Institute ( TEI ), opened in 2013, is a highly interactive, modern facility with a state-of-the-art diagnostic center and experienced clinical research staff. As Nebraska\u2019s only academic Department of Ophthalmology and the only provider of specialized uveitis eye care, training and innovation in the region, UNMC / TEI is committed to the education of the next generation, to finding cures and treatments for devastating diseases, to providing the best care for patients, and to serve Nebraska and its communities through award-winning outreach. We offer a highly competitive benefits package with academic rank and salary dependent on qualifications and experience. Required Qualifications M.D Board Certified / Board Eligible Ophthalmologist. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Occasionally Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Occasionally Standing Occasionally Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Both fine, repetitive and grasping use both the right and left hand. One hand is not used over the other. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a MD? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95643": {"title": "Gastroenterology/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Gastroenterology/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Gastroenterology/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 026 Department Int Med GI 50001304 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Gastroenterology/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Gastroenterology/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/15/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Gastroenterology faculty The Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, NE is recruiting an academic gastroenterologist to join us. We are expanding and offer opportunities for clinical scholars in general gastroenterology and major subspecialty areas including inflammatory bowel disease, liver disease, motility, endoscopy and intestinal failure. The potential for outreach to smaller communities and rural areas, telehealth and participation in clinical research is a highlight of this position. Our hospital partner, Nebraska Medicine, is one of the nation\u2019s most highly rated centers for the diagnosis and treatment of digestive disorders, covering the full breadth of gastrointestinal diseases and liver disorders. We utilize some of the most advanced diagnostic technologies available in the country. Opportunity Highlights: \u2022 Culture of collaboration, teamwork and collegiality \u2022 Outstanding faculty of renowned researchers \u2022 Patient-centric mindset to provide the highest quality service and patient care \u2022 Supportive and dedicated staff Community Highlights: \u2022 Omaha, Nebraska is rated by Forbes magazine as one of the top five best cities to raise a family \u2022 High quality of life and cost of living below the national average \u2022 Thriving arts and entertainment scene \u2022 Home of the NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series and the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo Our compensation package is extremely competitive and includes comprehensive benefits, generous employer paid retirement contributions, CME , and paid time off. The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree), who is board certified/eligible in gastroenterology with a strong commitment to patient care and teaching. Opportunities exist for individuals of all experience levels and various clinical interests. Interested candidates may apply with CV and letter of interest at https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95581 Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent Board certified in internal medicine. Board certified/eligible in gastroenterology or hepatology Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95642": {"title": "Transplant Hepatologist/Academic Rank/DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Transplant Hepatologist/Academic Rank/DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Transplant Hepatologist/Academic Rank/DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 025 Department Int Med GI 50001304 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Transplant Hepatologist/Academic Rank/DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Transplant Hepatologist/Academic Rank/DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/15/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, NE is actively recruiting a compassionate, patient-focused and collegial transplant hepatologist to join our faculty. The selected candidate will have a concentrated focus on the delivery of top-quality patient services and operational excellence. Nebraska Medicine, our hospital partner, is home to one of the most reputable and well-known liver organ transplant programs in the country. Since its inception in 1985, Nebraska Medicine\u2019s Liver Failure and Transplant Program has earned international recognition, a worldwide referral base and Medicare designation. Through our dedicated efforts in education, research, and clinical medicine, we have helped shape the field of liver transplants Opportunity Highlights: \u00b7 Latest techniques and expertise in living-related, reduced-size and auxiliary liver transplants \u00b7 Experienced multidisciplinary transplant team caring for living donors, candidates for transplant and recipients \u00b7 Dedicated anesthesiology team \u00b7 Fully accredited transplant hepatology fellowship \u00b7 Regional outreach opportunities Community Highlights: Live in a Top-Rated City! Omaha is No. 14 Most Affordable Places to Live in the U.S. by U.S. News & World Report U.S. News & World Report ranks Omaha among the Best Places to Live in the U.S. Recognized among the Best Places to Raise Kids by Smartasset.com Ranks as one of the Best Cities for Runners by Smartasset.com Smartasset.com ranks Omaha as the No. 16 Most Livable City in the U.S Our compensation package is extremely competitive and includes comprehensive benefits, generous employer paid retirement contributions, CME , and paid time off. The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO, MD/PhD (or equivalent degree), who is board certified/eligible in gastroenterology and transplant hepatology. We are looking for an individual who is committed to excellence in patient care, teaching and research. Contact Fedja Rochling, MD \u2013 frochling@unmc.edu with questions. Apply online at https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95580 Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent Board certified in internal medicine. Board certified/eligible in gastroenterology and transplant hepatology Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95641": {"title": "Advanced Endoscopist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Advanced Endoscopist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Advanced Endoscopist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 024 Department Int Med GI 50001304 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Advanced Endoscopist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Advanced Endoscopist/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/15/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Academic Gastroenterology \u2013 Advanced Endoscopy at UNMC The Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, NE has an opportunity for an advanced endoscopist to join us. In this faculty role, you will join two advanced endoscopists as the third member of the team. Our hospital partner, Nebraska Medicine, is ranked by U.S News and World Report as one of the nation\u2019s best gastroenterology programs to treat the biliary/pancreatic system, colon, esophagus, small bowel and stomach. Opportunity Highlights: \u00b7 Mix of procedures, inpatient care, and outpatient clinic \u00b7 Robust GI, medical oncology, and surgical oncology multidisciplinary teams \u00b7 Prioritization of physician well-being with ample resources and leadership support \u00b7 Teamwork culture \u00b7 World renowned academic environment for teaching medical students, residents, and fellows \u00b7 Advanced endoscopy fellowship program \u00b7 Patient-centric mindset to provide the highest quality service and patient care Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) Program qualified employer Community Highlights: \u00b7 High quality of life and one of the lowest costs of living in the country Home of the NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series and the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo \u00b7 One of the top 10 states in the US for Pre-K to 12th grade education Thriving arts and entertainment scene Our compensation package is extremely competitive and includes comprehensive benefits, generous employer paid retirement contributions, CME , and paid time off . The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree), who is board certified/eligible in gastroenterology with procedural skills in EUS / ERCP and a dedication to delivering high quality care. Fellowship training advanced endoscopy GI is preferred. Apply online \u2013 https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95579 . Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent Board certified in internal medicine. Board certified/eligible in gastroenterology or hepatology Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified in internal medicine? Yes No * Are you board certified/eligible in gastroenterology or hepatology? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95638": {"title": "Gastroenterologist Medical Director PIBDC/Academic/DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Gastroenterologist Medical Director PIBDC/Academic/DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Gastroenterologist Medical Director PIBDC/Academic/DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 022 Department Int Med GI 50001304 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Gastroenterologist Medical Director PIBDC/Academic/DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Gastroenterologist Medical Director PIBDC/Academic/DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/15/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary IBD Center Medical Director The Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, NE is recruiting a Medical Director for the multidisciplinary Frederick F. Paustian Inflammatory Bowel Disease Center ( PIBDC ). The Medical Director will serve as a visionary leader to build and grow a premier IBD Center at a highly ranked academic medical center. The selected candidate will play an integral role in the future growth of the Division. The PIBDC is a newly created 3800 square feet center that opened in 2022. It is dedicated to improving the lives of IBD patients through expert, integrated, innovative patient-centered care as well as through ground-breaking clinical, translational, and basic research programs. Opportunity Highlights: \u00b7 Beautiful, turnkey clinic with dedicated, support staff \u00b7 Funding for basic and clinical faculty research \u00b7 Collaborative group of clinicians, clinical trialists, and translational and basic scientists \u00b7 Comprehensive multidisciplinary team \u00b7 Seven exam rooms \u2013 one specifically equipped for colorectal surgery outpatient procedures \u00b7 Prospective biobank with a sample-linked clinical database Community Highlights: Live in a Top-Rated City! Omaha, Nebraska is No. 14 Most Affordable Places to Live in the U.S. by U.S. News & World Report U.S. News & World Report ranks Omaha among the Best Places to Live in the U.S. Recognized among the Best Places to Raise Kids by Smartasset.com Ranks as one of the Best Cities for Runners by Smartasset.com Smartasset.com ranks Omaha as the No. 16 Most Livable City in the U.S No. 5 Best City for Young Professionals according to finance.yahoo.com Our compensation package is extremely competitive and includes comprehensive benefits, generous employer paid retirement contributions, CME , and paid time off . The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO, MD/PhD (or equivalent degree), who is board certified/eligible in Gastroenterology and has a record of accomplishment in gastroenterology. We are looking for a leader with experience and dedication to excellence in patient care, teaching and research. We invite candidates without experience, but who have interest suitable for working towards becoming the Medical Director to apply. For immediate and confidential consideration, apply online at https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95577 . Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent Board certified in internal medicine. Board certified/eligible in gastroenterology Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95636": {"title": "Part-time Outpatient Gastroenterologist/Endoscopy Only", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Part-time Outpatient Gastroenterologist/Endoscopy Only Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Part-time Outpatient Gastroenterologist/Endoscopy Only Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 021 Department Int Med GI 50001304 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 60 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Part-time Outpatient Gastroenterologist/Endoscopy Only Job Title/Academic Rank Part-time Outpatient Gastroenterologist/Endoscopy Only Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type L1 - REG SPECIAL FAC/S Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/15/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Part-Time Outpatient Gastroenterologist \u2013 Endoscopy Only The Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, NE is actively recruiting an academic gastroenterologist to join our dynamic team. In this unique outpatient position, you will perform outpatient-based procedures at any of our Nebraska Medicine Endoscopy locations. We are committed to providing the highest quality health care to patients. Our hospital partner, Nebraska Medicine, has been rated by U.S. News & World Report as a High Performing Hospital in Gastroenterology for 11 consecutive years. Opportunity Highlights: \u00b7 Outpatient focus \u2013 performing endoscopy procedures only \u00b7 Potential to perform procedures at various state of the art endoscopy sites \u00b7 No clinic or inpatient consult service responsibilities \u00b7 Highly established primary care referral network \u00b7 Patient-centric mindset to provide the highest quality service and patient care Community Highlights: \u00b7 Omaha, Nebraska is rated by Forbes magazine as one of the top five best cities to raise a family High quality of life and cost of living below the national average Thriving arts and entertainment scene Home of the NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series and the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo Our compensation package is extremely competitive and includes comprehensive benefits, generous employer paid retirement contributions, CME , and paid time off . The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree), who is board certified/eligible in gastroenterology. Questions may be addressed to: Contact Fedja Rochling, MD \u2013 frochling@unmc.edu 402-559-6209 Interested candidates may apply online with CV and letter of interest at -https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95576. Required Qualifications MD, DO, or MBBS (or equivalent degree), who is board certified/eligible in gastroenterology. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Keyboarding is required. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95633": {"title": "Pulmonary, Critical Care/Lung TX/Academic Rank/DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Pulmonary, Critical Care/Lung TX/Academic Rank/DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Pulmonary, Critical Care/Lung TX/Academic Rank/DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026 - 031 Department Int Med Pulmonary 50000592 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Pulmonary, Critical Care/Lung TX/Academic Rank/DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Pulmonary, Critical Care/Lung TX/Academic Rank/DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/15/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ), Division of Pulmonary, Critical Care & Sleep is recruiting a pulmonary and critical care medicine specialist with a dedicated interest in lung transplantation. This faculty position offers the unique opportunity to devote 50% of your clinical effort to lung transplant care, working within one of the most comprehensive and collaborative transplant centers in the nation. In this role, you will become part of a highly skilled lung transplant team, providing patients with seamless care\u2014from pre-evaluation and surgery through long-term follow-up. Our clinical partner, Nebraska Medicine, is one of only a handful of institutions nationwide to perform all solid organ transplants under one roof, offering unparalleled resources and multidisciplinary collaboration. Opportunity Highlights \u2022 Dedicated 50% clinical effort in lung transplantation with a balanced schedule \u2022 Strong leadership support with long-term investment in your career growth \u2022 Opportunity to shape patient care, education, research, and innovation in pulmonary medicine for the region \u2022 Fully accredited pulmonary/critical care and sleep medicine fellowships with active teaching opportunities \u2022 Collegial, collaborative environment committed to personal and professional development \u2022 Loan Forgiveness Eligibility: Qualify through the Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program Exceptional Compensation & Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: \u2022 CME allowance \u2022 Competitive retirement contributions and other deferred comp opportunities \u2022 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u2022 A full suite of health and wellness benefits \u2022 Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) qualified employer Living in Omaha Omaha is one of the most affordable cities in the US, with one of the lowest costs of living nationwide. Recognized by Forbes as the #1 Best City to Move to in 2024, Omaha offers a thriving urban setting with a welcoming, family-friendly atmosphere. Residents enjoy: \u2022 Top-rated schools \u2022 A vibrant cultural scene \u2022 Abundant recreational opportunities The successful candidate should be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree), board certified/eligible in pulmonary and critical care medicine, with additional fellowship training in lung transplant pulmonary medicine. We invite experienced pulmonary critical care physicians with genuine interest in lung transplantation to consider this opportunity. Candidates should have an interest in teaching along with passion to help patients and their families deal with serious life-threatening illness Interested in learning more? Contact: Ruxana Sadikot, MD, Chief Pulmonary, Critical Care, Sleep & Allergy Email: rsadikot@unmc.edu To apply online go to https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95622 Required Qualifications MD, MBBS , DO or equivalent. Board certified. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments to be determined by patient care, research and academic activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise Yes Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures to be determined by patient care, research and academic activities. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion to be determined by patient care, research and academic activities. Keyboarding is required for electronic medical recordkeeping. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95467": {"title": "PT Preclinical Teaching Faculty/ Faculty Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | PT Preclinical Teaching Faculty/ Faculty Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application PT Preclinical Teaching Faculty/ Faculty Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Kearney, NE Requisition Number: 2026007 Department Dean College of Medicine 50000511 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: Academic \u2013 TBD Reg-Temp Part-Time Regular Work Schedule Academic TBD Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title PT Preclinical Teaching Faculty/ Faculty Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank PT Preclinical Teaching Faculty/ Faculty Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type L1 - REG SPECIAL FAC/S Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/12/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary Part-Time Preclinical Teaching Faculty UNMC College of Medicine \u2013 Kearney Regional Campus The University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) College of Medicine ( COM ) is seeking a part-time Pre-Clinical Teaching Faculty member to join its Kearney Regional Campus. The College is dedicated to educating and training physicians for practice in Greater Nebraska, with a particular focus on preparing students to meet the health care needs of rural and regional communities. This position offers a meaningful opportunity for a practicing physician to have a direct and lasting impact on medical students early in their training, shaping their clinical reasoning, professional identity, and commitment to patient-centered care in Nebraska. This role is designed for physicians with a strong interest in medical education. The successful candidate will contribute to small-group, active-learning experiences within the Phase 1 (preclinical) curriculum, with a particular emphasis on early clinical reasoning and professional skill development. The faculty member will hold an academic appointment within the College of Medicine department that aligns with their specialty. Responsibilities include: Facilitate small-group learning sessions in Phase 1 curricular components, including: Problem-Based Learning ( PBL ) Communication Skills Physical Diagnosis Evidence-Based Medicine Commit approximately one half-day per week during the academic year for scheduled teaching activities. Participate in required preparatory sessions and faculty development activities to ensure alignment with curricular goals and instructional methods. Engage in assessment and feedback activities related to assigned teaching responsibilities. Serve, as requested, on relevant College of Medicine committees consistent with the part-time nature of the appointment. Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95372 . Required Qualifications MD, DO, or equivalent degree with eligibility for faculty appointment at UNMC . Experience in clinical practice (current or past) and demonstrated interest in undergraduate medical education. Experience with, or willingness to learn, small-group facilitation and active-learning instructional methods. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Not Applicable Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation NA Repetitive Motion NA Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95466": {"title": "Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2026005 Department CON-Omaha Division 50000658 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Nursing FTE: 1.0 FTE Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F 8-5 Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Assistant Professor Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/12/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Family Nurse Practitioner ( FNP ) Track Professor provides academic leadership and instruction supporting preparation of advanced practice nurses for primary care across the lifespan. The role teaches and mentors students in diagnostic reasoning, comprehensive assessment, health promotion, disease prevention, and management of common acute and stable chronic conditions in ambulatory/family practice settings, while ensuring quality, compliance, and strong clinical partnership alignment. . Required Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing minimum; doctorate in nursing preferred. Licensed or eligible for licensure in Nebraska. Supplemental Qualifications Current teaching experience and experience in clinical environment preferred. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Not Applicable Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Not Applicable Sitting Not Applicable Standing Occasionally Squatting Not Applicable Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Clinical Settings Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation N/A Repetitive Motion N/A Grasping N/A If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Resume Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master's degree, or equivalent, in the field identified in this posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95284": {"title": "Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 301 Department Pathology, Microbiology & Immunology 50000521 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Faculty Position in Anatomic Pathology/Rank DOQ Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/05/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Pathology and Microbiology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) invites applications for a full-time, tenure-leading faculty position in the division of Anatomic Pathology with a focus on Dermatopathology. The successful candidate should possess strong diagnostic skills in dermatopathology and will have the opportunity to participate in another subspecialty such as bone and soft tissue pathology. Educational opportunities include teaching within the medical school and within an ACGME -accredited AP/CP residency program. Opportunities for developing research projects are available. Candidates interested in developing a funded research program are also encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will hold an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. (or equivalent) degree, and they should be certified or eligible for certification in AP or AP/CP by the American Board of Pathology. The department is a rapidly growing academic subspeciality-based practice with highly competitive compensation and opportunities for administrative responsibilities. For additional information, please contact Dr. Joseph D. Khoury, Professor and Chair, Department of Pathology and Microbiology by clicking here. Please include in the subject line Dermatopathology Application. Interested candidates should submit a summary of their interests, CV and other documentation online through this link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94520 Nebraska Medicine and UNMC share the same mission: to lead the world in transforming lives to create a healthy future for all individuals and communities through premier educational programs, innovative research and extraordinary patient care. This leading tertiary academic healthcare system is home to over 15,000 employees that include nearly 1,400 affiliated physicians covering primary care and nearly all specialty areas in medicine. The Nebraska Medical Center is the state\u2019s largest hospital and for several consecutive years has been awarded best in state by U.S. News & World Report, listed as one of the 100 greatest hospitals in America by Becker\u2019s Hospital Review and included in Forbes best in state employers. Omaha is the largest city in Nebraska and home to four Fortune 500 companies. This historic city sits along the Missouri River and features a vibrant cultural scene, family friendly neighborhoods, and more than 250 public parks spread across its unique historic districts. In addition to benefiting from major investments in UNMC , Omaha\u2019s strong philanthropic community supports renowned attractions such as the Omaha Henry Doorly Zoo, Lauritzen Gardens, and the Omaha Symphony. Required Qualifications M.D., M.D./Ph.D., Ph.D., or equivalent degree Certified or eligible for certification in AP or AP/CP by the American Board of Pathology Supplemental Qualifications Fellowship training in dermatopathology Experience in medical student, pathology resident and/or fellowship training Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain PPE includes lab coat, gloves and mask plus N95 mask Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Pathology techniques require both sets of hands and wrist to complete. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Visual capacity is essential for medical direction and review of patient cases whether in paper, computer, physical or slide format. Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter C.V. Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95255": {"title": "Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 399 Department Eppley Inst Faculty 50001826 Business Unit(College/Institute) Eppley Institute FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Cancer Researcher Academic Rank/DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/02/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The Eppley Institute at the University of Nebraska Medical Center, in collaboration with the NCI -Designated Fred & Pamela Buffett Cancer Center is conducting a search for tenure-leading faculty members in the broad discipline of cancer research. Assistant Professor candidates will demonstrate a strong upward trajectory, based on publications and/or early-stage cancer-relevant funding. Associate Professor candidates will have a sustained strong track record of cancer-relevant research funding and publications. Professor candidates will additionally have a track record of leadership roles within academic departments and/or NCI -designated cancer centers. Individuals in all areas of cancer research will be considered, with special emphases on: cancer and the environment, epigenetics and chromatin, gene-environment interactions, chemical carcinogenesis, DNA repair and genome stability, cancer signaling, tumor microenvironment and cancer immunology, cancer stem cells, tumor dormancy, tumor recurrence, and drug resistance, obesity and metabolism, metastasis, functional genomics, therapeutic target development, and cancer proteomics. Submit a full-length CV, a 3-page future research plan, and the names and contact for 3-5 references Required Qualifications Ph.D. in cancer related field Supplemental Qualifications Submit a full-length CV, a 3-page future research plan, and the names and contact for 3-5 references. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Lab environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Not Applicable Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals Yes Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Depends on successful candidate and their laboratory research whether certain exposures are going to take place and if they will be working with animals and need PPE . Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation N/A Repetitive Motion N/A Grasping N/A If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Other Doc Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95254": {"title": "Maxillofacial Prosthodontist / Faculty Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Maxillofacial Prosthodontist / Faculty Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Maxillofacial Prosthodontist / Faculty Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 395 Department Otol-Head and Neck Surgery 50000520 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Varies Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Maxillofacial Prosthodontist / Faculty Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Maxillofacial Prosthodontist / Faculty Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 01/02/2026 Position Qualification Position Summary The University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, Nebraska is actively seeking a Maxillofacial Prosthodontist.The position includes an opportunity for premier educational program teaching, innovative research and extraordinary patient care in a world renowned academic environment. Faculty members enjoy the benefit of new clinical facilities with a robust practice in partnership with otolaryngology subspecialists in neurotology, laryngology, head and neck surgical oncology, facial plastic and reconstructive surgery, rhinology and base of skull surgery, pediatric otolaryngology and allergy. As Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, UNMC is committed to the education of a 21st century health care work force, to finding cures and treatments for devastating diseases, to providing the best care for patients, and to serve Nebraska and its communities through award-winning outreach. We offer a highly competitive benefits package and rank and salary commensurate with qualifications. Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95044 . Required Qualifications MD BC/BE Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Up to 2 hours Crawling Occasionally Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current Yes Noise Yes Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain The candidates for this position would have the chance of encountering the above hazards. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation both Repetitive Motion both Grasping both If you selected any area above, please explain The candidates for this position would be surgeons that will need the use of both hands. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a MD? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95226": {"title": "Radiologist/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Radiologist/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Radiologist/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 390 Department Radiology 50000527 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: TBD Reg-Temp Academic - TBD Work Schedule days, nights, weekends, as needed Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Radiologist/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Radiologist/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/30/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Radiology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha, Nebraska is actively recruiting for a board-certified imaging radiologist to join our team of compassionate, patient-focused faculty. Our growing, research oriented department encompasses approximately 50,000 square feet and utilizes state-of-the-art equipment in diagnostic radiology, angiography, ultrasound, computed tomography, magnetic resonance imaging, and nuclear medicine. The UNMC campus has seen rapid growth in recent years with the construction of several new inpatient and outpatient facilities. In addition to this, planning for a new main campus inpatient facility is also underway. This busy practice is based at our University campus and also supports several satellite locations for our hospital partner, Nebraska Medicine and several other free-standing imaging clinics around the Omaha area. The successful candidate should have outstanding credentials in radiology. The Department of Radiology offers a collegial and supportive working atmosphere, and as Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, UNMC is committed to the education of a 21st century health care work force. By supporting the mission of education, discovery, and leading-edge care, the Academic Health Sciences Center aims to improve the health of people and the communities across Nebraska and around the world. UNMC is nestled in mid-town Omaha with many amenities nearby. A mid-western city with a low cost of living, Omaha has many options for excellent public and private schools, with several universities and additional training programs available in the area. The city has an active food and entertainment life, and Eppley Airfield serves all major airlines with exceptionally easy access. Family activities include numerous parks and recreational facilities, children\u2019s museum, and children\u2019s theater. Numerous golf courses and country clubs also can be found spread throughout the city, and The Henry Doorly Zoo has been named one of the premier zoos in the United States. Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94946 . UNMC is dedicated to creating an environment where everyone feels valued, respected and included. Required Qualifications M.D. Board certified in Radiology Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting 2-5 hours Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Body fluids \u2013 potential due to interaction with patients Moving machinery \u2013 x ray equipment has movement Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Yes Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Manipulation and repetitive motion \u2013 keyboarding and handwriting Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you BC/BE in the area identified in the job posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95180": {"title": "Med Peds Physician (Academic Rank DOQ)", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Med Peds Physician (Academic Rank DOQ) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Med Peds Physician (Academic Rank DOQ) Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 409 Department MMI Clinical Services 50000700 Business Unit(College/Institute) Munroe-Meyer Institute FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule 8:00am - 5:00pm; Hours May Vary Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Med Peds Physician (Academic Rank DOQ) Job Title/Academic Rank Med Peds Physician (Academic Rank DOQ) Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/22/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The Munroe-Meyer Institute for Genetics and Rehabilitation ( MMI ) at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) is accepting applications for a Med Peds Physician at open faculty rank (Rank DOQ ). This position will provide outpatient comprehensive medical care for patients of all age groups including infants, children, teenagers and seniors with autism spectrum disorder, other intellectual and developmental disabilities, as well as neurotypical individuals at Munroe-Meyer Institute for Genetics and Rehabilitation. Work in collaboration with other healthcare professionals to ensure continuity of care and deliver personalized and evidence-based medical services in a collaborative and supportive environment. Promote wellness and educate about the prevention of illness and health promotion and help patients meet their health needs. Practice Responsibilities: Provide high quality, compassionate care that reflects evidence-based guidelines, best practice, ethical considerations, cost and clinical effectiveness and patient/family acceptance and/or satisfaction. Assess the health status of patients of all ages and develop appropriate plans for health supervision and illness management in an outpatient setting by: Obtaining a comprehensive developmental, health and medical history. Performing physical examinations based on age and history. Assessing and diagnosing a variety of illnesses, ranging from the common problems such as injuries and infections, to more complex needs such as diabetes, asthma, high blood pressure and high cholesterol, with referral to specialty care when indicated. Identifying normal versus abnormal growth and developmental patterns. Performing or recommending age-appropriate and condition-specific screening, laboratory tests and diagnostic procedures. Reviewing and interpreting lab results and developing treatment plans based on findings. Analyzing factors that impact growth and development. Provide preventive care, including screenings and immunizations. Provide comprehensive, age/developmentally-appropriate teaching, counseling, and advising patients and their families about growth and development, health status, illnesses, management plans, and health promotion, disease and injury preventing activities and provide anticipatory guidance and identify risk factors based on growth and developmental factors, cultural and belief variables and family systems. Use prescriptive authority, in accordance with state and federal laws and regulations to treat illness, improve health status, and provide preventive care, by: Prescribing medications based on a patient\u2019s clinical history, current assessment data and health care needs. Prescribing medications based on current research and a thorough knowledge base in pharmacotherapeutics. Providing patient education regarding intended effects, specific instructions, side effects, and possible interactions of medications and/or treatments, cost, and alternative treatments or procedures. Monitor therapeutic and potential adverse effects of medications. Formulate a holistic, culturally sensitive, patient/family-centered plan of care recognizing the patient and family are active participants. Collaborate with internal and external healthcare partners to coordinate patient care to ensure high quality care. Provide med peds specialist consultation to other health care providers. Utilize any other appropriate intervention(s) within the scope of practice parameters, expertise and knowledge of the Med Peds Physician. Take call on weekdays, weekends and holidays in rotation with the other providers in the practice. Document patient interactions in patient\u2019s medical record and maintain accurate and timely records in compliance with healthcare regulations and practice standards. Submit accurate and timely billing. Maintain productivity standards according to program requirements. Protect confidentiality of patient information according to HIPAA standards. Participate in continuing education and professional development to stay current on medical advancements, treatments, and technologies. Engage in education, research or other scholarly activity as a member of an academic medical center. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong diagnostic and clinical skills. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Empathy and a family-centered approach to care. Willingness to work collaboratively in a team-based environment. About MMI : MMI is one of the oldest, largest, and most comprehensive intellectual and developmental disability centers in the world. MMI\u2019s mission is \u201cto be world leaders in transforming the lives of all individuals with disabilities and complex health care needs, their families and the community through outreach, engagement, premier educational programs, innovative research and extraordinary patient care\u201d. MMI utilizes an interdisciplinary team approach that assures a comprehensive integration of our four pillars: research, clinical services, education, and community engagement. MMI is one of eight academic units of UNMC . MMI has an annual budget of more than $40M, approximately 500 employees, and our 17 disciplines provide over 90,000 clinical services each year serving individuals with disabilities and complex medical needs across the lifespan. MMI is a federally designated University Center for Excellence in Developmental Disabilities ( UCEDD ) and has a Leadership Education in Neurodevelopmental and Related Disabilities ( LEND ) program. MMI provides limitless opportunities for clinical programming, innovative research, and community engagement. About Omaha: Omaha, Nebraska, is a dynamic and welcoming city that offers an exceptional quality of life. Known for its affordability, short commutes, and friendly Midwest atmosphere, Omaha also boasts a vibrant arts scene, nationally acclaimed restaurants, and abundant parks and trails. The city is home to the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo and Aquarium and hosts the annual NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series, both of which draw visitors from across the country. With several Fortune 500 companies, a growing innovation economy, and a strong sense of community, Omaha provides the perfect balance of professional opportunity and small-town charm\u2014making it an ideal place to live and work. Additional Information: MMI provides convenient on-site parking and access to an employee fitness center. To learn more about this opportunity, contact Amy Nordness, PhD, MMI Associate Dean and Director of MMI , at: asnordness@unmc.edu. Review of applicants will occur on a rolling basis as recruitment is ongoing. Rank will depend on qualifications. Applicants should upload with their application a letter of interest and curriculum vitae. University of Nebraska Employee Information: Faculty and Staff Benefits Required Qualifications Medical degree (MD or DO) from an accredited medical school. Completion of a Residency in Pediatrics and completion of a Residency in Internal Medicine from an ACGME accredited Institution Board Certified/Board Eligible in Pediatrics by the American Board of Pediatrics and Board Certified/Board Eligible in Internal Medicine by the American Board of Internal Medicin Eligible for state medical license to practice medicine in the state of Nebraska. Current DEA certificate. Current Basic Life Support ( BLS ) or Pediatric Advanced Life Support ( PALS ) and/or Advanced Life Support ( ALS ) certification through the American Heart Association. Supplemental Qualifications Experience in outpatient pediatric and adult medicine. Experience with individuals with intellectual and developmental disabilities. Knowledge of EPIC electronic health record systems. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Occasionally Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Potential exposure to blood, urine, vomit or other bodily fluids typically found in a primary care pediatric office. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a MD/DO? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95179": {"title": "Internal Medicine Physician (Academic Rank DOQ)", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Internal Medicine Physician (Academic Rank DOQ) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Internal Medicine Physician (Academic Rank DOQ) Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 408 Department MMI Clinical Services 50000700 Business Unit(College/Institute) Munroe-Meyer Institute FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule 8:00am - 5:00pm; Hours May Vary Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Internal Medicine Physician (Academic Rank DOQ) Job Title/Academic Rank Internal Medicine Physician (Academic Rank DOQ) Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/22/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The Munroe-Meyer Institute for Genetics and Rehabilitation ( MMI ) at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) is accepting applications for a Internal Medicine Physician at open faculty rank (Rank DOQ ). This position will provide outpatient comprehensive medical care for adults with autism spectrum disorder, other intellectual and developmental disabilities, as well as neurotypical individuals at Munroe-Meyer Institute for Genetics and Rehabilitation. Work in collaboration with other healthcare professionals to ensure continuity of care and deliver personalized and evidence-based medical services in a collaborative and supportive environment. Promote wellness and educate about the prevention of illness and health promotion and help patients meet their health needs. Practice Responsibilities: Provide high quality, compassionate care that reflects evidence-based guidelines, best practice, ethical considerations, cost and clinical effectiveness and patient and family acceptance and/or satisfaction. Assess the health status of adults and develop appropriate plans for health supervision and illness management in an outpatient setting by: Obtaining a comprehensive health and medical history. Performing physical examinations based on age and history. Assessing and diagnosing a variety of illnesses, ranging from the common problems such as injuries and infections, to more complex needs such as diabetes, asthma, high blood pressure and high cholesterol, with referral to specialty care when indicated. Performing or recommending age-appropriate and condition-specific screening, laboratory tests and diagnostic procedures. Reviewing and interpreting lab results and developing treatment plans based on findings. Provide preventive care, including screenings and immunizations. Provide comprehensive, age/developmentally-appropriate teaching, counseling, and advising patients and their families about health status, illnesses, management plans, and health promotion, disease and injury preventing activities and provide anticipatory guidance and identify risk factors based on disability factors, cultural and belief variables and family systems. Use prescriptive authority, in accordance with state and federal laws and regulations to treat illness, improve health status, and provide preventive care, by: Prescribing medications based on a patient\u2019s clinical history, current assessment data and health care needs. Prescribing medications based on current research and a thorough knowledge base in pharmacotherapeutics. Providing patient education regarding intended effects, specific instructions, side effects, and possible interactions of medications and/or treatments, cost, and alternative treatments or procedures. Monitor therapeutic and potential adverse effects of medications. Formulate a holistic, culturally sensitive, patient-centered plan of care recognizing the patient and family are active participants. Collaborate with internal and external healthcare partners to coordinate patient care to ensure high quality care. Provide internal medicine specialist consultation to other health care providers. Utilize any other appropriate intervention(s) within the scope of practice parameters, expertise and knowledge of the Internal Medicine Physician. Take call on weekdays, weekends and holidays in rotation with the other providers in the practice. Document patient interactions in patient\u2019s medical record and maintain accurate and timely records in compliance with healthcare regulations and practice standards. Submit accurate and timely billing. Maintain productivity standards according to program requirements. Protect confidentiality of patient information according to HIPAA standards. Participate in continuing education and professional development to stay current on medical advancements, treatments, and technologies. Engage in education, research or other scholarly activity as a member of an academic medical center. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong diagnostic and clinical skills. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Empathy and a family-centered approach to care. Willingness to work collaboratively in a team-based environment. About MMI : MMI is one of the oldest, largest, and most comprehensive intellectual and developmental disability centers in the world. MMI\u2019s mission is \u201cto be world leaders in transforming the lives of all individuals with disabilities and complex health care needs, their families and the community through outreach, engagement, premier educational programs, innovative research and extraordinary patient care\u201d. MMI utilizes an interdisciplinary team approach that assures a comprehensive integration of our four pillars: research, clinical services, education, and community engagement. MMI is one of eight academic units of UNMC . MMI has an annual budget of more than $40M, approximately 500 employees, and our 17 disciplines provide over 90,000 clinical services each year serving individuals with disabilities and complex medical needs across the lifespan. MMI is a federally designated University Center for Excellence in Developmental Disabilities ( UCEDD ) and has a Leadership Education in Neurodevelopmental and Related Disabilities ( LEND ) program. MMI provides limitless opportunities for clinical programming, innovative research, and community engagement. About Omaha: Omaha, Nebraska, is a dynamic and welcoming city that offers an exceptional quality of life. Known for its affordability, short commutes, and friendly Midwest atmosphere, Omaha also boasts a vibrant arts scene, nationally acclaimed restaurants, and abundant parks and trails. The city is home to the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo and Aquarium and hosts the annual NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series, both of which draw visitors from across the country. With several Fortune 500 companies, a growing innovation economy, and a strong sense of community, Omaha provides the perfect balance of professional opportunity and small-town charm\u2014making it an ideal place to live and work. Additional Information: MMI provides convenient on-site parking and access to an employee fitness center. To learn more about this opportunity, contact Amy Nordness, PhD, MMI Associate Dean and Director of MMI , at: asnordness@unmc.edu. Review of applicants will occur on a rolling basis as recruitment is ongoing. Rank will depend on qualifications. Applicants should upload with their application a letter of interest and curriculum vitae. University of Nebraska Employee Information: Faculty and Staff Benefits Required Qualifications Medical degree (MD or DO) from an accredited medical school. Completion of a Residency in Internal Medicine from an ACGME accredited Institution Board Certified/Board Eligible in Internal Medicine by the American Board of Internal Medicine Eligible for state medical license to practice medicine in the state of Nebraska. Current DEA certificate. Current Basic Life Support ( BLS ) or Advanced Life Support ( ALS ) certification through the American Heart Association. Supplemental Qualifications Experience in outpatient adult medicine. Experience with individuals with intellectual and developmental disabilities. Knowledge of EPIC electronic health record systems. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Occasionally Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Potential exposure to blood, urine, vomit or other bodily fluids typically found in a primary care pediatric office. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a MD/DO? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95094": {"title": "Psychology - Multilingual (Academic/Faculty Rank DOQ)", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Psychology - Multilingual (Academic/Faculty Rank DOQ) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Psychology - Multilingual (Academic/Faculty Rank DOQ) Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 403 Department MMI Psychology 50000698 Business Unit(College/Institute) Munroe-Meyer Institute FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Full time (12 months) Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Psychology - Multilingual (Academic/Faculty Rank DOQ) Job Title/Academic Rank Psychology - Multilingual (Academic/Faculty Rank DOQ) Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The Munroe-Meyer Institute ( MMI ) for Genetics and Rehabilitation at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha is currently accepting applications for a multilingual faculty position in the Department of Psychology (Rank DOQ ). Minimum requirements are a doctoral degree in Clinical or School Psychology. Applicant must have Nebraska licensure (or license eligible) while board certification (particularly BCBA ) is also valued. Candidates with a clinical internship from APA / CPA -accredited programs in psychology are preferred. Clinical activities center on delivery of behavioral health assessment, diagnostic and treatment services for neurotypical individuals (especially children, adolescents and families) as well as individuals with intellectual and developmental disabilities across the lifespan. Referrals come from schools, physicians, and community agencies throughout the region. Faculty may choose to focus their clinical services, training and research in 1) outpatient BH clinics at MMI , 2) integrated primary care sites across the Omaha metro area, or 3) school-based mental health clinics in the surrounding community. All of the above duties require applicants to be multilingual. See UNMC\u2013MMI Psychology website for more information about the program. About MMI Psychology: The department of Psychology at the MMI is a collegial group of clinical educators and researchers dedicated to integrating training and research within clinical service delivery in a highly collaborative, interdisciplinary setting. Department faculty play a vital role in education and training, providing clinical supervision through a large, well-funded internship program within the APA -accredited Nebraska Internship Consortium, as well as a growing postdoctoral fellowship program. While the department is grounded in a behavioral orientation, it welcomes applicants with diverse but complementary theoretical perspectives. Several faculty also teach in the Applied Behavior Analysis master\u2019s degree program, which prepares graduates for licensure as mental health practitioners and certification as Board Certified Behavior Analysts. Faculty are encouraged to pursue clinical research that aligns with the department\u2019s mission, with flexibility in specific areas of focus. About MMI : MMI is one of the oldest, largest, and most comprehensive intellectual and developmental disability centers in the world. MMI\u2019s mission is \u201cto be world leaders in transforming the lives of all individuals with disabilities and complex health care needs, their families and the community through outreach, engagement, premier educational programs, innovative research and extraordinary patient care\u201d. MMI utilizes an interdisciplinary team approach that assures a comprehensive integration of our four pillars: research, clinical services, education, and community engagement. MMI is one of eight academic units of UNMC . MMI has an annual budget of more than $40M, approximately 500 employees, and our 17 disciplines provide over 90,000 clinical services each year serving individuals with disabilities and complex medical needs across the lifespan. MMI is a federally designated University Center for Excellence in Developmental Disabilities ( UCEDD ) and has a Leadership Education in Neurodevelopmental and Related Disabilities ( LEND ) program. MMI provides limitless opportunities for clinical programming, innovative research, and community engagement. About Omaha: Omaha, Nebraska, is a dynamic and welcoming city that offers an exceptional quality of life. Known for its affordability, short commutes, and friendly Midwest atmosphere, Omaha also boasts a vibrant arts scene, nationally acclaimed restaurants, and abundant parks and trails. The city is home to the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo and Aquarium and hosts the annual NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series, both of which draw visitors from across the country. With several Fortune 500 companies, a growing innovation economy, and a strong sense of community, Omaha provides the perfect balance of professional opportunity and small-town charm\u2014making it an ideal place to live and work. Additional Information: MMI provides convenient on-site parking and access to an employee fitness center. To learn more about this opportunity, contact Brandy Clarke, Ph.D., LP, Director, MMI Psychology, at: brandy.clarke@unmc.edu. Review of applicants will occur on a rolling basis as recruitment is ongoing. Rank will depend on qualifications. Applicants should upload with their application a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, and three letters of recommendation with contact information. University of Nebraska Employee Information: Faculty and Staff Benefits Required Qualifications PhD in Clinical or School Psychology. Nebraska licensure (or license eligible). Multilingual Supplemental Qualifications Candidates with a clinical internship from APA / CPA -accredited programs in psychology are preferred. Board certification particularly BCBA is preferred. English and Spanish preferred. Other languages will be considered. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Up to 2 hours Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Over 5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Not Applicable Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation NA Repetitive Motion NA Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD and clinical internship from an APA/CPA-accredited program in psychology with specialty training in Pediatric or clinical child psychology or school psychology? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95093": {"title": "Neuropsychologist - Multilingual (Academic Rank DOQ)", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Neuropsychologist - Multilingual (Academic Rank DOQ) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Neuropsychologist - Multilingual (Academic Rank DOQ) Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 402 Department MMI Psychology 50000698 Business Unit(College/Institute) Munroe-Meyer Institute FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Full time (12 months) Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Neuropsychologist - Multilingual (Academic Rank DOQ) Job Title/Academic Rank Neuropsychologist - Multilingual (Academic Rank DOQ) Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The Munroe-Meyer Institute ( MMI ) for Genetics and Rehabilitation at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha is currently accepting applications for a multilingual faculty position in the Department of Psychology as Neuropsychologist (Academic Rank DOQ ). Minimum requirements are a doctoral degree in Clinical, School, or Counseling Psychology with training and experience in neuropsychological assessment and research. Applicant must have Nebraska licensure (or license eligible) while board certification ( ABPP ) is also valued. Candidates with a clinical internship from APA / CPA -accredited programs in psychology are preferred. This faculty position would be tasked with developing a program around neuropsychological services for children and adults with intellectual and developmental disabilities including: Neuropsychological assessment and diagnostics Clinical training in neuropsychology for predoctoral interns and postdoctoral fellows A program of clinical research. In addition, this position would be tasked with developing a program that uses practice extenders or psychometrists to provide direct testing, reserving the licensed psychologist for diagnostics and interpretation, training, and research. All of the above duties require applicants to be multilingual. Clinical referrals come from schools, physicians, and community agencies throughout the region. Typical presenting concerns include brain tumor and treatment, TBI /concussion, epilepsy and other seizure disorders, and genetic and other developmental disorders. Institute-based coordination of clinical care and interdisciplinary research is provided. See UNMC\u2013MMI Psychology website for more information about the program. About MMI Psychology: The department of Psychology at the MMI is a collegial group of clinical educators and researchers dedicated to integrating training and research within clinical service delivery in a highly collaborative, interdisciplinary setting. Department faculty play a vital role in education and training, providing clinical supervision through a large, well-funded internship program within the APA -accredited Nebraska Internship Consortium, as well as a growing postdoctoral fellowship program. While the department is grounded in a behavioral orientation, it welcomes applicants with diverse but complementary theoretical perspectives. Several faculty also teach in the Applied Behavior Analysis master\u2019s degree program, which prepares graduates for licensure as mental health practitioners and certification as Board Certified Behavior Analysts. Faculty are encouraged to pursue clinical research that aligns with the department\u2019s mission, with flexibility in specific areas of focus. About MMI : MMI is one of the oldest, largest, and most comprehensive intellectual and developmental disability centers in the world. MMI\u2019s mission is \u201cto be world leaders in transforming the lives of all individuals with disabilities and complex health care needs, their families and the community through outreach, engagement, premier educational programs, innovative research and extraordinary patient care\u201d. MMI utilizes an interdisciplinary team approach that assures a comprehensive integration of our four pillars: research, clinical services, education, and community engagement. MMI is one of eight academic units of UNMC . MMI has an annual budget of more than $40M, approximately 500 employees, and our 17 disciplines provide over 90,000 clinical services each year serving individuals with disabilities and complex medical needs across the lifespan. MMI is a federally designated University Center for Excellence in Developmental Disabilities ( UCEDD ) and has a Leadership Education in Neurodevelopmental and Related Disabilities ( LEND ) program. MMI provides limitless opportunities for clinical programming, innovative research, and community engagement. About Omaha: Omaha, Nebraska, is a dynamic and welcoming city that offers an exceptional quality of life. Known for its affordability, short commutes, and friendly Midwest atmosphere, Omaha also boasts a vibrant arts scene, nationally acclaimed restaurants, and abundant parks and trails. The city is home to the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo and Aquarium and hosts the annual NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series, both of which draw visitors from across the country. With several Fortune 500 companies, a growing innovation economy, and a strong sense of community, Omaha provides the perfect balance of professional opportunity and small-town charm\u2014making it an ideal place to live and work. Additional Information: MMI provides convenient on-site parking and access to an employee fitness center. To learn more about this opportunity, contact Brandy Clarke, Ph.D., LP, Director, MMI Psychology, at: brandy.clarke@unmc.edu. Review of applicants will occur on a rolling basis as recruitment is ongoing. Rank will depend on qualifications. Applicants should upload with their application a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, and three letters of recommendation with contact information. University of Nebraska Employee Information: Faculty and Staff Benefits Required Qualifications PhD in Clinical, School or Counseling Psychology. Nebraska licensure (or license eligible). Multilingual Supplemental Qualifications Candidates with a clinical internship from APA / CPA -accredited programs in psychology are preferred. Board certification particularly BCBA is preferred. English and Spanish preferred. Other languages will be considered. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Up to 2 hours Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Over 5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Not Applicable Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation NA Repetitive Motion NA Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD and clinical internship from an APA/CPA-accredited program in psychology with specialty training in Pediatric or clinical child psychology or school psychology? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/95021": {"title": "Vice Chair Radiology Research/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Vice Chair Radiology Research/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Vice Chair Radiology Research/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 377 Department Radiology 50000527 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: TBD Reg-Temp Academic - TBD Work Schedule days, nights, weekends, as needed Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Vice Chair Radiology Research/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Vice Chair Radiology Research/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/18/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) is seeking an accomplished leader to serve as Vice Chair of Research in the Department of Radiology. This is a unique opportunity to shape the future of radiology through innovative research, interdisciplinary collaboration, and strategic leadership. The successful candidate will be responsible for developing a nationally recognized research program, drive translational research initiatives, mentoring faculty and trainees in radiology research, and securing extramural funding to advance imaging science and improve patient outcomes. Join a nationally recognized academic medical center with access to cutting-edge facilities, including collaboration with the Fred and Pamela Buffett Cancer Center\u2014 Nebraska\u2019s only NCI -designated cancer center in the state and one of just 73 nationwide. The ideal candidate will be a fellowship-trained radiologist and appointed to an on-site dual-role faculty position with responsibilities equally divided between radiology research (0.5 FTE ) and sub-specialized clinical practice (0.5 FTE ) . Candidates must demonstrate a proven record of exceptional clinical expertise in their radiology sub-speciality. The department is particularly interested in candidates with expertise in theranostics , who would contribute clinically to a busy nuclear medicine practice, or those with a background in informatics or artificial intelligence , who would practice within a diagnostic radiology sub-specialty. Sub-specialty alignment may be prioritized based on departmental needs. Research Position Highlights \u00b7 Develop a nationally recognized research program in radiology with a focus on innovation and clinical interdisciplinary collaboration. \u00b7 Collaborate with research divisions throughout the UNMC system including NCI designated Fred and Pamela Buffett Cancer Center \u00b7 Manage translational research initiatives that combine basic science discoveries with clinical applications to improve patient care. \u00b7 Secure extramural funding through grants and strategic partnerships. \u00b7 Participate in departmental strategic planning, aligning research goals with the missions of the University of Nebraska Medical Center. \u00b7 Mentor faculty, residents, fellows, and medical students in research methodologies, scholarly productivity, and career development. \u00b7 Design, initiate, and lead investigator-driven imaging trials and develop competitive research proposals. \u00b7 Provide support for clinical trials in radiology and interface between research coordinator and interdisciplinary teams. \u00b7 Lead and further develop an established Tumor Metrics Lab in the Department of Radiology Clinical Position Highlights \u00b7 Sub-specialized focus: All radiology sub-specialties are welcome to apply and must demonstrate a proven record of exceptional clinical expertise \u00b7 The department is especially interested in candidates with expertise in theranostics who can contribute to a busy nuclear medicine practice, as well as those with other diagnostic radiology sub-specialities with a background in informatics or artificial intelligence. An interest in tumor metrics / clinical response evaluation would also be of benefit. \u00b7 Participate in tumor boards for multidisciplinary disease groups \u00b7 Virtually no call: no primary evening/overnight/weekend shifts, only minimal back-up call for rare coverage during connectivity outages or to provide consultations on cases for our highly trained remote teleradiologists \u00b7 Home workstations given to all faculty \u00b7 Flexible, equitable, and transparent scheduling \u2013 can take vacation in half-day blocks, long-term vacation planning within the group, academic time built into the schedule, dedicated preparation times for all tumor boards, etc. \u00b7 Salary and vacation: Highly competitive total compensation package including salary and time off when compared to Midwest private practices \u00b7 Generous CME budget Environment & Technology \u00b7 The department values clinical excellence and high-level resident education but not at the expense of physician staff burn-out or the requirement for burdensome call responsibilities \u00b7 Relaxed, collegial environment \u00b7 State-of-the-art imaging equipment across CT, MRI , ultrasound, nuclear medicine, PET /CT, and diagnostic radiology \u00b7 Supportive, progressive department culture focused on professional satisfaction and work-life balance The University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) is committed to creating a learning environment free from discrimination and harassment. UNMC is dedicated to creating an environment where everyone feels valued, respected, and included. Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94927 . Required Qualifications Qualifications \u00b7 M.D. or D.O. degree \u00b7 Board certified or board eligible by the American Board of Radiology \u00b7 Completion of a radiology fellowship \u00b7 Eligibility for medical licensure in Nebraska \u00b7 Strong commitment to clinical excellence and collaborative practice \u00b7 Demonstrated interest and experience in academic radiology research with a proven record of research productivity \u00b7 Prior leadership experience desired with the preferred candidate having a proven track record of mentoring junior faculty, residents, and medical students through various research endeavors including project completion, paper writing, and grant applications Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting 2-5 hours Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Body fluids \u2013 potential due to interaction with patients Moving machinery \u2013 x ray equipment has movement Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Yes Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Manipulation and repetitive motion \u2013 keyboarding and handwriting Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you BC/BE in the area identified in the job posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94967": {"title": "Facial Plastics Surgeon / Faculty Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Facial Plastics Surgeon / Faculty Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Facial Plastics Surgeon / Faculty Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 366 Department Otol-Head and Neck Surgery 50000520 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Varies Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Facial Plastics Surgeon / Faculty Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Facial Plastics Surgeon / Faculty Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/17/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) Department of Otolaryngology\u2013Head & Neck Surgery is seeking a full-time faculty member at any academic rank to join our growing division. The successful candidate will provide comprehensive care in facial plastic and reconstructive surgery, including both functional and cosmetic procedures, facial trauma, head and neck reconstruction, and general otolaryngology\u2013head and neck surgery. Our department is deeply committed to excellence in patient care, medical education, research, and community service. Position Requirements Degree: M.D., M.D./Ph.D., or equivalent Training: Completion of an ACGME -accredited Residency in Otolaryngology \u2013 Head & Neck Surgery and Fellowship in Facial Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery Certification: Board certified or board eligible by the American Board of Otolaryngology \u2013 Head and Neck Surgery (or equivalent) Licensure: Eligible for medical licensure in the State of Nebraska prior to start date Clinical Responsibilities The successful candidate will provide medical and surgical care for cosmetic and reconstructive conditions of the face, including but not limited to: Rhinoplasty Facelift and Neck Lift Brow Lift Blepharoplasty Otoplasty Facial reconstruction following Mohs surgery Development of programs in facial nerve reanimation and gender-affirming surgery is strongly encouraged. Demonstrated excellence in clinical practice, program development, quality improvement, and innovation in care delivery is required. Teaching & Academic Responsibilities Educate and mentor medical students, residents, and fellows Participate in didactic and formal lecture activities Contribute to the academic and research missions of the department Academic rank and compensation (including a generous package of fringe benefits) will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested candidates should apply at the following link: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94828 Required Qualifications MD BC/BE Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Up to 2 hours Crawling Occasionally Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Up to 2 hours Reaching Up to 2 hours Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current Yes Noise Yes Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain The candidates for this position would be medical doctors that have the chance of encountering the above hazards. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation both Repetitive Motion both Grasping both If you selected any area above, please explain The candidates for this position would be surgeons that will need the use of both hands. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a MD? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94947": {"title": "Neurotologist / Faculty Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Neurotologist / Faculty Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Neurotologist / Faculty Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 364 Department Otol-Head and Neck Surgery 50000520 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Varies Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Neurotologist / Faculty Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Neurotologist / Faculty Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/17/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary Neurotology Faculty Opportunity in the Upper Midwest The Department of Otolaryngology \u2013 Head and Neck Surgery at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, Nebraska is growing and actively seeking a Neurotologist to join our faculty. This opportunity includes: \u2022 Established Department with 15 physicians \u2022 Partnership with subspecialists in laryngology, head and neck surgical oncology, facial plastic and reconstructive surgery, rhinology and base of skull surgery, pediatric otolaryngology and allergy \u2022 New, state of the art clinical facilities with the latest technology A strong commitment to patient care, medical student, resident, and fellow education, as well as clinical research is required. This individual will be a part of an established neurotology practice and be an integral member of the multidisciplinary team in a world renowned academic environment. In addition, the position affords excellent opportunities for programmatic builds, leadership development, and community outreach. The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified/eligible in Otolaryngology and has completed fellowship training in Otology/Neurotology. As Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, UNMC is committed to the education of a 21st century health care work force, to finding cures and treatments for devastating diseases, to providing the best care for patients, and to serve Nebraska and its communities through award-winning outreach. We offer a highly competitive benefits package and rank and salary commensurate with qualifications. Candidates interested in working within a dynamic and stimulating setting are encouraged to apply with CV and letter of interest. https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94822 Required Qualifications MD BC/BE Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Up to 2 hours Crawling Occasionally Driving Occasionally Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current Yes Noise Yes Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain The candidates for this position would be medical doctors that have the chance of encountering the above hazards. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation both Repetitive Motion both Grasping both If you selected any area above, please explain The candidates for this position would be surgeons that will need the use of both hands. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94931": {"title": "Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 357 Department Biochem and Molecular Biology 50000510 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/17/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology invites applications for an Assistant/Associate/Full Professor. Qualifications include a Ph.D. and/or M.D. degree in a scientific field and relevant experience. Preference will be given to outstanding candidates who can utilize state-of-the-art biochemical, molecular, and array approaches to understanding mechanisms during physiological and pathological conditions, including cancer. The successful applicant will be expected to have an independent research program and contribute to the department\u2019s teaching programs. Applications are being accepted online at https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94710 . Required Qualifications Ph.D. and/ or M.D. in scientific field Supplemental Qualifications Experience in biochemistry and molecular biology scientific field Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Animal facility Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Not Applicable Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Lab work done by Fac member Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation both Repetitive Motion both Grasping both If you selected any area above, please explain general lab benchwork Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an MD or MD/PhD degree in the field identified in the posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 4