logy. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment sterile operating environment \u2013 this person will perform surgery on humans PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current Yes Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain this person is expected to perform surgery on humans Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain this person is expected to perform surgery on humans Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * Are you BC/BE in the area identified in the job posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94798": {"title": "Urogynecology Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Urogynecology Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Urogynecology Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 334 Department Obstetrics/Gynecology 50000515 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Variable -- includes nights and weekends and holidays Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Urogynecology Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Urogynecology Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Additional Requisition Title 2nd Urogyn Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary UROGYNECOLOGIST The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) is seeking a fellowship-trained Urogynecologist to join our faculty. This role offers the best of both worlds\u2014professional growth in a respected academic medical center and the chance to enjoy a balanced lifestyle in one of the most affordable, family-friendly cities in the country. At UNMC , you will be part of a supportive and collegial team within the Olson Center for Women\u2019s Health, where providers work together to deliver personalized, integrated care. With access to new technology and a strong referral base, you will have the tools and support to build a rewarding practice while also shaping the next generation of physicians. Opportunity Highlights Join a collaborative group of 20 OB- GYN faculty with subspecialists in Urogynecology, Maternal-Fetal Medicine, Gynecologic Oncology, and General OB- GYN Practice with brand-new, state-of-the-art urodynamics equipment Enjoy a schedule that balances clinical work with opportunities for teaching and mentorship Participate in research as much\u2014or as little\u2014as you choose, with abundant institutional support Exceptional Compensation & Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: \u00b7 CME allowance \u00b7 Competitive retirement contributions and other deferred comp opportunities \u00b7 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u00b7 A full suite of health and wellness benefits \u00b7 Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) eligible employer Living in Omaha Omaha is one of the most affordable cities in the US, with one of the lowest costs of living nationwide. Recognized by Forbes as the #1 Best City to Move to in 2024, Omaha offers a thriving urban setting with a welcoming, family-friendly atmosphere. Residents enjoy: \u00b7 Top-rated schools \u00b7 A vibrant cultural scene \u00b7 Abundant recreational opportunities The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) whois board certified/eligible in obstetrics and gynecology with additional fellowship training in female pelvic medicine & reconstructive surgery. Apply online \u2013 https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94620 Required Qualifications MD or equivalent Board-certified in Obstetrics and Gynecology. Board certified or board-eligible in GYN Oncology. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment sterile operating environment \u2013 this person will perform surgery on humans PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current Yes Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain this person is expected to perform surgery on humans Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain this person is expected to perform surgery on humans Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * Are you BC/BE in the area identified in the job posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94797": {"title": "MFM - Academic Rank/DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | MFM - Academic Rank/DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application MFM - Academic Rank/DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 331 Department Obstetrics/Gynecology 50000515 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Variable -- includes nights and weekends and holidays Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title MFM - Academic Rank/DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank MFM - Academic Rank/DOQ Additional Requisition Title tba Berg Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, NE is actively recruiting a Maternal-Fetal Medicine physician to join a division of seven providers. This is a wonderful opportunity for a self-motivated physician to join a well-respected and successful academic practice with an enthusiastic approach to providing a high level of quality care in women\u2019s health. In this faculty role, you will work as part of a multi-disciplinary team to provide diagnostic, consultative and continuing care to high-risk obstetrics patients in the Olson Center for Women\u2019s Health. The Olson Center provides multidisciplinary care to pregnant patients, to include ultrasound, genetics and medical management in pregnancy. The practice has collaborative care with specialists in Cardiology, Endocrinology and Pulmonary medicine. This is an opportunity to serve a diverse patient population and deliver focused care in order to help patients achieve their goals. Opportunity highlights: \u00b7 Join a group of twenty five obstetrician-gynecologists including Urogynecology, MFM , Gynecologic Oncology and general OB-Gyn \u00b7 State of the art ultrasound equipment \u00b7 Teaching opportunities with residents and medical students \u00b7 Abundant clinical research and basic science collaborations (if desired) Omaha is a vibrant, attractive city with more than 925,000 people living within the metropolitan area. All the amenities of a much larger metropolitan area are found in Omaha along with a blend of Midwestern hospitality. Yet, the cost of living is 19 percent less than the national average. Forbes magazine recently rated Omaha as one of the top five best cities to raise a family. Specific questions may be directed to: Sarosh Rana, MD, Chairperson rgblum@unmc.edu Required Qualifications MD or equivalent Board-certified in Obstetrics and Gynecology. Board certified or board-eligible in GYN Oncology. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment sterile operating environment \u2013 this person will perform surgery on humans PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current Yes Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain this person is expected to perform surgery on humans Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain this person is expected to perform surgery on humans Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * Are you BC/BE in the area identified in the job posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94796": {"title": "Gyn Oncology Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Gyn Oncology Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Gyn Oncology Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 328 Department Obstetrics/Gynecology 50000515 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Variable -- includes nights and weekends and holidays Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Gyn Oncology Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Gyn Oncology Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Additional Requisition Title 5th Gyn Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary Candidates sought for: Gynecologic Oncology Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology University of Nebraska Medical Center The successful candidate will join a group of twenty five obstetrician-gynecologists in a busy academic practice which includes Urogyn, MFM , Gyn Onc, and General OBG . Responsibilities include provision of clinical care as part of a multi-disciplinary team at Nebraska Medicine, and participating in resident and medical student education. Clinical research and basic science collaborations are available. UNMC /Nebraska Medicine is the most esteemed academic medical center in the region offering exceptional patient care combined with innovative research and education. Committed to advancing quality health care, Nebraska Medicine represents the clinical integration of The Nebraska Medical Center, the state\u2019s largest and highest rated hospital, Bellevue Medical Center, and UNMC Physicians, the area\u2019s largest physician group practice. Omaha, Nebraska is the 42nd largest city in America. Home to the NCAA College World Series and the nation\u2019s highest-rated zoo. Omaha is an affordable, family-friendly city with excellent schools and low crime rates. In addition, it is a regional destination for arts, entertainment, manufacturing and services. Required Qualifications MD or equivalent Board-certified in Obstetrics and Gynecology. Board certified or board-eligible in GYN Oncology. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment sterile operating environment \u2013 this person will perform surgery on humans PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current Yes Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain this person is expected to perform surgery on humans Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain this person is expected to perform surgery on humans Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * Are you BC/BE in the area identified in the job posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94795": {"title": "General Ob/Gyn Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | General Ob/Gyn Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application General Ob/Gyn Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 327 Department Obstetrics/Gynecology 50000515 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Variable -- includes nights and weekends and holidays Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title General Ob/Gyn Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank General Ob/Gyn Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Additional Requisition Title 14th generalist Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center is recruiting dynamic physicians for an OB/Gyn generalist faculty position. The selected candidate would join a group of thirteen OB/Gyn generalists in a full spectrum obstetric and gynecologic practice in an academic environment. Together, our faculty have many years of experience delivering quality and compassionate care to women of all ages. Highlights of this opportunity include: \u2022Collaborative, collegial environment with opportunities for personal and professional development \u2022Competitive benefits package and rank and salary commensurate with qualifications \u2022Level IIIC state-of-the-art NICU \u2022New LDR and post-partum unit \u2022Flexible schedules customized to accommodate your needs The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified/eligible in Obstetrics & Gynecology. Candidates should have outstanding interpersonal skills along with enthusiasm for patient care, medical student and resident education. As Nebraska\u2019s only public academic health sciences center, UNMC is committed to the education of a 21st century health care work force, to finding cures and treatments for devastating diseases, to providing the best care for patients, and to serving our state and its communities through award-winning outreach Required Qualifications MD or equivalent Board-certified in Obstetrics and Gynecology. Board certified or board-eligible in GYN Oncology. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment sterile operating environment \u2013 this person will perform surgery on humans PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current Yes Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain this person is expected to perform surgery on humans Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain this person is expected to perform surgery on humans Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * Are you BC/BE in the area identified in the job posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94794": {"title": "General Ob/Gyn Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | General Ob/Gyn Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application General Ob/Gyn Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 326 Department Obstetrics/Gynecology 50000515 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Variable -- includes nights and weekends and holidays Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title General Ob/Gyn Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank General Ob/Gyn Physician Faculty - Academic Rank/DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary FORMER RAF 2024-094 approved March 2025. The successful candidate will join a group of twenty obstetrician-gynecologists in a busy academic practice which includes Urogyn, MFM , Gyn Onc, and General OBG . Responsibilities include provision of clinical care as part of a multi-disciplinary team at Nebraska Medicine, and participating in resident and medical student education. Clinical research and basic science collaborations are available. UNMC /Nebraska Medicine is the most esteemed academic medical center in the region offering exceptional patient care combined with innovative research and education. Committed to advancing quality health care, Nebraska Medicine represents the clinical integration of The Nebraska Medical Center, the state\u2019s largest and highest rated hospital, Bellevue Medical Center, and UNMC Physicians, the area\u2019s largest physician group practice. Required Qualifications MD or equivalent Board-certified or board-eligible in Obstetrics and Gynecology. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment sterile operating environment \u2013 this person will perform surgery on humans PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current Yes Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain this person is expected to perform surgery on humans Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain this person is expected to perform surgery on humans Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * Are you BC/BE in the area identified in the job posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94787": {"title": "Addiction Medicine Physician/Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Addiction Medicine Physician/Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Addiction Medicine Physician/Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 347 Department Psychiatry 50000526 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F with occasional weekend coverage Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Addiction Medicine Physician/Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Addiction Medicine Physician/Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The Department of Psychiatry at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha, NE, is recruiting an Addiction Medicine Physician to join our Addiction Division faculty. This position offers a unique blend of clinical care, teaching, and academic involvement. You will provide patient care in a busy addiction treatment clinic where addiction medicine physicians and addiction psychiatrists collaborate, while also teaching fellows, psychiatry residents, family medicine residents, and third-year medical students. Our growing Addiction Division includes: -Outpatient addiction psychiatrist -Psychiatrist board-certified in addiction medicine leading the Addiction Psychiatry Consult Liaison Service -Emergency medicine physician and pediatrician, both board-certified in addiction medicine -Child and adolescent psychiatrist who is board-certified in addiction medicine Opportunity Highlights -Teach with national leaders in addiction medicine education and research -Multidisciplinary team of mental health professionals and nurses in collegial environment -Enjoy a flexible schedule that supports work-life harmony -Potential to develop innovative programs in integrated collaborative care -Pursue research and career growth opportunities, including potential leadership as Fellowship Program Director -Contribute to our ACGME -accredited Addiction Medicine Fellowship, now recruiting for its 6th year Exceptional Compensation & Benefits Physicians enjoy a highly competitive package, inclusive of variable compensation plan. Additional benefits include: - CME allowance -Competitive retirement contributions and other deferred comp opportunities -Comprehensive malpractice coverage -A full suite of health and wellness benefits -Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) Program qualified employer Living in Omaha Omaha is one of the most affordable cities in the US, with one of the lowest costs of living nationwide. Recognized by Forbes as the #1 Best City to Move to in 2024. Omaha offers a thriving urban setting with awelcoming, family-friendly atmosphere. Residents enjoy: -Top rated schools -A vibrant cultural scene -Abundant recreational opportunities The ideal candidate must be MD/DO (or equivalent degree) and is board certified/board eligible in addiction medicine. Contact Dr. Howard Liu, Psychiatry Department Chair at hyliu@unmc.edu with questions. Apply at: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94663 Required Qualifications M.D. Board eligible or board certified in addiction medicine Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Not Applicable Sitting Over 5 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Not Applicable Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain This physician would work with outpatient and inpatient patients. Physician may be exposed to bodily fluids or medications in both of these settings. This physician would operate a computer. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain This physician would be writing, using the computer, and other equipment necessary for patient care. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94725": {"title": "Pediatric Faculty - Academic Rank Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Pediatric Faculty - Academic Rank Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Pediatric Faculty - Academic Rank Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 343 Department COD-Growth and Development 50000753 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Dentistry FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Pediatric Faculty - Academic Rank Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Pediatric Dentistry/Faculty Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The University of Nebraska Medical Center College of Dentistry is seeking a full-time, tenure leading faculty member in the Department of Growth and Development, Pediatric Dentistry. This position involves didactic, preclinical, and clinical teaching at both predoctoral and postdoctoral levels across multiple sites, including Children\u2019s Hospital (Omaha), the College of Dentistry (Lincoln), and select extramural rotations. The ideal candidate will hold a DDS / DMD degree, have completed a CODA -accredited pediatric dentistry program, be eligible for Nebraska licensure, and demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching, research, and patient care. Required Qualifications Qualified candidates must have a DDS / DMD degree or an equivalent degree from an international program, must have completed a CODA -accredited pediatric dentistry program, be eligible for Nebraska licensure, and demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching, research, and patient care. Supplemental Qualifications Experience in clinical or didactic education is preferred but not required. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Not Applicable Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Not Applicable Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise Yes Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain exposures in conjunction with dental treatment Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation both Repetitive Motion both Grasping both If you selected any area above, please explain in conjunction with dental treatment Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Other Doc Cover Letter Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a DDS/DMD or foreign equivalent degree? Yes No * Will you have a Residency certificate in Pediatric Dentistry from an ADA accredited specialty training program by the date indicated in the position summary? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94724": {"title": "Acute Care Surgeon - Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Acute Care Surgeon - Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Acute Care Surgeon - Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 349 Department Surgery-Acute Care Surgery 50003925 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F 8-5; some night call and weekends; varies Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Acute Care Surgeon - Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Acute Care Surgeon - Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary Acute Care Surgeon Opportunity The Division of Acute Care Surgery ( ACS ) at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha is seeking a dedicated Acute Care Surgeon to join our collaborative and supportive team of 20 surgeons and a robust group of APPs. This is an excellent opportunity to be part of a collegial team committed to delivering high-quality, compassionate care in a dynamic and high-volume environment. Our hospital partner, Nebraska Medicine, is an American College of Surgeons-designated Level I Trauma Center and a Level II Pediatric Trauma Center, managing: - 3,100+ trauma-related admissions annually - 2,100+ emergency general surgery cases per year Opportunity Highlights : \u00b7 Broad scope of practice, including elective general surgery, emergency general surgery, trauma, and surgical critical care , managing high-acuity patients \u00b7 Join a fast-paced, high-volume, and high-performing surgical team \u00b7 Train and mentor future surgeons in our ACGME -accredited Surgical Critical Care Fellowship \u00b7 Access to Da Vinci Robotic Surgical Systems with dedicated robot block time \u00b7 Opportunities to engage in clinical research and education programs \u00b7 Mentor and train residents, fellows, and medical students \u00b7 Loan Forgiveness \u2013 UNMC is a qualified employer under the Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) Program Why Omaha? Ranked among Forbes\u2019 Top 20 Best Cities to Live in the USA , Omaha offers: \u00b7 Affordable living with a high quality of life \u00b7 A thriving arts, entertainment, and dining scene \u00b7 Exciting attractions, including the NCAA Men\u2019s College Baseball World Series and the world-famous Henry Doorly Zoo Compensation & Benefits: \u00b7 Highly competitive compensation package \u00b7 Comprehensive benefits and employer-paid retirement contributions \u00b7 Generous CME allowance and paid time off \u00b7 A supportive environment for personal and professional growth The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified or board eligible in Surgical Critical Care, have completed a fellowship in Surgical Critical Care and demonstrate a strong interest in teaching residents and medical students. Apply Today: https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94693 Required Qualifications The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified or board eligible in Surgical Critical Care, have completed a fellowship in Surgical Critical Care and demonstrate a strong interest in teaching residents and medical students. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current Yes Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals Yes Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Atmospheric: biohazards, radiation (x-rays), exposure to patients and research materials Blood/body fluids: during patient exams and procedures Chemical hazards: lab chemicals Working on or around machinery: Medical/lab equipment Electrical current: Medical/lab equipment Work with lab animals: Research animals (mice/pigs/rabbits) Operating hand/power tools: laparoscopic tools, other medical/lab equipment Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Operation of surgical tools and medical equipment during surgical procedures Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94690": {"title": "Urogynecologist/Assistant Professor", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Urogynecologist/Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Urogynecologist/Assistant Professor Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 339 Department Surgery-Urologic Surgery 50003934 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule M-F 8-5; some night call and weekends; varies Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Urogynecologist/Assistant Professor Job Title/Academic Rank Urogynecologist/Assistant Professor Additional Requisition Title Urogynecologist/Assistant Professor Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The Division of Urology at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, NE is actively recruiting a urologist that specializes in Female Pelvic Medicine to join us. This is a wonderful opportunity for a self-motivated physician to join a well-respected and successful academic practice with an enthusiastic approach to providing a high level of quality care in women\u2019s health. In this faculty role, you will work alongside a collegial staff of fellow urologists, along with female health care providers to develop a personalized treatment plan for each patient. This position will collaborate with The Olson Center for Women\u2019s Health. The Olson Center offers innovative female pelvic medicine and uses an integrated approach to care to help improve the lives of patients. This is an opportunity to serve a diverse patient population and deliver focused care in order to help patients achieve their goals. The successful candidate must have an MD (or equivalent degree) and be board certified or board eligible in Urology. Interested candidates may use this link to apply with CV and letter of interest \u2013 https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94655 . Required Qualifications The successful candidate must have an MD (or equivalent degree) and be board certified or board eligible in Urology. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment, Lab environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery Yes Electrical current Yes Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals Yes Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Atmospheric: biohazards, radiation (x-rays), exposure to patients and research materials Blood/body fluids: during patient exams and procedures Chemical hazards: lab chemicals Working on or around machinery: Medical/lab equipment Electrical current: Medical/lab equipment Work with lab animals: Research animals (mice/pigs/rabbits) Operating hand/power tools: laparoscopic tools, other medical/lab equipment Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Operation of surgical tools and medical equipment during surgical procedures. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board eligible/board certified in the field specified in this posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94681": {"title": "Infectious Diseases/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Infectious Diseases/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Infectious Diseases/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 323 Department Int Med Infectious Diseases 50000589 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule TBD by supervisor and responsibilities Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Infectious Diseases/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Job Title/Academic Rank Infectious Diseases/Academic Rank/Depends on Qualifications Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/10/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary Infectious Diseases Physician at UNMC The Division of Infectious Diseases at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha is actively recruiting an Infectious Diseases physician to join our faculty. This role offers a unique opportunity to contribute to specialized ID services, including biocontainment, solid organ transplant, oncology, and critical care. Join a robust team of 30 ID physicians, supported by APPs, clinical, and research staff, delivering the full spectrum of infectious disease care at our clinical partner, Nebraska Medicine. Our division is deeply committed to subspecialty ID care, cutting-edge research, and graduate medical education through our ID fellowship program. Highlights: \u2022 Associate Medical Director of the Biocontainment Unit ( BCU ) \u2013 play a key role in one of the nation\u2019s premier biocontainment programs. \u2022 Critical Care ID Call Coverage \u2013 assist in managing infectious disease cases in critical care settings. \u2022 Inpatient ID Coverage \u2013 provide specialized care for solid organ transplant and oncology ID service lines. \u2022 Associate Medical Director of Infection Control \u2013 contribute to infection prevention initiatives. \u2022 Global Health & Research Support \u2013 opportunities to engage in two funded grants through Global Health & the College of Public Health. Why Omaha? Ranked among the Top 20 Best Cities to Live in the USA (Forbes), Omaha offers: \u2022 Affordable Cost of Living \u2013 Enjoy a high quality of life with a low cost of living. \u2022 Thriving Culture & Entertainment \u2013 Experience the Henry Doorly Zoo, a vibrant arts scene, and the NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series. \u2022 Family-Friendly Community \u2013 Benefit from excellent schools, parks, and a welcoming Midwestern atmosphere. Compensation & Benefits: \u2022 Highly competitive package, inclusive of a variable compensation plan. \u2022 Employer-paid retirement contributions and generous CME allowances. \u2022 Comprehensive malpractice coverage \u2022 A full suite of health and wellness benefits The ideal candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is board certified/eligible in Infectious Diseases. Apply Online: | https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94572 . Join us at UNMC and make a lasting impact in infectious diseases. Required Qualifications MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent. Board certified/Board eligible in infectious diseases. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment Full extent of working environments TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Over 5 hours Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Up to 2 hours Standing Up to 2 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric Yes Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards Yes Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity Yes Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Full extent of exposures TBD by patient care, academic and research activities Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation yes - both Repetitive Motion yes - both Grasping yes - both If you selected any area above, please explain Full extent of hand/wrist involvement and repetitive motion TBD by patient care, academic and research activities. Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94666": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 291 Department Neurological Sciences 50001975 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule As directed by supervisor Requisition Category Research - Academic Requisition Title Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Title/Academic Rank Postdoctoral Research Associate Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type A1 - REG OTHER ACAD SAL Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Professional Non-Faculty (Includes Other Academic) Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The WANG Lab at the University of Nebraska Medical Center\u2019s Department of Neurological Sciences is seeking a Postdoctoral Research Associate. The Postdoctoral Research Associate will contribute to developing and/or applying artificial intelligence, machine learning, and image segmentation and/or data science-based methods to address cutting-edge topics, including but not limited to, disease diagnosis/prognosis, biomarkers identification and treatment prediction, etc. Required Qualifications: A PhD by time of hiring in a relevant field. Relevant fields include (but are not limited to) Computer Science, statistics, mathematics, automation, informatics, and Engineering. Experience in deep learning, machine learning and medical imaging processing Programming experience: Python, MATLAB , SPSS , Shell. Experience in working with Linux workstation. Excellent organizational and time-management skills and ability to self-direct work. Ability to work as a team member. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Questions may be directed to Dr. Jieqiong Wang at jiwang@unmc.edu Required Qualifications A PhD by time of hiring in a relevant field. Relevant fields include (but are not limited to) Computer Science, statistics, mathematics, automation, informatics, and Engineering. Experience in deep learning, machine learning and medical imaging processing Programming experience: Python, MATLAB , SPSS , Shell. Experience in working with Linux workstation. Excellent organizational and time-management skills and ability to self-direct work. Ability to work as a team member. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Animal facility Other working environment N/A PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Not Applicable Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Over 5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools Yes If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Working with patients or research participants; working with and prototyping research equipment. Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have, or will you possess in the near future, a Doctoral degree in the area(s) identified in this posting? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94609": {"title": "Psychology (Academic/Faculty Rank DOQ)", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Psychology (Academic/Faculty Rank DOQ) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Psychology (Academic/Faculty Rank DOQ) Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 317 Department MMI Psychology 50000698 Business Unit(College/Institute) Munroe-Meyer Institute FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Full time (12 months) Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Psychology (Academic/Faculty Rank DOQ) Job Title/Academic Rank Psychology (Academic/Faculty Rank DOQ) Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The Munroe-Meyer Institute ( MMI ) for Genetics and Rehabilitation at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha is currently accepting applications for a faculty position in the Department of Psychology (Rank DOQ ). Minimum requirements are a doctoral degree in Clinical or School Psychology. Applicant must have Nebraska licensure (or license eligible) while board certification (particularly BCBA ) is also valued. Candidates with a clinical internship from APA / CPA -accredited programs in psychology are preferred. Clinical activities center on delivery of behavioral health assessment, diagnostic and treatment services for neurotypical individuals (especially children, adolescents and families) as well as individuals with intellectual and developmental disabilities across the lifespan. Referrals come from schools, physicians, and community agencies throughout the region. Faculty may choose to focus their clinical services, training and research in 1) outpatient BH clinics at MMI , 2) integrated primary care sites across the Omaha metro area, or 3) school-based mental health clinics in the surrounding community. See UNMC\u2013MMI Psychology website for more information about the program. About MMI Psychology: The department of Psychology at the MMI is a collegial group of clinical educators and researchers dedicated to integrating training and research within clinical service delivery in a highly collaborative, interdisciplinary setting. Department faculty play a vital role in education and training, providing clinical supervision through a large, well-funded internship program within the APA -accredited Nebraska Internship Consortium, as well as a growing postdoctoral fellowship program. While the department is grounded in a behavioral orientation, it welcomes applicants with diverse but complementary theoretical perspectives. Several faculty also teach in the Applied Behavior Analysis master\u2019s degree program, which prepares graduates for licensure as mental health practitioners and certification as Board Certified Behavior Analysts. Faculty are encouraged to pursue clinical research that aligns with the department\u2019s mission, with flexibility in specific areas of focus. About MMI : MMI is one of the oldest, largest, and most comprehensive intellectual and developmental disability centers in the world. MMI\u2019s mission is \u201cto be world leaders in transforming the lives of all individuals with disabilities and complex health care needs, their families and the community through outreach, engagement, premier educational programs, innovative research and extraordinary patient care\u201d. MMI utilizes an interdisciplinary team approach that assures a comprehensive integration of our four pillars: research, clinical services, education, and community engagement. MMI is one of eight academic units of UNMC . MMI has an annual budget of more than $40M, approximately 500 employees, and our 17 disciplines provide over 90,000 clinical services each year serving individuals with disabilities and complex medical needs across the lifespan. MMI is a federally designated University Center for Excellence in Developmental Disabilities ( UCEDD ) and has a Leadership Education in Neurodevelopmental and Related Disabilities ( LEND ) program. MMI provides limitless opportunities for clinical programming, innovative research, and community engagement. About Omaha: Omaha, Nebraska, is a dynamic and welcoming city that offers an exceptional quality of life. Known for its affordability, short commutes, and friendly Midwest atmosphere, Omaha also boasts a vibrant arts scene, nationally acclaimed restaurants, and abundant parks and trails. The city is home to the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo and Aquarium and hosts the annual NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series, both of which draw visitors from across the country. With several Fortune 500 companies, a growing innovation economy, and a strong sense of community, Omaha provides the perfect balance of professional opportunity and small-town charm\u2014making it an ideal place to live and work. Additional Information: MMI provides convenient on-site parking and access to an employee fitness center. To learn more about this opportunity, contact Brandy Clarke, Ph.D., LP, Director, MMI Psychology, at: brandy.clarke@unmc.edu. Review of applicants will occur on a rolling basis as recruitment is ongoing. Rank will depend on qualifications. Applicants should upload with their application a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, and three letters of recommendation with contact information. University of Nebraska Employee Information: Faculty and Staff Benefits Required Qualifications PhD in Clinical or School Psychology. Nebraska licensure (or license eligible). Supplemental Qualifications Candidates with a clinical internship from APA / CPA -accredited programs in psychology are preferred. Board certification particularly BCBA is preferred. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Up to 2 hours Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Over 5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Not Applicable Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation NA Repetitive Motion NA Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD and clinical internship from an APA/CPA-accredited program in psychology with specialty training in Pediatric or clinical child psychology or school psychology? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94607": {"title": "Cognitive and Behavioral Neurologist - Academic Rank DOQ", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Cognitive and Behavioral Neurologist - Academic Rank DOQ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Cognitive and Behavioral Neurologist - Academic Rank DOQ Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 289 Department Neurological Sciences 50001975 Business Unit(College/Institute) College of Medicine FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule As directed by Division Chief Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Cognitive and Behavioral Neurologist - Academic Rank DOQ Job Title/Academic Rank Cognitive and Behavioral Neurologist - Academic Rank DOQ Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary Academic Behavioral Neurologist Opportunity The Department of Neurological Sciences at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, NE is recruiting a physician with expertise in Cognitive and Behavioral Neurology. In this faculty role, you will join behavioral neurologists, advanced practice providers, nurse case manager and support staff who evaluate and treat over 1,000 unique patients a year. Our team of clinicians, scientists and educators are dedicated to saving lives, relieving suffering, and reducing the terrible impact of neurological disease on our patients, families, and community. The faculty have NIH -supported research programs investigating Alzheimer\u2019s disease and related neurodegenerative disorders. Nebraska Medicine, our hospital partner, has been recognized as a High Performing Hospital in neurology and neurosurgery for 5 years by U.S. News & World Report. Opportunity Highlights: \u00b7 Clinical practice with diverse variety of cases \u00b7 Collaborative approach to care in collegial practice environment \u00b7 Fully accredited behavioral neurology and neuropsychiatry fellowship program \u00b7 Opportunity for involvement in behavioral neurology clinical trial research programs with many possibilities for collaboration \u00b7 Inpatient neurology service opportunities available if desired Community Highlights: \u00b7 Attractive city with population of more than 925,000 people \u00b7 Continually earns national accolades for quality of life \u00b7 Cost of living is less than national average \u00b7 Thriving arts and entertainment scene \u00b7 Home of the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo and NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series Our compensation package is extremely competitive. In addition, comprehensive benefits including relocation, CME and generous employer paid retirement are offered. The successful candidate must be an MD/DO (or equivalent degree) who is ABPN board certified/eligible and fellowship trained in Behavioral Neurology and Neuropsychiatry, Geriatric Neurology, or equivalent fellowship in the specialty. If you are interested in learning more, please contact: Dan Murman, MD Director, Behavioral Neurology Division and Fellowship Vice Chair, Clinical and Translational Research Professor, Department of Neurological Sciences dlmurman@unmc.edu 402-559-9953 Apply online at h https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94486 . Individuals from diverse backgrounds are encouraged to apply. Required Qualifications M.D. or equivalent degree, have completed an ACGME -certified Neurology residency, be ABPN board eligible or certified in Neurology, and have completed fellowship training in Behavioral Neurology and Neuropsychiatry, Geriatric Neurology, or equivalent fellowship in the specialty. Supplemental Qualifications Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Lab environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Occasionally Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting 2-5 hours Standing 2-5 hours Squatting Occasionally Walking Up to 2 hours EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids Yes Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE Yes Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Seeing patients in clinic Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation Both Repetitive Motion Both Grasping Both If you selected any area above, please explain Documenting and seeing patients Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess an MD, DO, MBBS or equivalent degree? Yes No * Are you board certified or board eligible? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Careerlink Employee Referral HERC Indeed Job Fair Lincoln Journal Star Linkedin Omaha World Herald UNMC Job Site Facebook NEWorks Handshake Other * If Other, please specify the source. Otherwise, indicate NA. (Open Ended Question) Breakthroughs for life. \u00a9 University of Nebraska Medical Center 42nd and Emile, Omaha, NE 68198 Individuals who need accommodation during the online application or interview process may contact 402-559-4070 or unmcstaffing@unmc.edu to request an accommodation. For questions regarding application, please contact UNMC Staffing at unmcstaffing@unmc.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://unmc.peopleadmin.com/postings/94558": {"title": "Neuropsychologist (Academic Rank DOQ)", "description": "University of Nebraska Medical Center | Neuropsychologist (Academic Rank DOQ) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Employment Eligibility Verification Right To Work Know Your Rights Hiring Manager Log-in Quick Tips for Online Application Neuropsychologist (Academic Rank DOQ) Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisition Details GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: UNMC is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer, including an equal opportunity employer of protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Location Omaha, NE Requisition Number: 2025 - 315 Department MMI Psychology 50000698 Business Unit(College/Institute) Munroe-Meyer Institute FTE: 100 Reg-Temp Full-Time Regular Work Schedule Full time (12 months) Requisition Category Faculty Requisition Title Neuropsychologist (Academic Rank DOQ) Job Title/Academic Rank Neuropsychologist (Academic Rank DOQ) Additional Requisition Title Appointment Type DOQ - DEPENDS ON QUALS Salary Range Salary Commensurate with Experience Job/EEO Category Faculty Job Requisition Begin Date 12/16/2025 Position Qualification Position Summary The Munroe-Meyer Institute ( MMI ) for Genetics and Rehabilitation at the University of Nebraska Medical Center ( UNMC ) in Omaha is currently accepting applications for a faculty position in the Department of Psychology as Neuropsychologist (Academic Rank DOQ ). Minimum requirements are a doctoral degree in Clinical, School, or Counseling Psychology with training and experience in neuropsychological assessment and research. Applicant must have Nebraska licensure (or license eligible) while board certification ( ABPP ) is also valued. Candidates with a clinical internship from APA / CPA -accredited programs in psychology are preferred. This faculty position would be tasked with developing a program around neuropsychological services for children and adults with intellectual and developmental disabilities including: Neuropsychological assessment and diagnostics Clinical training in neuropsychology for predoctoral interns and postdoctoral fellows A program of clinical research. In addition, this position would be tasked with developing a program that uses practice extenders or psychometrists to provide direct testing, reserving the licensed psychologist for diagnostics and interpretation, training, and research. Clinical referrals come from schools, physicians, and community agencies throughout the region. Typical presenting concerns include brain tumor and treatment, TBI /concussion, epilepsy and other seizure disorders, and genetic and other developmental disorders. Institute-based coordination of clinical care and interdisciplinary research is provided. See UNMC\u2013MMI Psychology website for more information about the program. About MMI Psychology: The department of Psychology at the MMI is a collegial group of clinical educators and researchers dedicated to integrating training and research within clinical service delivery in a highly collaborative, interdisciplinary setting. Department faculty play a vital role in education and training, providing clinical supervision through a large, well-funded internship program within the APA -accredited Nebraska Internship Consortium, as well as a growing postdoctoral fellowship program. While the department is grounded in a behavioral orientation, it welcomes applicants with diverse but complementary theoretical perspectives. Several faculty also teach in the Applied Behavior Analysis master\u2019s degree program, which prepares graduates for licensure as mental health practitioners and certification as Board Certified Behavior Analysts. Faculty are encouraged to pursue clinical research that aligns with the department\u2019s mission, with flexibility in specific areas of focus. About MMI : MMI is one of the oldest, largest, and most comprehensive intellectual and developmental disability centers in the world. MMI\u2019s mission is \u201cto be world leaders in transforming the lives of all individuals with disabilities and complex health care needs, their families and the community through outreach, engagement, premier educational programs, innovative research and extraordinary patient care\u201d. MMI utilizes an interdisciplinary team approach that assures a comprehensive integration of our four pillars: research, clinical services, education, and community engagement. MMI is one of eight academic units of UNMC . MMI has an annual budget of more than $40M, approximately 500 employees, and our 17 disciplines provide over 90,000 clinical services each year serving individuals with disabilities and complex medical needs across the lifespan. MMI is a federally designated University Center for Excellence in Developmental Disabilities ( UCEDD ) and has a Leadership Education in Neurodevelopmental and Related Disabilities ( LEND ) program. MMI provides limitless opportunities for clinical programming, innovative research, and community engagement. About Omaha: Omaha, Nebraska, is a dynamic and welcoming city that offers an exceptional quality of life. Known for its affordability, short commutes, and friendly Midwest atmosphere, Omaha also boasts a vibrant arts scene, nationally acclaimed restaurants, and abundant parks and trails. The city is home to the world-renowned Henry Doorly Zoo and Aquarium and hosts the annual NCAA Men\u2019s College World Series, both of which draw visitors from across the country. With several Fortune 500 companies, a growing innovation economy, and a strong sense of community, Omaha provides the perfect balance of professional opportunity and small-town charm\u2014making it an ideal place to live and work. Additional Information: MMI provides convenient on-site parking and access to an employee fitness center. To learn more about this opportunity, contact Brandy Clarke, Ph.D., LP, Director, MMI Psychology, at: brandy.clarke@unmc.edu. Review of applicants will occur on a rolling basis as recruitment is ongoing. Rank will depend on qualifications. Applicants should upload with their application a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, and three letters of recommendation with contact information. University of Nebraska Employee Information: Faculty and Staff Benefits Required Qualifications PhD in Clinical, School or Counseling Psychology. Nebraska licensure (or license eligible). Supplemental Qualifications Candidates with a clinical internship from APA / CPA -accredited programs in psychology are preferred. Board certification particularly BCBA is preferred. Working Environment & Physical Requirements WORKING ENVIRONMENT The information provided below best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the Environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office environment, Clinical environment Other working environment NA PHYSICAL REQUIREMENT Bending, stooping, twisting Occasionally Crawling Not Applicable Driving Up to 2 hours Kneeling Occasionally Reaching Occasionally Sitting Over 5 hours Standing Occasionally Squatting Not Applicable Walking Occasionally EXPOSURES Atmospheric No Blood/body fluids No Chemical hazards No Working on or around moving machinery No Electrical current No Noise No Changes of temperature/humidity No Wear PPE No Work with laboratory animals No Radiation Operating hand/power tools No If you answered yes to any area above, please explain Hand/Wrists Fine Manipulation NA Repetitive Motion NA Grasping NA If you selected any area above, please explain Addtional Describe any other aspects and demands of the job not listed in this description. Applicant Documents Required Documents C.V. Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Doc Requisition Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD and clinical internship from an APA/CPA-accredited program in psychology with specialty training in Pediatric or clinical child psychology or school psychology? Yes No * How did yo